DESCRIPTION:80 miles difficult\, shorter option 50 miles\nmoderate (but sti
 ll includes Bear Wallow Hill).\nThose 30 extra miles are worth it! This is 
 a\nchallenging route with some great scenery.\nThe Cordry-Sweetwater Bermud
 a Triangle has\nswallowed some riders so bring a map and try\nto keep other
  riders in sight. Excellent saddle\ntime for RAIN trainees.\n\nThe route wi
 ll utilize Bittersweet Road which\nhas been improved since last year.\n\n<a
  href="http://www.bloomingtonbicycleclub.org/private/BBCMaps/map_pack_1/cor
 dry_sweetwater.pdf">Cordry-Sweetwater Lakes</a>\n\n<a href="http://ridewith
 gps.com/routes/1530307">GPS<a/>
LAST-MODIFIED:20140618T161040Z
LOCATION:Bryan Park Pool Parking Lot @ 39.15435\,-86.523
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Cordry-Sweetwater Lakes Ride - Leader: Stan Ellis
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Bicycle Club
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20151205
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20151206
DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:9q96u9v2eq45hd2a2f18s1a1q8@google.com
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20151027T144324Z
DESCRIPTION:Nebo North Trail Head (<a href="http://www.fs.usda.gov/Internet
 /FSE_DOCUMENTS/stelprdb5287871.pdf">map</a>)\n\nMeet at Mr Lubies 9:00AM to
  car pool to this event\n\nAll are welcome to ride MTB\,FAT Bike or whateve
 r you bring\n\nFatbike rider/fan or fat-curious? Come ride with the Hoosier
  Fat Bike Fellowship on December 5\, 2015 on Global Fat Bike Day.\nMake sur
 e that if you're attending\, you've got your Hoosier National Forest trails
  pass. It looks like it'll be a brisk day with an overnight low just under 
 freezing and a daytime high just shy of 50\, but the forecast looks mostly 
 clear this week\, aside from a slight chance of rain early. There look to b
 e a few clear\, sunny days leading up to the ride.\nLet's meet at the Nebo 
 North trailhead at 10am. Those that want a shorter ride can do Nebo out/bac
 k or even do a Nebo/Combs loop if that sounds more interesting to them. The
  long route will include a short excursion into Hoosier National Forest ont
 o Trails 18 and 19\, with a little bit of gravel roads to connect them. I e
 xpect the long route to be 25ish mobal Fat bike Day\n\n<a href="https://www
 .facebook.com/events/494250307394434">Global Fat Bike Day</a>\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20151216T095705Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Global Fat Bike Day
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
X-MICROSOFT-CDO-ALLDAYEVENT:TRUE
X-MICROSOFT-DISALLOW-COUNTER:FALSE
X-APPLE-TRAVEL-ADVISORY-BEHAVIOR:AUTOMATIC
END:VEVENT
