BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Bicycle Club
DTSTART:20160423T140000Z
DTEND:20160423T190000Z
DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:7hja255uume077atqegn4cvda4@google.com
CREATED:20160412T022234Z
DESCRIPTION:Section 4 of I-69 is finally completed\, so we\ncan finally rid
 e to Hobbieville again ! The west\npart of Rock East Road might still be in
 \nrough shape\, but there is a new bridge on\nHobbieville Road over I-69 th
 at gets us right\nout to SR 54.  So\, it is business as usual on\nthe first
  part of this ride\, and a minor victory\nover road construction.\n\nSee th
 e other Cincinnati. Visit the\nhistoric\, refurbished Yoho Grocery in\nSols
 berry\, laugh in the face of Whitehall\nHill and take a sharp right at its 
 base.\n\nHowever\, Vernal Pike is closed on the way\nback to town so we wil
 l do our detour south on\non the Karst Greenway and get back to town\nvia R
 ockport Road.  The sum total of it is about\n52 miles.  We'll do some gathe
 r ups along the\nway and you have to do a stop at Yoho's in\nSolsberry.  \n
 \n<a href="http://www.bloomingtonbicycleclub.org/private/BBCMaps/map_pack_2
 /hobbieville.pdf">Hobbieville Without Vernal (pdf)</a>\n\n<a href=https://r
 idewithgps.com/routes/4574542">GPS Links<a/>
LAST-MODIFIED:20160423T141201Z
LOCATION:Bryan Park Pool Parking Lot @ 39.15435\,-86.523
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Hobbieville Without Vernal - Leader: John Bassett
TRANSP:OPAQUE
X-APPLE-TRAVEL-ADVISORY-BEHAVIOR:AUTOMATIC
END:VEVENT
