UID:nmqokfi2khlarv0uop71tbatko@google.com
CREATED:20170417T000647Z
DESCRIPTION:This route is sort of known\nfor Wineries\, but mainly known fo
 r\nhills.  You get a good dose of Lake\nLemon and some nice country roads\n
 in the northwest part of the county.\n\nSince Kinser Pike is closed at SR 3
 7\,\nand Bottom Road is closed at Bean\nBlossom Creek\, we will detour thro
 ugh\nCampus\, Prow Road\, and SR 46 to\nMaple Grove Rd. to get up north.  W
 e\nwill cross SR 37 at Oliver Winery\, and\nfollow SR 37 north a short dist
 ance to\nFox Hollow Road.  We resume the normal\nroute at Old 37 and Anders
 on\nRoad.\n\n<a href="http://bloomingtonbicycleclub.org/maps/John_Bassett_M
 aps/The_Wineries_Ride__via_Maple_Grove_47.pdf">The Wineries Ride via Maple 
 Grove 47</a>\n\n<a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/7157320">GPS Links<
 a/>\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20170417T001335Z
LOCATION:Bryan Park Pool Parking Lot @ 39.15435\,-86.523
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:The Wineries Ride - Leader: Dimetri Poppeliers
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
