BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Bicycle Club
DTSTART:20150524T180000Z
DTEND:20150524T203000Z
DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:tjnjuminbtqg56fkupdfd6cc48@google.com
CREATED:20150523T123317Z
DESCRIPTION:Lets start off this year's Family Rides with a reprise of last 
 year's Ice Cream Run\, slightly simplified. Again\, we have multiple length
  options depending on your family's preferences.\n\nThe whole route is mark
 ed with bike lanes or sharrows where it isn't dedicated bike/pedestrian inf
 rastructure. The long option does use some of 7th street downtown\, includi
 ng crossing College and Walnut streets. Most of it is campus and residentia
 l streets. We will NOT use 46 at all - Brusters is accessible from parking 
 lots on S. Morningside Drive.\n\nWe'll meet at Butler Park on W 9th St for 
 a 2:00pm departure\, and take the B-line Trail to 7th Street\, where we wil
 l pick up the 7th and Longview Greenway. We will follow 7th street through 
 campus and across town to Longview\, using the bike/pedestrian underpass to
  cross the bypass with no traffic.\n\nOur first stop will be at Park Ridge 
 Park (Not to be confused with Park Ridge East Park) on Longview Avenue. We 
 will plan to leave about 2:40. This will allow for a short break to play at
  the playground here\, and lets families looking for a shorter ride join us
  here.\n\nWe will have a brief stop at Park Ridge East Park\, to allow our 
 smaller "big kids" to switch from trailers and cargo bikes to their own ped
 al bikes for the last quarter mile.\n\nThen we have ice cream and turn arou
 nd :-)\n\nIf you do the whole route\, it's about 4.3 miles each way\, or 8.
 6 total.\nFrom Park Ridge Park\, the route is 0.9 miles one-way or 1.8 tota
 l.\nFrom Park Ridge East Park\, the route is 0.3 milfes each way\, or 0.6 t
 otal.\n\nGoogle Maps link: https://www.google.com/maps/dir/Rev.+Ernest+D.+B
 utler+Park\,+812+W+9th+St\,+Bloomington\,+IN+47404\,+United+States/Park+Rid
 ge+Park\,+East+Longview+Avenue\,+Bloomington\,+IN/Park+Ridge+East+Park\,+Ea
 st+Morningside+Drive\,+Bloomington\,+IN/Bruster%27s+Real+Ice+Cream\,+East+3
 rd+Street\,+Bloomington\,+IN/@39.1673911\,-86.4916779\,16z/am=t/data=!4m31!
 4m30!1m10!1m1!1s0x886c6726ce2099bf:0xd8538836761d204b!2m2!1d-86.542908!2d39
 .171174!3m4!1m2!1d-86.501731!2d39.1676815!3s0x886c66a11cac0cfb:0x803afc2117
 e1ca91!1m5!1m1!1s0x886c6419e9bd9fd1:0xfbfd157f4f024d1b!2m2!1d-86.490415!2d3
 9.168067!1m5!1m1!1s0x886c646968572d55:0xa51f754ec0503118!2m2!1d-86.47359!2d
 39.167317!1m5!1m1!1s0x886c6469c8a0efcf:0x7096fa7344ac39f0!2m2!1d-86.472444!
 2d39.164683!3e1
LAST-MODIFIED:20150523T123317Z
LOCATION:Rev. Ernest D. Butler Park\, 812 West 9th Street\, Bloomington\, I
 N 47404\, United States
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Family Ride: 7th & Longview Ice Cream Run
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
