DESCRIPTION:This ride is a classic "almost century"\nand a must do!  Due to
  I69 closure of\nVernal Pike the ride will\nbegin and end at Karst Farm Par
 k\non Endwright Road\, but will be of\ncomparable distance (96 miles) to\ns
 tarting at Bryan Park.  Lunch in\nClay City is usually at the IGA north\nof
  town (see map and GPS).\n \n<a href="http://bloomingtonbicycleclub.org/map
 s/John_Bassett_Maps/JoesClayCity_AlmostCentury_KarstPark_95.pdf">Joe's Clay
  City Almost A Century Karst Park</a>\n\n<a href="http://ridewithgps.com/ro
 utes/9369743">GPS from Karst Park 95<a/>\n\nRiders interested in a shorter 
 option may\nwant to retrace their steps from Spencer\,\nor follow one of th
 e routes below.\n\nShort options\, 66 and 45 miles:\n\n<a href="http://bloo
 mingtonbicycleclub.org/maps/Jim%20Schroeder/9Aand9B%20Spencer%20Circuit.pdf
 ">Spencer Circuit & Spencer Hilly</a>
