CREATED:20160603T124507Z
DESCRIPTION:Ninety miles difficult. This "almost" century\nincorporates the
  best of what this area has to\noffer cyclists - big climbs\, rolling hills
 \, curves\,\nflats\, buccolic views\, bizarre town names\n(Zelma) and sites
  (the Stonehead). Ride this\nonce and you'll ride it again !  Warning: No\n
 indoor plumbing till Story at mile 50\, unless\nthere is a new place in Fre
 etown.\n\nUPDATE:  With the closure of SR 45 at\nHelmsburg\, we will likely
  need to detour onto\nOwl Creek and Lanam Ridge to get over to\nSouth Shore
 .  That route is shown on the\nGPS links below.  Also\, SR 135 has new\nchi
 p and seal.\n\n6/22/16:  NOTE REVISED TIME IS\n8:00 TO AVOID THE HEAT!\n\n<
 a href="http://www.bloomingtonbicycleclub.org/private/BBCMaps/map_pack_1/na
 shville_90.pdf">Nashville 90</a>\n\n<a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes
 /14207174"608332">GPS Links Nashville 90 2016 Version via OWL Creek 89<a/>
LAST-MODIFIED:20160623T015836Z
LOCATION:Bryan Park Pool Parking Lot @ 39.15435\,-86.523
SEQUENCE:2
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Nashville 90  Ride - Leader:  Warren Smith
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
