DESCRIPTION:Hear the story of the 20th century revolution that reconstructe
 d America’s streets and cities to accommodate automobiles.  Learn about how
  we can shift back to people-centered streets with lecturer Peter Norton\, 
 author of “Fighting Traffic: The Dawn of the Motor Age in the American City
 .”  This FREE event is brought to you by Open Streets Bloomington (a projec
 t of the Center for Sustainable Living)\, Bloomington Bicycle Club\, and th
 e Applied Community Commons Working Group.\n\n<a href="http://simplycsl.org
 /rediscovering-streets-as-public-spaces-monday-october-13th-700pm-woodburn-
 hall-auditorium/">http://simplycsl.org</a>\n\nJoin with Google Hangouts: ht
 tps://hangouts.google.com/hangouts/_/umail.iu.edu/speaker-peter?hceid=Y3VjN
 jZndW9hbTFoaGNxcTJybmFuaWlubDhAZ3JvdXAuY2FsZW5kYXIuZ29vZ2xlLmNvbQ.e0dpsu49u
 hemu5ik1jlo03dlm4&hs=121
LAST-MODIFIED:20141007T133346Z
LOCATION:Woodburn Hall Auditorium @ 39.168033\, -86.520401
SEQUENCE:3
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Speaker: Peter Norton - City Traffic
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
