CREATED:20160602T020744Z
DESCRIPTION:A 57 mile route that takes riders to all of\nthe towns condense
 d in the name. (This is\nan extension of the Texas Ridge to Gosport\nRide w
 hich offers 39 & 46 mile shorter\noptions.) Keep your eyes peeled for buffa
 lo\nand potholes! Those who sign on for the full\n57 are treated to riding 
 on Rocky Hill\nRoad - an Owen County hidden treasure.\n\nThere is also an 8
 9 mile long\nroute that will head north to Quincy and\nCataract Falls from 
 Gosport\, and return to\nBloomington via the later part of the\nElsitgospew
 hi route.\n\nREVISION 6/16/16:  SINCE VERNAL PIKE\nIS CLOSED AT SR 37 WE WI
 LL START/\nEND THE RIDE AT KARST FARM PARK.\nBASIC RIDE IS 54 MILES AND THE
 \nCATRACT FALLS EXTENSION WILL BE\n86 MILES .\n\nTHE "2016 VERSION" MATERIA
 LS\nREFLECT THIS CHANGE.  \n\n<a href="http://bloomingtonbicycleclub.org/ma
 ps/John_Bassett_Maps/Ellstigospwhi_2016_Version_54.pdf">Elstigospewhi 2016 
 Version 54</a>\n\n<a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/14466229">GPS Lin
 ks for Ellstigospwhi 2016 Version</a>\n\n<a href="http://bloomingtonbicycle
 club.org/maps/John_Bassett_Maps/Cataract_Falls_2016_Version_86.pdf">Catarac
 t Falls 2016 Version 86<a/>\n\n<a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/1446
 6926">GPS Links for Cataract Falls 2016 Version<a/>\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20160616T182245Z
LOCATION:Karst Farm Park @ 39.140340\, -86.597677
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Elstigospewhi & Cataract Falls - Leader: Stan Ellis
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
