DESCRIPTION:The annual double century.  This one is a real\ntoughie\, but y
 ou can just do the middle century\npart starting / ending at French Lick.  
 There is also a metric century for those inclined.\nDetails to follow. \n\n
 Double Century: <a href="http://ridewithgps.com/routes/3893876">http://ride
 withgps.com/routes/3893876</a>\n\nMiddle Century: <a href="http://ridewithg
 ps.com/routes/4800329">http://ridewithgps.com/routes/4800329</a>\n\nMetric 
 Century option: <a href="http://ridewithgps.com/routes/4320426">http://ride
 withgps.com/routes/4320426</a>\n\n\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20140606T124525Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:St. Meinrad Double Century - Leader: Jim Schroeder
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Bicycle Club
DTSTART:20140607T130000Z
DTEND:20140607T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:gap7t41ekqhqs76uagbfive87s@google.com
CREATED:20140325T005133Z
DESCRIPTION:This is a drive and ride that we did last year\,\nexcept the ro
 ute is changed a little to avoid\na couple of gravel roads we blundered int
 o.\n\nThe entire route is 96 miles and begins and\nends at Spring Mill Stat
 e Park.  Start there\nbecause a century ride will get you to the Ohio\nRive
 r and back.  Shorter options include turning\nback north at Marengo for a 6
 3 mile loop\, or\nturning right at the famous Crawford County\nShoe Tree fo
 r about 82 miles.  Tour God’s\nCounty and enjoy a lunch at the Overlook\nRe
 staurant on the Ohio River\, or eat on the\nrun at the Subway in Tower at I
 -64.  Car pool\nleaving Bryan Park at 8:00\, or met at Spring\nMill State P
 ark at 9:00.  Bring your park pass.\nThink about a post ride buffet at the 
 park lodge.\n\n<a href="http://bloomingtonbicycleclub.org/maps/Special_Maps
 /Spring%20Mill%20to%20Leavenworth%2096.pdf">Paper Map and Cue Sheet</a>\n\n
 <a href="http://ridewithgps.com/routes/2970469">GPS</a>\n\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20150618T090513Z
LOCATION:Spring Mill State Park\, Mitchell\, IN @ 38.735030\, -86.414270
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Spring Mill to Leavenworth - Leader: John Bassett
TRANSP:OPAQUE
