DESCRIPTION:A 57 mile route that takes riders to all of the towns\ncondense
 d in the name. (This is an extension of\nthe Texas Ridge ride to Gosport wh
 ich offers 39 &\n46 mile shorter options.) Keep your eyes peeled\nfor buffa
 lo and potholes! Those who sign on for\nthe full 57 are treated to riding o
 n Rocky Hill\nRoad - an Owen County hidden treasure.\n\nStan Ellis will als
 o lead an 89 mile long\nroute that will head north to Quincy and\nCataract 
 Falls from Gosport\, and return to\nBloomington via the later part of the\n
 Elsitgospewhi route. \n\n<a href="http://bloomingtonbicycleclub.org/maps/Ji
 m%20Schroeder/Ellstigospewhi.pdf">Elstigospewhi</a>\n\n<a href="http://ride
 withgps.com/routes/1585554">GPS</a>\n\n<a href="http://ridewithgps.com/rout
 es/2340414">Cataract Fall 89<a/>\n
LAST-MODIFIED:20150530T130251Z
LOCATION:Bryan Park Pool Parking Lot @ 39.15435\,-86.523
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Elstigospewhi & Cataract Falls- Leaders: Jen Miers & Stan Ellis
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
