 at Brusters for ice cream<br><br>The "Older\, Wiser\, and a Little Slower" 
 training group emphasizes moderate rides\, and a route planned in advance t
 hat is posted on the ride calendar. This is a no drop ride\, but not a begi
 nner's ride. The OWLS often average 15 to 19 mph on flat roads\, and typica
 lly have an overall average moving speed between 12 and 15 mph including hi
 lls. Distances vary from 20 to 30 miles\, depending partly on available lig
 ht. Early season rides will be somewhat shorter and slower.<br><br>Question
 s? Contact<a href="mailto:allan.edmonds@gmail.com" target="_blank"> Allan E
 dmonds</a>&nbsp\;or <a href="mailto:gail.morell@gmail.com" target="_blank">
 Gail Morell</a><br><br>Starts in the parking lot of Sherwood Oaks Christian
  Church.
