DESCRIPTION:This is our usual fist ride of the season out to the Muscatatuc
 k National Wildlife Refuge on Bottom Road.&nbsp\; The basic route is a pret
 ty level 24 mile out &amp\; back designed to be an easy ride to shake off t
 he Winter cobwebs.&nbsp\; The route is easily extended to 32 miles with a l
 oop to the north\, as show in the mapping\, or can be extended east across 
 I-69 via the Sample Road overpass for those who want some additional miles.
 &nbsp\; You could even ride a little gravel over to the new covered bridge 
 on Maple Grove Road and return to Bottom Road and Bloomington via Maple Gro
 ve (North-South) and Maple Grove (East-West).&nbsp\;<br><br><a href="http:/
 /bloomingtonbicycleclub.org/maps/John_Bassett_Maps/Muscatatuck_Wildlife_Ref
 uge_-_Beyond__2018_Ver_32.pdf" id="ow2218" __is_owner="true">Muscatatuck Wi
 ldlife Refuge &amp\; Beyond 2018 Version 32</a><br><br><a href="https://rid
 ewithgps.com/routes/26907106">GPS Files</a><a></a>
