 t blow through stop signs. Consider bike lights.<br></li><li>Be COURTEOUS: 
 Single up in traffic<br></li><li>Be PREDICTABLE: Signal your intentions to 
 cars and fellow riders.</li></ul>The "Older\, Wiser\, and a Little Slower" 
 training group emphasizes moderate rides\, and a route planned in advance t
 hat is posted on the ride calendar. This is a no drop ride\, but not a begi
 nner's ride. The OWLS often average 15 to 19 mph on flat roads\, and typica
 lly have an overall average moving speed between 12 and 15 mph including hi
 lls. Distances vary from 20 to 30 miles\, depending partly on available lig
 ht. Early season rides will be somewhat shorter and slower. Rides depart pr
 omptly at 5:45.<br><br>Non-members should sign up for a&nbsp\;<a href="http
 s://secure.getmeregistered.com/get_information.php?event_id=133776">free tr
 ial membership</a>\, good for up to three rides\, and which includes electr
 onically signing a liability waiver\,&nbsp\;prior to participation.<br><br>
 Questions? Contact <a href="mailto:allan.edmonds@gmail.com">Allan Edmonds</
 a> or <a href="mailto:gail.morell@gmail.com">Gail Morell</a>
