DESCRIPTION:51 moderate miles with a 26 mile short option.&nbsp\; This rout
 e takes riders through Morgan Monroe State Forest and past "The Touchables"
  Sculpture Garden.&nbsp\; Consider coasting and taking a gander at the uniq
 ue pieces scattered on the west side of the road.<br><br><br>We will take t
 he new Old 37 connector on the east side of I-69 from the Liberty Church in
 terchange down to Old 37\, more or less duplicating the original mapping of
  this ride.&nbsp\; But\, you always have the option to spice up your life a
 nd take Hacker Creek Road back to Forest Road junction.&nbsp\; Of course\, 
 that means climbing the infamous Hacker Creek Hill.<br><br><a href="https:/
 /www.bloomingtonbicycleclub.org/maps/BBCMaps/map_pack_2/low_gap_touchables.
 pdf" target="_blank">Low Gap to Martinsville ("The Touchables")</a><br><br>
 <a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/28325235" target="_blank">GPS Files
 </a>
LAST-MODIFIED:20180813T233510Z
LOCATION:Bryan Park Pool Parking Lot @ 39.15435\,-86.523
