BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Bicycle Club
DTSTART:20180421T140000Z
DTEND:20180421T190000Z
DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:1krra6hp0s51nctr0khc6v690j@google.com
CREATED:20180320T233303Z
DESCRIPTION:<br>This route is sort of known for Wineries\, but mainly known
  for hills.  You get a good dose of Lake Lemon and some nice country roads 
 in the northwest part of the county.<br><br>Since you cannot cross SR37 at 
 Sample Road now due to I69 construction\, we will get to Oliver Winery from
  the east.&nbsp\; We will follow the new I69 access road (actually the old 
 highway) north from Sample Road and Oliver Winery to Fox Hollow Road\, and 
 resume the traditional Wineries route at Anderson Road.&nbsp\; The whole th
 ing is about 44 miles\;&nbsp\; come join in the fun!!<br><br><a href="http:
 //bloomingtonbicycleclub.org/maps/John_Bassett_Maps/Wineries_Ride_2018_Vers
 ion.pdf" target="_blank">The Wineries Ride 2018 Version</a><br><br><a href=
 "https://ridewithgps.com/routes/27179333" target="_blank">GPS Links</a><a><
 br></a>
