DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20200630T174500
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20200630T194500
DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:9p45m8hkqk5cb1cv973v44b00o@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20200630T174500
CREATED:20200302T150145Z
DESCRIPTION:<a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/30162001" id="ow370" __
 is_owner="true">Airport Ride</a>&nbsp\;via Gifford and Duncan\, 27 miles<br
 ><br>Please observe social distancing norms as we gather and ride. We plan 
 no formal leader. EVERYONE is a leader. Familiarize yourself with the ride 
 before heading out. We will ride in small groups.People in the last group w
 ill endeavor to sweep the route and assist others as needed.<br><ul><li>Be 
 SAFE. Don't blow through stop signs. Consider bike lights.<br></li><li>Be C
 OURTEOUS: Single up in traffic<br></li><li>Be PREDICTABLE: Signal your inte
 ntions to cars and fellow riders.</li></ul>The "Older\, Wiser\, and a Littl
 e Slower" training group emphasizes moderate rides\, and a route planned in
  advance that is posted on the ride calendar. This is a no drop ride\, but 
 not a beginner's ride. The OWLS often average 15 to 19 mph on flat roads\, 
 and typically have an overall average moving speed between 12 and 15 mph in
 cluding hills. Distances vary from 20 to 30 miles\, depending partly on ava
 ilable light. Early season rides will be somewhat shorter and slower. Rides
  depart promptly at 5:45.<br><br>Non-members should sign up for a <a href="
 https://secure.getmeregistered.com/get_information.php?event_id=133776">fre
 e trial membership</a>\, good for up to three rides\, and which includes el
 ectronically signing a liability waiver\,&nbsp\;prior to participation.<br>
 <br>Questions? Contact <a href="mailto:allan.edmonds@gmail.com">Allan Edmon
 ds</a> or <a href="mailto:gail.morell@gmail.com">Gail Morell</a>
LAST-MODIFIED:20200701T163655Z
LOCATION:Sherwood Oaks Christian Church\, 2700 E Rogers Rd\, Bloomington\, 
 IN 47401\, USA
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:OWLS Ride
TRANSP:OPAQUE
