BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Bicycle Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20200623T174500
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20200623T194500
DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:9p45m8hkqk5cb1cv973v44b00o@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20200623T174500
CREATED:20200302T150145Z
DESCRIPTION:<a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/30685756" id="ow378" __
 is_owner="true">Up the Dam Hill (out Gore)</a>&nbsp\; 26.5 miles<br><br>Ple
 ase observe social distancing norms as we gather and ride. We plan no forma
 l leader. EVERYONE is a leader. Familiarize yourself with the ride before h
 eading out. We will ride in small groups.People in the last group will ende
 avor to sweep the route and assist others as needed.<br><ul><li>Be SAFE. Do
 n't blow through stop signs. Consider bike lights.<br></li><li>Be COURTEOUS
 : Single up in traffic<br></li><li>Be PREDICTABLE: Signal your intentions t
 o cars and fellow riders.</li></ul>The "Older\, Wiser\, and a Little Slower
 " training group emphasizes moderate rides\, and a route planned in advance
  that is posted on the ride calendar. This is a no drop ride\, but not a be
 ginner's ride. The OWLS often average 15 to 19 mph on flat roads\, and typi
 cally have an overall average moving speed between 12 and 15 mph including 
 hills. Distances vary from 20 to 30 miles\, depending partly on available l
 ight. Early season rides will be somewhat shorter and slower. Rides depart 
 promptly at 5:45.<br><br>Non-members should sign up for a <a href="https://
 secure.getmeregistered.com/get_information.php?event_id=133776">free trial 
 membership</a>\, good for up to three rides\, and which includes electronic
 ally signing a liability waiver\,&nbsp\;prior to participation.<br><br>Ques
 tions? Contact <a href="mailto:allan.edmonds@gmail.com">Allan Edmonds</a> o
 r <a href="mailto:gail.morell@gmail.com">Gail Morell</a>
LAST-MODIFIED:20200623T202530Z
LOCATION:Sherwood Oaks Christian Church\, 2700 E Rogers Rd\, Bloomington\, 
 IN 47401\, USA
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:OWLS Ride
TRANSP:OPAQUE
