  "Older\, Wiser\, and a Little Slower" training group emphasizes moderate r
 ides\, and a route planned in advance that is posted on the ride calendar. 
 This is a no drop ride\, but not a beginner's ride. The OWLS often average 
 15 to 19 mph on flat roads\, and typically have an overall average moving s
 peed between 12 and 15 mph including hills. Distances vary from 20 to 30 mi
 les\, depending partly on available light. Early season rides will be somew
 hat shorter and slower.<br><br>Questions? Contact<a href="mailto:allan.edmo
 nds@gmail.com" target="_blank"> Allan Edmonds</a>&nbsp\;or <a href="mailto:
 gail.morell@gmail.com" target="_blank">Gail Morell</a><br><br>Starts in the
  parking lot of Sherwood Oaks Christian Church.
