DESCRIPTION:<a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https%3A%2F%2Fridewithgps
 .com%2Froutes%2F25779028&amp\;sa=D&amp\;usd=2&amp\;usg=AFQjCNEqL0K_xg1hp-qk
 iytlLwwq4eNfoA" target="_blank">Upper Birdie Galyan and Back</a>&nbsp\; 20.
 5 miles (Those who want a shorter ride can turn around at the bridge at mil
 e 8.9 and cut one climb.)<br><br><br>The "Older\, Wiser\, and a Little Slow
 er" training group emphasizes moderate rides\, and a route planned in advan
 ce that is posted on the ride calendar. This is a no drop ride\, but not a 
 beginner's ride. The OWLS often average 15 to 19 mph on flat roads\, and ty
 pically have an overall average moving speed between 12 and 15 mph includin
 g hills. Distances vary from 20 to 30 miles\, depending partly on available
  light. Early season rides will be somewhat shorter and slower.<br><br>Ques
 tions? Contact<a href="mailto:allan.edmonds@gmail.com" target="_blank"> All
 an Edmonds</a>&nbsp\;or <a href="mailto:gail.morell@gmail.com" target="_bla
 nk">Gail Morell</a><br><br>Starts in the parking lot of Sherwood Oaks Chris
 tian Church.
LAST-MODIFIED:20180320T013646Z
LOCATION:Sherwood Oaks Christian Church\, 2700 E Rogers Rd\, Bloomington\, 
 IN 47401\, USA
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:OWLS Ride to Upper Birdie Galyan
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
