DESCRIPTION:A 57 mile route that takes riders to all of\nthe towns condense
 d in the name. (This is\nan extension of the Texas Ridge to Gosport\nRide w
 hich offers 39 & 46 mile shorter\noptions.) Keep your eyes peeled for buffa
 lo\nand potholes! Those who sign on for the full\n57 are treated to Rocky H
 ill\nRoad - an Owen County hidden treasure.\n\nGlenn Berger will also lead 
 an extension\nto this route (89 miles) that will head north\nto Quincy and 
 Cataract Falls from Gosport\,\nand return to Bloomington via the later\npar
 t of the Ellsitgospewhi route.\n\n<a href="http://bloomingtonbicycleclub.or
 g/maps/John_Bassett_Maps/Ellstigospwhi_-_57.pdf">Ellstigospewhi 57</a>\n\n<
 a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/1585554">GPS Links for Ellstigospwhi
 </a>\n\n<a href="http://bloomingtonbicycleclub.org/maps/John_Bassett_Maps/C
 ataract_Falls_89.pdf">Cataract Falls 89<a/>\n\n<a href="https://ridewithgps
 .com/routes/14466809">GPS Links for Cataract Falls<a/>\n
