 ing group emphasizes moderate rides\, and a route planned in advance that i
 s posted on the ride calendar. This is a no drop ride\, but not a beginner'
 s ride. The OWLS often average 15 to 19 mph on flat roads\, and typically h
 ave an overall average moving speed between 12 and 15 mph including hills. 
 Distances vary from 20 to 30 miles\, depending partly on available light. E
 arly season rides will be somewhat shorter and slower.<br><br>Questions? Co
 ntact<a href="mailto:allan.edmonds@gmail.com" target="_blank"> Allan Edmond
 s</a>&nbsp\;or <a href="mailto:gail.morell@gmail.com" target="_blank">Gail 
 Morell</a><br><br>Starts in the parking lot of Sherwood Oaks Christian Chur
 ch.
