BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Bicycle Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20200702T174500
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20200702T194500
DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:9p45m8hkqk5cb1cv973v44b00o@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20200702T174500
CREATED:20200302T150145Z
DESCRIPTION:<a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/33164170" id="ow653" __
 is_owner="true">Two Creeks and a Lake</a>&nbsp\;27 miles<br><br>Please obse
 rve social distancing norms as we gather and ride. We plan no formal leader
 . EVERYONE is a leader. Familiarize yourself with the ride before heading o
 ut. We will ride in small groups.People in the last group will endeavor to 
 sweep the route and assist others as needed.<br><ul><li>Be SAFE. Don't blow
  through stop signs. Consider bike lights.<br></li><li>Be COURTEOUS: Single
  up in traffic<br></li><li>Be PREDICTABLE: Signal your intentions to cars a
 nd fellow riders.</li></ul>The "Older\, Wiser\, and a Little Slower" traini
 ng group emphasizes moderate rides\, and a route planned in advance that is
  posted on the ride calendar. This is a no drop ride\, but not a beginner's
  ride. The OWLS often average 15 to 19 mph on flat roads\, and typically ha
 ve an overall average moving speed between 12 and 15 mph including hills. D
 istances vary from 20 to 30 miles\, depending partly on available light. Ea
 rly season rides will be somewhat shorter and slower. Rides depart promptly
  at 5:45.<br><br>Non-members should sign up for a <a href="https://secure.g
 etmeregistered.com/get_information.php?event_id=133776">free trial membersh
 ip</a>\, good for up to three rides\, and which includes electronically sig
 ning a liability waiver\,&nbsp\;prior to participation.<br><br>Questions? C
 ontact <a href="mailto:allan.edmonds@gmail.com">Allan Edmonds</a> or <a hre
 f="mailto:gail.morell@gmail.com">Gail Morell</a>
LAST-MODIFIED:20200630T134321Z
LOCATION:Sherwood Oaks Christian Church\, 2700 E Rogers Rd\, Bloomington\, 
 IN 47401\, USA
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:OWLS Ride
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
