CREATED:20200603T133439Z
DESCRIPTION:<br>This week we will do one more shortish tuneup restart ride 
 before we get back into the swing or your regular summer ride schedule.<br>
 <br>his route is sort of known for Wineries\, but mainly known for hills.  
 You get a good dose of Lake Lemon and some nice country roads in the northw
 est part of the county.<br><br>With the completion of the Sample Road inter
 change on I-69 we can again do this route approximately as it was originall
 y designed.&nbsp\; From Oliver Winery we will follow the new I-69 access ro
 ad (actually the old highway) north to Fox Hollow Road\, and resume the tra
 ditional Wineries route at Anderson Road.&nbsp\; The whole thing is about 4
 6 miles\;&nbsp\; come join in the fun!!<br><br>Non-members should sign up f
 or a <a href="https://secure.getmeregistered.com/get_information.php?event_
 id=133776">free trial membership</a>\, good for up to three rides\, and whi
 ch includes electronically signing a liability waiver\,&nbsp\;prior to part
 icipation.&nbsp\;&nbsp\;<br><br><a href="http://bloomingtonbicycleclub.org/
 maps/John_Bassett_Maps/The_Wineries_Ride_2019_Ver_46.pdf">The Wineries Ride
  2019 Ver 46</a><br><br><a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/29730807">G
 PS Files</a><br><br><a><br></a>
LAST-MODIFIED:20200603T134018Z
LOCATION:Bryan Park Pool Parking Lot @ 39.15435\,-86.523\, 
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:The Wineries Ride - Leader: Everyone
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
