DTSTART:20190420T140000Z
DTEND:20190420T190000Z
DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:3rfc67bjsn88qiiga1sso9bkiv@google.com
CREATED:20190416T172726Z
DESCRIPTION:<br><br>CANCELLED DUE TO RAIN !!!<br><br><br>This route is sort
  of known for Wineries\, but mainly known for hills.  You get a good dose o
 f Lake Lemon and some nice country roads in the northwest part of the count
 y.<br><br><br>With the completion of the Sample Road interchange on I-69 we
  can again do this route approximately as it was originally designed.&nbsp\
 ; From Oliver Winery we will follow the new I-69 access road (actually the 
 old highway) north to Fox Hollow Road\, and resume the traditional Wineries
  route at Anderson Road.&nbsp\; The whole thing is about 46 miles\;&nbsp\; 
 come join in the fun!!<br><br><a href="http://bloomingtonbicycleclub.org/ma
 ps/John_Bassett_Maps/The_Wineries_Ride_2019_Ver_46.pdf" target="_blank">The
  Wineries Ride 2019 Ver 46</a><br><br><a href="https://ridewithgps.com/rout
 es/29730807" target="_blank">GPS Files</a><br><br><a><br></a>
LAST-MODIFIED:20190420T122329Z
LOCATION:Bryan Park Pool Parking Lot @ 39.15435\,-86.523
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:The Wineries Ride - Leader: Mark Gehlhausen
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
