DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20180621T201500
DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:6493lo23hltp408cpb9auek9gu_R20180503T214500@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20180619T174500
CREATED:20180302T015448Z
DESCRIPTION:<a href="https://goo.gl/AuSMmF" target="_blank">South Shore</a>
  - 34 miles<br><br>The "Older\, Wiser\, and a Little Slower" training group
  emphasizes moderate rides\, and a route planned in advance that is posted 
 on the ride calendar. This is a no drop ride\, but not a beginner's ride. T
 he OWLS often average 15 to 19 mph on flat roads\, and typically have an ov
 erall average moving speed between 12 and 15 mph including hills. Distances
  vary from 20 to 30 miles\, depending partly on available light. Early seas
 on rides will be somewhat shorter and slower.<br><br>Questions? Contact<a h
 ref="mailto:allan.edmonds@gmail.com" target="_blank"> Allan Edmonds</a>&nbs
 p\;or <a href="mailto:gail.morell@gmail.com" target="_blank">Gail Morell</a
 ><br><br>Starts in the parking lot of Sherwood Oaks Christian Church.
LAST-MODIFIED:20190625T235726Z
LOCATION:Sherwood Oaks Christian Church\, 2700 E Rogers Rd\, Bloomington\, 
 IN 47401\, USA
SEQUENCE:2
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:OWLS South Shore
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Bicycle Club
DTSTART:20200104T150000Z
DTEND:20200104T200000Z
DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:11u81lcbhpukl7d9nnijj1rh83@google.com
CREATED:20191202T150024Z
DESCRIPTION:Our first Saturday off road ride of the year has something for 
 everyone..\n\nWe will assemble at the camp site just beside trail 19 in the
  Hoosier National Forrest.\nGo down tower ridge rd to the first road past t
 he tower. County Rd 1500 turn right. go approx\n1.50 miles to camp site on 
 left. \n\nWe will have a fire going. From this site you can do whatever you
  want to do. You can ride MTB trails. you can ride gravel\, you can hike tr
 ails or you can stay by the fire and enjoy good company and share stories. 
 Bring any snacks  and beverages to share that you wish.\n\nAll rides will b
 e impromptu. I hope you can join us for this fun day of  fellowship. \n\nMe
 et at old K-mart East 10:00 to car pool to campsite.\n\nBring chairs if you
  want to sit around the camp fire. \n\n   
LAST-MODIFIED:20191202T150024Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:First Saturday off road ride
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
