DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><b>This ride is being moved to Tuesday this week to 
 take advantage of warmer temps</b></html-blob><br><html-blob><br></html-blo
 b><br><html-blob><u></u>Join us this Wednesday night gravel ride. It is one
  of our club's favorites. An out and back from Blackwell Horse Camp to Hick
 ory Grove Church.<u></u><br><u></u><br><u></u><br><u></u>This is a fun 20 m
 iles.&nbsp\; MTB\, cross or gravel bike preferred. This is all gravel.<br><
 br>BRING LIGHTS!!!!!<br><br><br><br><a href="http://bloomingtonbicycleclub.
 org/maps/Gravel_Rides/Hickory%20Grove%20Out%20and%20Back%2021.pdf">Hickory 
 Grove 21</a><br><br><a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/38373153">GPS F
 iles</a><u></u></html-blob>
LAST-MODIFIED:20220118T003919Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Hickory Grove out & Back 21
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Bicycle Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20210824T174500
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20210824T194500
DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:3ec6lbtuh6edcbf846ib8c4r0n@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20210824T174500
CREATED:20210314T144013Z
DESCRIPTION:<p><a href="https://bloomingtonbicycleclub.org/maps/iRides/Elle
 ttsville_Loop_iRide_Long_29.pdf">Ellettsville Loop iRide Long 29</a><br></p
 ><p><a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/28448443">GPS Files</a><br></p>
 <p>The iRide is an intermediate level ride of moderate pace and distance wi
 th regrouping points.&nbsp\; Pace is anticipated to be 15-17 mph.<br></p><p
 >The tRide is an advanced level ride of high pace and moderate distance tha
 t may or may not include regrouping points. &nbsp\;Pace is anticipated to b
 e 18+ mph. Expect occasional sprint or Strava segments\, pace line riding a
 t high speed\, intervals\, and fewer regrouping stops.</p><p>The iRide and 
 tRide will start at the same place and will ride the same scheduled route\,
  but the start of these two groups will be staggered with the tRide startin
 g first at 5:45 and the iRide just behind them. Mileages will increase as t
 he season progresses.&nbsp\; </p><p>Riders are expected to look out for eac
 h other during the rides.&nbsp\; Ride maps and GPS links will be posted her
 e in advance. Riders unfamiliar with the route should bring along a copy of
  the map.</p>Non-members should sign up for a&nbsp\;<a href="https://secure
 .getmeregistered.com/get_information.php?event_id=133776">free trial member
 ship</a>\, good for up to three rides\, and which includes electronically s
 igning a liability waiver\,&nbsp\;prior to participation.
LAST-MODIFIED:20220614T150551Z
LOCATION:Bryan Park Pool Parking Lot @ 39.15435\,-86.523
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:iRide / tRide - Ellettsville Loop iRide Long 29
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Bicycle Club
DTSTART:20210522T140000Z
DTEND:20210522T183000Z
DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:5s5v4bt0c3hj3gd9vfl6kb2e34@google.com
CREATED:20210516T224353Z
DESCRIPTION:<b>UPDATE 5/20/21:&nbsp\; Due to an I69 road closure on the eas
 t end of Southview Drive in Martinsville we will do a slight detour\, as fo
 llows.&nbsp\; Approach Martinsville on Burton Lane\, as normal.&nbsp\; Inst
 ead of turning right on Southview (no thru traffic sign here) proceed strai
 ght across SR37 (now closed) to the usual Marathon Convenience Store on the
  left.&nbsp\; We will refuel here.&nbsp\; Upon leaving the Marathon\, turn 
 left on Burton and proceed north three blocks to Duo Street.&nbsp\; Follow 
 Duo east to Orange\, turn right on Orange\, go one block and turn east agai
 n on Bill's Blvd.&nbsp\; Follow Bill's Blvd. east to Ohio Street.&nbsp\; Tu
 rn right on Ohio and cross SR37 onto Mahalasville Road to rejoin the route.
 &nbsp\; Revised GPS files are provided below.</b><br><br><a href="http://bl
 oomingtonbicycleclub.org/maps/John_Bassett_Maps/M_-_M_-Martinsville-Mahalas
 ville-_via_South_Shore_60.pdf">M&amp\;M Ride (Martinsville-Mahalasville) vi
 a South Shore</a><br><br><a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/36107982">
 Revised GPS Files</a><br><br>This is a fun\, moderate 60 mile ride that inc
 orporates some fast flats and just a few healthy climbs.&nbsp\; We do a cou
 ple of modifications to the traditional route to accommodate the new traffi
 c patterns resultant from I-69 and bypass some climbs on busy SR 45 on the 
 return route.<br><br>Non-members should sign up for a <a href="https://secu
 re.getmeregistered.com/get_information.php?event_id=133776">free trial memb
 ership</a>\, good for up to three rides\, and which includes electronically
  signing a liability waiver\,&nbsp\;prior to participation.&nbsp\;&nbsp\;
LAST-MODIFIED:20210520T225913Z
LOCATION:Bryan Park Pool Parking Lot @ 39.15435\,-86.523
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:M&M Ride (Martinsville-Mahalasville) - Leader: TBD
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
