DESCRIPTION:<a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/2197486">Pine Grove Boa
 t Ramp</a>&nbsp\;16 miles<br><br>Please observe social distancing norms as 
 we gather and ride.&nbsp\;<ul><li>Be SAFE. Don't blow through stop signs. C
 onsider bike lights.<br></li><li>Be COURTEOUS: Single up in traffic<br></li
 ><li>Be PREDICTABLE: Signal your intentions to cars and fellow riders.</li>
 </ul>The "Older\, Wiser\, and a Little Slower" training group emphasizes mo
 derate rides\, and a route planned in advance that is posted on the ride ca
 lendar. This is a no drop ride\, but not a beginner's ride. The OWLS often 
 average 15 to 19 mph on flat roads\, and typically have an overall average 
 moving speed between 12 and 15 mph including hills. Distances vary from 20 
 to 30 miles\, depending partly on available light. Early season rides will 
 be somewhat shorter and slower. Rides depart promptly at 5:45.<br><br>Non-m
 embers should sign up for a <a href="https://secure.getmeregistered.com/get
 _information.php?event_id=133776">free trial membership</a>\, good for up t
 o three rides\, and which includes electronically signing a liability waive
 r\,&nbsp\;prior to participation.<br><br>Questions? Contact&nbsp\;<a href="
 mailto:gail.morell@gmail.com">Gail Morell</a>.
