 oute and assist others as needed.</i><br><ul><li>Be SAFE. Don't blow throug
 h stop signs. Consider bike lights.<br></li><li>Be COURTEOUS: Single up in 
 traffic<br></li><li>Be PREDICTABLE: Signal your intentions to cars and fell
 ow riders.</li></ul>This branch of the OWLS training group also emphasizes 
 somewhat slower\, moderate rides\, and a route planned in advance that is p
 osted on the ride calendar. This is a no drop ride\, but not a beginner's r
 ide. Expect an overall average moving speed 11 - 15 mph including hills. Di
 stances vary from 20 to 30 miles. Early season rides will be somewhat short
 er and slower. Rides depart promptly at 9:30am.<br><br>Non-members should s
