DESCRIPTION:Too much rain.&nbsp\;<br><br>Watch the calendar for weather-rel
 ated updates and for future rides.<br><br><i>Please observe social distanci
 ng norms as we gather and ride. We plan no formal leader. EVERYONE is a lea
 der. Familiarize yourself with the ride before heading out. We will ride in
  small groups. People in the last group will endeavor to sweep the route an
 d assist others as needed.</i><ul><li>Be SAFE. Don't blow through stop sign
 s. Consider bike lights.<br></li><li>Be COURTEOUS: Single up in traffic<br>
 </li><li>Be PREDICTABLE: Signal your intentions to cars and fellow riders.<
 /li></ul>This branch of the OWLS training group also emphasizes somewhat sl
 ower\, moderate rides\, and a route planned in advance that is posted on th
 e ride calendar. This is a no drop ride\, but not a beginner's ride. Expect
  an overall average moving speed 11 - 15 mph including hills. Distances var
 y from 20 to 30 miles. Early season rides will be somewhat shorter and slow
 er. Rides depart promptly at 9:30am.<br><br>Non-members should sign up for 
 a <a href="https://secure.getmeregistered.com/get_information.php?event_id=
 133776">free trial membership</a>\, good for up to three rides\, and which 
 includes electronically signing a liability waiver\,&nbsp\;prior to partici
 pation.<br><br>Questions? Contact <a href="mailto:allan.edmonds@gmail.com">
 Allan Edmonds</a>
