DESCRIPTION:<a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/19778195" id="ow855" __
 is_owner="true">Short Russell</a>&nbsp\;19 miles<br><ul><li>Be SAFE. Don't 
 blow through stop signs. Consider bike lights.<br></li><li>Be COURTEOUS: Si
 ngle up in traffic<br></li><li>Be PREDICTABLE: Signal your intentions to ca
 rs and fellow riders.</li></ul>The "Older\, Wiser\, and a Little Slower" tr
 aining group emphasizes moderate rides\, and a route planned in advance tha
 t is posted on the ride calendar. This is a no drop ride\, but not a beginn
 er's ride. The OWLS often average 15 to 19 mph on flat roads\, and typicall
 y have an overall average moving speed between 12 and 15 mph including hill
 s. Distances vary from 20 to 30 miles\, depending partly on available light
 . Early season rides will be somewhat shorter and slower. Rides depart prom
 ptly at 5:45.<br><br>Non-members will be required to sign a <a href="https:
 //drive.google.com/file/d/1jDxK92FPgpyvj2cCT7vV2S8RZTWDR_RH/view" target="_
 blank">liability waiver</a> prior to participation.<br><br>Questions? Conta
