DESCRIPTION:CANCELLED.\n<br><br>Watch the calendar for weather-related upda
 tes and for future rides.<br><br><i>Please observe social distancing norms 
 as we gather and ride. We plan no formal leader. EVERYONE is a leader. Fami
 liarize yourself with the ride before heading out. We will ride in small gr
 oups. People in the last group will endeavor to sweep the route and assist 
 others as needed.</i><br><ul><li>Be SAFE. Don't blow through stop signs. Co
 nsider bike lights.<br></li><li>Be COURTEOUS: Single up in traffic<br></li>
 <li>Be PREDICTABLE: Signal your intentions to cars and fellow riders.</li><
 /ul>This branch of the OWLS training group also emphasizes somewhat slower\
 , moderate rides\, and a route planned in advance that is posted on the rid
 e calendar. This is a no drop ride\, but not a beginner's ride. Expect an o
 verall average moving speed 11 - 15 mph including hills. Distances vary fro
 m 20 to 30 miles. Early season rides will be somewhat shorter and slower. R
 ides depart promptly at 9:30am.<br><br>Non-members should sign up for a <a 
 href="https://secure.getmeregistered.com/get_information.php?event_id=13377
 6">free trial membership</a>\, good for up to three rides\, and which inclu
 des electronically signing a liability waiver\,&nbsp\;prior to participatio
 n.<br><br>Questions? Contact <a href="mailto:allan.edmonds@gmail.com">Allan
  Edmonds</a>
