  plan no formal leader. EVERYONE is a leader. Familiarize yourself with the
  ride before heading out. We will ride in small groups. People in the last 
 group will endeavor to sweep the route and assist others as needed.</i><br>
 <ul><li>Be SAFE. Don't blow through stop signs. Consider bike lights.<br></
 li><li>Be COURTEOUS: Single up in traffic<br></li><li>Be PREDICTABLE: Signa
 l your intentions to cars and fellow riders.</li></ul>This branch of the OW
 LS training group also emphasizes somewhat slower\, moderate rides\, and a 
 route planned in advance that is posted on the ride calendar. This is a no 
 drop ride\, but not a beginner's ride. Expect an overall average moving spe
 ed 11 - 15 mph including hills. Distances vary from 20 to 30 miles. Early s
 eason rides will be somewhat shorter and slower. Rides depart promptly at 9
 :30am.<br><br>Non-members should sign up for a <a href="https://secure.getm
 eregistered.com/get_information.php?event_id=133776">free trial membership<
 /a>\, good for up to three rides\, and which includes electronically signin
 g a liability waiver\,&nbsp\;prior to participation.<br><br>Questions? Cont
 act <a href="mailto:allan.edmonds@gmail.com">Allan Edmonds</a>
