 or weather-related updates and for future rides.&nbsp\;<ul><li>Be SAFE. Don
 't blow through stop signs. Consider bike lights.<br></li><li>Be COURTEOUS:
  Single up in traffic<br></li><li>Be PREDICTABLE: Signal your intentions to
  cars and fellow riders.</li></ul>This branch of the OWLS training group al
 so emphasizes somewhat slower\, moderate rides\, and a route planned in adv
 ance that is posted on the ride calendar. This is a no drop ride\, but not 
 a beginner's ride. Expect an overall average moving speed 11 - 15 mph inclu
 ding hills. Distances vary from 20 to 30 miles. Early season rides will be 
 somewhat shorter and slower. Rides depart promptly at 9:30am.<br><br>Non-me
 mbers should sign up for a <a href="https://secure.getmeregistered.com/get_
 information.php?event_id=133776">free trial membership</a>\, good for up to
