DESCRIPTION:<a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/37555570" id="ow674" __
 is_owner="true">Tramway </a>20 miles<br><br>Please observe social distancin
 g norms as we gather and ride.&nbsp\;<ul><li>Be SAFE. Don't blow through st
 op signs. Consider bike lights.<br></li><li>Be COURTEOUS: Single up in traf
 fic<br></li><li>Be PREDICTABLE: Signal your intentions to cars and fellow r
 iders.</li></ul>The "Older\, Wiser\, and a Little Slower" training group em
 phasizes moderate rides\, and a route planned in advance that is posted on 
 the ride calendar. This is a no drop ride\, but not a beginner's ride. The 
 OWLS often average 15 to 19 mph on flat roads\, and typically have an overa
 ll average moving speed between 12 and 15 mph including hills. Distances va
 ry from 20 to 30 miles\, depending partly on available light. Early season 
 rides will be somewhat shorter and slower. Rides depart promptly at 5:45.<b
 r><br>Non-members should sign up for a <a href="https://secure.getmeregiste
 red.com/get_information.php?event_id=133776">free trial membership</a>\, go
 od for up to three rides\, and which includes electronically signing a liab
 ility waiver\,&nbsp\;prior to participation.<br><br>Questions? Contact&nbsp
 \;<a href="mailto:gail.morell@gmail.com">Gail Morell</a>.
