DESCRIPTION:<a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/33523208" id="ow906" __
 is_owner="true">South Shore Shuffle to Russell</a> 28 miles<br><br>Please o
 bserve social distancing norms as we gather and ride. We plan no formal lea
 der. EVERYONE is a leader. Familiarize yourself with the ride before headin
 g out. We will ride in small groups.People in the last group will endeavor 
 to sweep the route and assist others as needed.<br><ul><li>Be SAFE. Don't b
 low through stop signs. Consider bike lights.<br></li><li>Be COURTEOUS: Sin
 gle up in traffic<br></li><li>Be PREDICTABLE: Signal your intentions to car
 s and fellow riders.</li></ul>The "Older\, Wiser\, and a Little Slower" tra
 ining group emphasizes moderate rides\, and a route planned in advance that
  is posted on the ride calendar. This is a no drop ride\, but not a beginne
 r's ride. The OWLS often average 15 to 19 mph on flat roads\, and typically
  have an overall average moving speed between 12 and 15 mph including hills
 . Distances vary from 20 to 30 miles\, depending partly on available light.
  Early season rides will be somewhat shorter and slower. Rides depart promp
 tly at 5:45.<br><br>Non-members should sign up for a <a href="https://secur
 e.getmeregistered.com/get_information.php?event_id=133776">free trial membe
 rship</a>\, good for up to three rides\, and which includes electronically 
 signing a liability waiver\,&nbsp\;prior to participation.<br><br>Questions
 ? Contact <a href="mailto:allan.edmonds@gmail.com">Allan Edmonds</a> or <a 
 href="mailto:gail.morell@gmail.com">Gail Morell</a>
LAST-MODIFIED:20200728T111406Z
