  up in traffic<br></li><li>Be PREDICTABLE: Signal your intentions to cars a
 nd fellow riders.</li></ul>The "Older\, Wiser\, and a Little Slower" traini
 ng group emphasizes moderate rides\, and a route planned in advance that is
  posted on the ride calendar. This is a no drop ride\, but not a beginner's
  ride. The OWLS often average 15 to 19 mph on flat roads\, and typically ha
 ve an overall average moving speed between 12 and 15 mph including hills. D
 istances vary from 20 to 30 miles\, depending partly on available light. Ea
 rly season rides will be somewhat shorter and slower. Rides depart promptly
  at 5:45.<br><br>Non-members should sign up for a <a href="https://secure.g
 etmeregistered.com/get_information.php?event_id=133776">free trial membersh
