CREATED:20201219T202705Z
DESCRIPTION:<p>The 5th annual Christmas Bike Ride. Sunday\, December 20th&n
 bsp\; @ 4:30 p.m.</p><p>&nbsp\;<b><u>Please wear a mask</u></b></p><p>&nbsp
 \;A year has passed since Santa was last seen on his cruiser bike in Bloomi
 ngton. That means it's time to dust off your Christmas spirit and your bicy
 cle and parade it down the B-line.</p><p>Decorate your bike and yourself (l
 ights encouraged) for a short holiday cruise. We will meet at the Country C
 lub Trail Head for a spin up the B-line to the Sample gates and back. . It'
 s your annual opportunity to display your ugliest holiday sweater\, favorit
 e Christmas morning pj’s\, killer bike light display \,pine bough arrangeme
 nt expertise\, or whatever other weird holiday mojo you want to share with 
 the unsuspecting pedestrians of our little burg.&nbsp\;</p><p>Bring your bi
 ke (of course).</p><p>Bring the kids. </p><p>Bring a helmet. </p><p>Leave&n
 bsp\; your sense of dignity at home.</p><p>&nbsp\;</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20201219T202705Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Ride with Santa
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Bicycle Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20201015T174500
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20201015T194500
DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:15rm2p5r1cldsblb0bmpeaofq5_R20200721T214500@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20201015T174500
CREATED:20200525T122037Z
DESCRIPTION:<p><a href="https://bloomingtonbicycleclub.org/maps/iRides/Kerr
 _Creek_Russell_Loop_20.pdf" id="ow352" __is_owner="true">Kerr Creek Russell
  Loop 20</a><br></p><p><a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/6277848" id=
 "ow362" __is_owner="true">GPS Files</a><br></p><p>The iRide is a no-drop In
 termediate level ride of moderate pace and distance with regrouping points.
 &nbsp\; Pace is anticipated to be 15-17 mph.</p><p>The tRide is an advanced
  level ride of high pace and moderate distance that may or may not include 
 regrouping points. &nbsp\;Pace is anticipated to be 18+ mph. Expect occasio
 nal sprint or Strava segments\, pace line riding at high speed\, intervals\
 , and fewer regrouping stops.</p><p>The iRide and tRide will start at the s
 ame place and will ride the same scheduled route\, but the start of these t
 wo groups will be staggered with the tRide starting first at 5:45 and the i
 Ride just behind them. Mileages will increase as the season progresses.&nbs
 p\; </p><p>Riders are expected to look out for each other during the rides.
 &nbsp\; Ride maps and GPS links will be posted here in advance. Riders unfa
 miliar with the route should bring along a copy of the map.</p>Non-members 
