DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u><u></u><u></u><a href="https://ridewithgps.co
 m/routes/3498661" id="ow417" __is_owner="true">https://ridewithgps.com/rout
 es/3498661</a><br><br>Please observe social distancing norms as we gather a
 nd ride.&nbsp\;<ul><li>Be SAFE. Don't blow through stop signs. Consider bik
 e lights.<br></li><li>Be COURTEOUS: Single up in traffic<br></li><li>Be PRE
 DICTABLE: Signal your intentions to cars and fellow riders.</li></ul>The "O
 lder\, Wiser\, and a Little Slower" training group emphasizes moderate ride
 s\, and a route planned in advance that is posted on the ride calendar. Thi
 s is a no drop ride\, but not a beginner's ride.The OWLS group welcomes a w
 ide range of intermediate riders\, and typically breaks off into a faster a
 nd slower group with the former averaging an overall moving speed of 16-18 
 mph\, and the slower group averaging 13-15 mph (including hills).&nbsp\;Dis
 tances vary from 20 to 30 miles\, depending partly on available light. Earl
 y season rides will be somewhat shorter and slower. Rides depart promptly a
 t 5:45.<br><br>Non-members should sign up for a <a href="https://secure.get
 meregistered.com/get_information.php?event_id=136627">free trial membership
 </a>\, good for up to three rides\, and which includes electronically signi
 ng a liability waiver\,&nbsp\;prior to participation.<br><br>Questions? Con
 tact&nbsp\;<a href="mailto:gail.morell@gmail.com">Gail Morell</a>.<u></u><u
 ></u><u></u></html-blob>
LAST-MODIFIED:20220920T161237Z
