DESCRIPTION:<a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/3035863" id="ow408" __i
 s_owner="true">Pine Grove Boat Ramp</a> via Stipp and Swartz Ridge 20 miles
 <br><ul><li>Be SAFE. Don't blow through stop signs. Consider bike lights.<b
 r></li><li>Be COURTEOUS: Single up in traffic<br></li><li>Be PREDICTABLE: S
 ignal your intentions to cars and fellow riders.</li></ul>The "Older\, Wise
 r\, and a Little Slower" training group emphasizes moderate rides\, and a r
 oute planned in advance that is posted on the ride calendar. This is a no d
 rop ride\, but not a beginner's ride. The OWLS often average 15 to 19 mph o
 n flat roads\, and typically have an overall average moving speed between 1
 2 and 15 mph including hills. Distances vary from 20 to 30 miles\, dependin
 g partly on available light. Early season rides will be somewhat shorter an
 d slower. Rides depart promptly at 5:45.<br><br>Non-members will be require
 d to sign a <a href="https://drive.google.com/file/d/1jDxK92FPgpyvj2cCT7vV2
 S8RZTWDR_RH/view">liability waiver</a> prior to participation.<br><br>Quest
 ions? Contact <a href="mailto:allan.edmonds@gmail.com">Allan Edmonds</a> or
  <a href="mailto:gail.morell@gmail.com">Gail Morell</a>
