DESCRIPTION:<p><a href="https://bloomingtonbicycleclub.org/maps/iRides/Circ
 le_West_Rev_1_33.pdf" id="ow387" __is_owner="true">Circle West Rev1 33</a><
 br></p><p><a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/23981175" id="ow377" __is
 _owner="true">GPS Files</a></p><p>The iRide is a no-drop Intermediate level
  ride of moderate pace and distance with regrouping points.&nbsp\; Pace is 
 anticipated to be 15-17 mph.<br></p><p>The tRide is an advanced level ride 
 of high pace and moderate distance that may or may not include regrouping p
 oints. &nbsp\;Pace is anticipated to be 18+ mph. Expect occasional sprint o
 r Strava segments\, pace line riding at high speed\, intervals\, and fewer 
 regrouping stops.</p><p>The iRide and tRide will start at the same place an
 d will ride the same scheduled route\, but the start of these two groups wi
 ll be staggered with the tRide starting first at 5:45 and the iRide just be
 hind them. Mileages will increase as the season progresses.&nbsp\; </p><p>R
 iders are expected to look out for each other during the rides.&nbsp\; Ride
  maps and GPS links will be posted here in advance. Riders unfamiliar with 
 the route should bring along a copy of the map.</p>Non-members should sign 
 up for a&nbsp\;<a href="https://secure.getmeregistered.com/get_information.
 php?event_id=133776">free trial membership</a>\, good for up to three rides
 \, and which includes electronically signing a liability waiver\,&nbsp\;pri
 or to participation.
LAST-MODIFIED:20220614T150539Z
LOCATION:Bryan Park Pool Parking Lot @ 39.15435\,-86.523
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:iRide / tRide - Circle West Rev1 33
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Bicycle Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20201020T174500
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20201020T194500
DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:9p45m8hkqk5cb1cv973v44b00o@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20201020T174500
CREATED:20200302T150145Z
DESCRIPTION:<a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/31260845" id="ow1671" _
 _is_owner="true">Bolin and Rockport</a> 16 miles<br><br>Please observe soci
 al distancing norms as we gather and ride. We plan no formal leader. EVERYO
 NE is a leader. Familiarize yourself with the ride before heading out. We w
 ill ride in small groups.People in the last group will endeavor to sweep th
 e route and assist others as needed.<br><ul><li>Be SAFE. Don't blow through
  stop signs. Consider bike lights.<br></li><li>Be COURTEOUS: Single up in t
 raffic<br></li><li>Be PREDICTABLE: Signal your intentions to cars and fello
 w riders.</li></ul>The "Older\, Wiser\, and a Little Slower" training group
  emphasizes moderate rides\, and a route planned in advance that is posted 
 on the ride calendar. This is a no drop ride\, but not a beginner's ride. T
 he OWLS often average 15 to 19 mph on flat roads\, and typically have an ov
 erall average moving speed between 12 and 15 mph including hills. Distances
  vary from 20 to 30 miles\, depending partly on available light. Early seas
 on rides will be somewhat shorter and slower. Rides depart promptly at 5:45
 .<br><br>Non-members should sign up for a <a href="https://secure.getmeregi
 stered.com/get_information.php?event_id=133776">free trial membership</a>\,
  good for up to three rides\, and which includes electronically signing a l
 iability waiver\,&nbsp\;prior to participation.<br><br>Questions? Contact <
 a href="mailto:allan.edmonds@gmail.com">Allan Edmonds</a> or <a href="mailt
 o:gail.morell@gmail.com">Gail Morell</a>
LAST-MODIFIED:20201012T224124Z
LOCATION:Sherwood Oaks Christian Church\, 2700 E Rogers Rd\, Bloomington\, 
 IN 47401\, USA
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:OWLS - Bolin and Rockport
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Bicycle Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20210911T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20210911T140000
DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:1o8ek474md65uon7vi4a1pfqgf@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20210911T090000
CREATED:20210228T161501Z
DESCRIPTION:<p><a href="https://bloomingtonbicycleclub.org/maps/John_Basset
 t_Maps/Joes_Cemetery_Ride_74.pdf">Joe's Cemetery Ride 74</a></p><p><a href=
 "https://ridewithgps.com/routes/37331850">GPS Files</a><br></p><p>On this t
 he twentieth anniversary of 9/11\, the BBC offers a special memorial ride t
 hat honors the three thousand souls that perished that day. It also honors 
 the seven thousand service members who have been killed in the Iraq and Afg
 hanistan wars. </p><p>Last year this ride was the CIBA Cemetery Tour\, and 
 was a drive and ride from Martinsville. This year’s version leaves from Bry
 an Park. While the new route bypasses several of the thirteen cemeteries\, 
 it does incorporate the “Crybaby Bridge”.&nbsp\; It eliminates all of last 
 year’s fresh chip and seal roads and replaces them with many miles of glass
  smooth\, freshly paved blacktop\, and a new crossing of I-69 north of Mart
 insville.</p><p>Services are available at miles 28 and 50 of the route.</p>
 <p>Non-members should sign up for a <a href="https://secure.getmeregistered
 .com/get_information.php?event_id=133776">free trial membership</a>\, good 
 for up to three rides\, and which includes electronically signing a liabili
 ty waiver\,&nbsp\;prior to participation.&nbsp\;&nbsp\;<br></p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20220614T150624Z
LOCATION:Bryan Park Pool Parking Lot @ 39.15435\,-86.523
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Joe's Cemetery Ride 74 - Leader:  Joe Anderson
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
