DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u><u></u><u></u><a href="https://ridewithgps.co
 m/routes/36140374" id="ow1127" __is_owner="true">https://ridewithgps.com/ro
 utes/36140374</a></html-blob><br><html-blob><br><br>Please observe social d
 istancing norms as we gather and ride.&nbsp\;<ul><li>Be SAFE. Don't blow th
 rough stop signs. Consider bike lights.<br></li><li>Be COURTEOUS: Single up
  in traffic<br></li><li>Be PREDICTABLE: Signal your intentions to cars and 
 fellow riders.</li></ul>The "Older\, Wiser\, and a Little Slower" training 
 group emphasizes moderate rides\, and a route planned in advance that is po
 sted on the ride calendar. This is a no drop ride\, but not a beginner's ri
 de.The OWLS group welcomes a wide range of intermediate riders\, and typica
 lly breaks off into a faster and slower group with the former averaging an 
 overall moving speed of 16-18 mph\, and the slower group averaging 13-15 mp
 h (including hills).&nbsp\;Distances vary from 20 to 30 miles\, depending p
 artly on available light. Early season rides will be somewhat shorter and s
 lower. Rides depart promptly at 5:45.<br><br>Non-members should sign up for
  a <a href="https://secure.getmeregistered.com/get_information.php?event_id
 =136627">free trial membership</a>\, good for up to three rides\, and which
  includes electronically signing a liability waiver\,&nbsp\;prior to partic
 ipation.<br><br>Questions? Contact&nbsp\;<a href="mailto:gail.morell@gmail.
 com">Gail Morell</a>.<u></u><u></u><u></u></html-blob>
LAST-MODIFIED:20220731T180215Z
