CREATED:20201108T154015Z
DESCRIPTION:<br><b><br></b><b>Due to weather This ride has been moved to Su
 nday</b><br><b><br></b>Join in for a fun Brown County gravel ride starting 
 and ending at Hard Truth in Nashville.&nbsp\; This is a loop ride borrowed 
 from Jeff Fetterer and has its fair share of ups and downs.&nbsp\; With the
  exception of Covered Bridge Road the clockwise loop generally goes down th
 e steep grades and up the gentler grades.&nbsp\; Get to near the top of Bea
 r Wallow Hill without ever being on Bear Wallow Hill Road. And\, finish up 
 with a great gravel decent on Wallow Hollow.<br><br>Route is entirely grave
 l and pavement&nbsp\;- no trail.&nbsp\;<br><br>Stick around at Hard Truth a
 fter the ride for some great Big Woods food and beverages.<br><b>(they do h
 ave outside setting)</b><br><br>D<b>ue to Covid-19 No formal car pooling wi
 ll be offered</b><br><br><a href="https://bloomingtonbicycleclub.org/maps/G
 ravel_Rides/Jeff-s_Salmeron_-_Wallow_Hollow_Loop_from_Hard_Truth_29.pdf">PD
 F Map and Queue Sheet</a><br><br><a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/31
 648043">GPS Files</a>
LAST-MODIFIED:20201112T232546Z
LOCATION:Big K Parking Lot @ 39.162664\, -86.492045
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Jeff's Salmeron / Wallow Hollow Loop from Hard Truth 29man 
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
