DESCRIPTION:<a href="https://www.bloomingtonbicycleclub.org/maps/BBCMaps/ma
 p_pack_2/low_gap_touchables.pdf">Low Gap to Martinsville ("The Touchables")
 </a><br><br><a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/28325235">GPS Files</a>
 <br><br>51 moderate miles with a 26 mile short option.&nbsp\; This route ta
 kes riders through Morgan Monroe State Forest and past "The Touchables" Scu
 lpture Garden.&nbsp\; Consider coasting and taking a gander at the unique p
 ieces scattered on the west side of the road.<br><br>We will take the new O
 ld 37 connector on the east side of I-69 from the Liberty Church interchang
 e down to Old 37\, more or less duplicating the original mapping of this ri
 de.&nbsp\; But\, you always have the option to spice up your life and take 
 Hacker Creek Road back to Forest Road junction.&nbsp\; Of course\, that mea
 ns climbing the infamous Hacker Creek Hill.<br><br><b>Current information (
 July 19) is that Southview Drive at Mahalasville Road will be open in time 
 for the ride.&nbsp\; Stay tuned for more information on this and an updated
  GPS link\, if needed.</b><br><br>Non-members should sign up for a&nbsp\;<a
  href="https://secure.getmeregistered.com/get_information.php?event_id=1337
 76">free trial membership</a>\, good for up to three rides\, and which incl
 udes electronically signing a liability waiver\,&nbsp\;prior to participati
 on.
