DESCRIPTION:<a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/31013323" id="ow391" __
 is_owner="true">Reverse Short Leonard 22 miles</a><br><br>Please observe so
 cial distancing norms as we gather and ride. We plan no formal leader. EVER
 YONE is a leader. Familiarize yourself with the ride before heading out. We
  will ride in small groups.People in the last group will endeavor to sweep 
 the route and assist others as needed.<br><ul><li>Be SAFE. Don't blow throu
 gh stop signs. Consider bike lights.<br></li><li>Be COURTEOUS: Single up in
  traffic<br></li><li>Be PREDICTABLE: Signal your intentions to cars and fel
 low riders.</li></ul>The "Older\, Wiser\, and a Little Slower" training gro
 up emphasizes moderate rides\, and a route planned in advance that is poste
 d on the ride calendar. This is a no drop ride\, but not a beginner's ride.
  The OWLS often average 15 to 19 mph on flat roads\, and typically have an 
 overall average moving speed between 12 and 15 mph including hills. Distanc
 es vary from 20 to 30 miles\, depending partly on available light. Early se
 ason rides will be somewhat shorter and slower. Rides depart promptly at 5:
 45.<br><br>Non-members should sign up for a <a href="https://secure.getmere
 gistered.com/get_information.php?event_id=133776">free trial membership</a>
 \, good for up to three rides\, and which includes electronically signing a
  liability waiver\,&nbsp\;prior to participation.<br><br>Questions? Contact
  <a href="mailto:allan.edmonds@gmail.com">Allan Edmonds</a> or <a href="mai
 lto:gail.morell@gmail.com">Gail Morell</a>
