CREATED:20210314T144013Z
DESCRIPTION:<p><a href="http://bloomingtonbicycleclub.org/maps/iRides/Sceni
 c_Shilo_30.pdf" id="ow387" __is_owner="true">Scenic Shilo 30</a><br></p><p>
 <a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/27762065" id="ow398" __is_owner="tr
 ue">GPS Files</a><br></p><p>The iRide is a no-drop Intermediate level ride 
 of moderate pace and distance with regrouping points.&nbsp\; Pace is antici
 pated to be 15-17 mph.<br></p><p>The tRide is an advanced level ride of hig
 h pace and moderate distance that may or may not include regrouping points.
  &nbsp\;Pace is anticipated to be 18+ mph. Expect occasional sprint or Stra
 va segments\, pace line riding at high speed\, intervals\, and fewer regrou
 ping stops.</p><p>The iRide and tRide will start at the same place and will
  ride the same scheduled route\, but the start of these two groups will be 
 staggered with the tRide starting first at 5:45 and the iRide just behind t
 hem. Mileages will increase as the season progresses.&nbsp\; </p><p>Riders 
 are expected to look out for each other during the rides.&nbsp\; Ride maps 
 and GPS links will be posted here in advance. Riders unfamiliar with the ro
 ute should bring along a copy of the map.</p>Non-members should sign up for
  a&nbsp\;<a href="https://secure.getmeregistered.com/get_information.php?ev
 ent_id=133776">free trial membership</a>\, good for up to three rides\, and
  which includes electronically signing a liability waiver\,&nbsp\;prior to 
 participation.
LAST-MODIFIED:20220614T150517Z
LOCATION:Bryan Park Pool Parking Lot @ 39.15435\,-86.523
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:iRide / tRide -Scenic Shilo 30
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Bicycle Club
DTSTART:20200808T130000Z
DTEND:20200808T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:7j5oktpjs0ktap0q36jdjdlhcd@google.com
CREATED:20190527T132723Z
DESCRIPTION:<br><a href="http://bloomingtonbicycleclub.org/maps/John_Basset
 t_Maps/Spring%20Mill%20Leavenworth%2096%20revised.pdf">Spring Mill to Leave
 nworth</a><br><br><a href="http://ridewithgps.com/routes/2970469">GPS Links
 </a><br><br>This is a drive and ride has been very well attended the last s
 everal years\, and&nbsp\;is back by by popular demand. The entire route is 
 96 miles and begins and&nbsp\;ends at Spring Mill State Park.  Start there&
 nbsp\;because a century ride will get you to the Ohio&nbsp\;River and back.
   Shorter options include turning&nbsp\;back north at Marengo for a 63 mile
  loop\, or&nbsp\;turning right at the famous Crawford County&nbsp\;Shoe Tre
 e for about 82 miles.  Tour some of&nbsp\;the best southern Indiana has to 
 offer\, and&nbsp\;enjoy the spectacular view of the Ohio River&nbsp\;at the
  Leavenworth Overlook\, the point where&nbsp\;we turn back north.<br><br>Th
 e first part of the ride is relatively flat\, the middle part is hilly\, an
 d the last part is flat again on a lot of new pavement north of US 150.&nbs
 p\; See Lost River\, Marengo\, the Blue River at Milltown\, the world famou
 s Shoe Tree\, Wyandotte Cave\, the Leavenworth Overlook\, idyllic Amish cou
 ntryside in Orange County\, and the "Knob" you have to go right over the to
 p of.&nbsp\;&nbsp\;<br><br>We will not offer a formal car pool this year du
 e to COVID-19 concerns.&nbsp\; Meet&nbsp\;at Spring Mill State Park Inn (up
 per level of the parking garage) at 9:00.&nbsp\; Bring your park pass.&nbsp
 \;This is a good one.<br><br>Non-members should sign up for a <a href="http
 s://secure.getmeregistered.com/get_information.php?event_id=133776">free tr
 ial membership</a>\, good for up to three rides\, and which includes electr
 onically signing a liability waiver\,&nbsp\;prior to participation.&nbsp\;&
 nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;
LAST-MODIFIED:20200803T172522Z
LOCATION:Spring Mill Parking Garage @38.734265\, -86.414427
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Spring Mill to Leavenworth 96 - Leader: John Bassett
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
