DESCRIPTION:<p><a href="https://bloomingtonbicycleclub.org/maps/John_Basset
 t_Maps/Waterworks_Plus_a_Hill_20.pdf" target="_blank">Waterworks Plus a Hil
 l 20</a><br></p><p><a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/6360172" target=
 "_blank">GPS Files</a><br></p><p>The iRide is a no-drop Intermediate level 
 ride of moderate pace and distance with regrouping points.  Pace is anticip
 ated to be 15-17 mph.</p><p>The tRide is an advanced level ride of high pac
 e and moderate distance that may or may not include regrouping points.  Pac
 e is anticipated to be 18+ mph. Expect occasional sprint or Strava segments
 \, pace line riding at high speed\, intervals\, and fewer regrouping stops.
 </p><p>The iRide and tRide will start at the same place and will ride the s
 ame scheduled route\, but the start of these two groups will be staggered w
 ith the tRide starting first at 5:45 and the iRide just behind them. Mileag
 es will increase as the season progresses.  </p><p>Riders are expected to l
 ook out for each other during the rides.  Ride maps and GPS links will be p
 osted here in advance. Riders unfamiliar with the route should bring along 
 a copy of the map.</p>Non-members should sign up for a <a href="https://sec
 ure.getmeregistered.com/get_information.php?event_id=133776" target="_blank
 ">free trial membership</a>\, good for up to three rides\, and which includ
 es electronically signing a liability waiver\, prior to participation.
