DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u><u></u><u></u><a href="https://ridewithgps.co
 m/routes/25778799" id="ow1319" __is_owner="true">https://ridewithgps.com/ro
 utes/25778799</a><br><br>Please observe social distancing norms as we gathe
 r and ride.&nbsp\;<ul><li>Be SAFE. Don't blow through stop signs. Consider 
 bike lights.<br></li><li>Be COURTEOUS: Single up in traffic<br></li><li>Be 
 PREDICTABLE: Signal your intentions to cars and fellow riders.</li></ul>The
  "Older\, Wiser\, and a Little Slower" training group emphasizes moderate r
 ides\, and a route planned in advance that is posted on the ride calendar. 
 This is a no drop ride\, but not a beginner's ride.The OWLS group welcomes 
 a wide range of intermediate riders\, and typically breaks off into a faste
 r and slower group with the former averaging an overall moving speed of 16-
 18 mph\, and the slower group averaging 13-15 mph (including hills).&nbsp\;
 Distances vary from 20 to 30 miles\, depending partly on available light. E
 arly season rides will be somewhat shorter and slower. Rides depart promptl
 y at 5:45.<br><br>Non-members should sign up for a <a href="https://secure.
 getmeregistered.com/get_information.php?event_id=136627">free trial members
 hip</a>\, good for up to three rides\, and which includes electronically si
 gning a liability waiver\,&nbsp\;prior to participation.<br><br>Questions? 
 Contact&nbsp\;<a href="mailto:gail.morell@gmail.com">Gail Morell</a>.<u></u
 ><u></u><u></u></html-blob>
