 s</a></p><p>The iRide is an intermediate level ride of moderate pace and di
 stance with regrouping points.&nbsp\; Pace is anticipated to be 15-17 mph.<
 br></p><p>The tRide is an advanced level ride of high pace and moderate dis
 tance that may or may not include regrouping points. &nbsp\;Pace is anticip
 ated to be 18+ mph. Expect occasional sprint or Strava segments\, pace line
  riding at high speed\, intervals\, and fewer regrouping stops.</p><p>The i
 Ride and tRide will start at the same place and will ride the same schedule
 d route\, but the start of these two groups will be staggered with the tRid
 e starting first at 5:45 and the iRide just behind them. Mileages will incr
 ease as the season progresses.&nbsp\; </p><p>Riders are expected to look ou
 t for each other during the rides.&nbsp\; Ride maps and GPS links will be p
 osted here in advance. Riders unfamiliar with the route should bring along 
 a copy of the map.</p>Non-members should sign up for a&nbsp\;<a href="https
 ://secure.getmeregistered.com/get_information.php?event_id=133776">free tri
 al membership</a>\, good for up to three rides\, and which includes electro
 nically signing a liability waiver\,&nbsp\;prior to participation.
