 back through <a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/38343514" id="ow1060" 
 __is_owner="true">Cascades</a>. Longer version back on <a href="https://rid
 ewithgps.com/routes/38343505" id="ow1047" __is_owner="true">Mt. Gilead and 
 Kerr Creek</a>. (22 miles)<br><br>Watch the calendar for weather-related up
 dates and for future rides.&nbsp\;<ul><li>Be SAFE. Don't blow through stop 
 signs. Consider bike lights.<br></li><li>Be COURTEOUS: Single up in traffic
 <br></li><li>Be PREDICTABLE: Signal your intentions to cars and fellow ride
 rs.</li></ul>This branch of the OWLS training group also emphasizes somewha
 t slower\, moderate rides\, and a route planned in advance that is posted o
 n the ride calendar. This is a no drop ride\, but not a beginner's ride. Ex
 pect an overall average moving speed 11 - 15 mph including hills. Distances
  vary from 20 to 30 miles. Early season rides will be somewhat shorter and 
 slower.During cold weather the ride departs at 1:30pm.<br><br>Non-members s
 hould sign up for a&nbsp\;<a href="https://secure.getmeregistered.com/get_i
 nformation.php?event_id=133776">free trial membership</a>\, good for up to 
 three rides\, and which includes electronically signing a liability waiver\
 ,&nbsp\;prior to participation.<br><br>Questions? Contact&nbsp\;<a href="ma
 ilto:allan.edmonds@gmail.com">Allan Edmonds</a>
