DESCRIPTION:<a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/33346254" id="ow644" __
 is_owner="true">Triple Creek</a> 26 miles<br><br>Please observe social dist
 ancing norms as we gather and ride. We plan no formal leader. EVERYONE is a
  leader. Familiarize yourself with the ride before heading out. We will rid
 e in small groups.People in the last group will endeavor to sweep the route
  and assist others as needed.<br><ul><li>Be SAFE. Don't blow through stop s
 igns. Consider bike lights.<br></li><li>Be COURTEOUS: Single up in traffic<
 br></li><li>Be PREDICTABLE: Signal your intentions to cars and fellow rider
 s.</li></ul>The "Older\, Wiser\, and a Little Slower" training group emphas
 izes moderate rides\, and a route planned in advance that is posted on the 
 ride calendar. This is a no drop ride\, but not a beginner's ride. The OWLS
  often average 15 to 19 mph on flat roads\, and typically have an overall a
 verage moving speed between 12 and 15 mph including hills. Distances vary f
 rom 20 to 30 miles\, depending partly on available light. Early season ride
 s will be somewhat shorter and slower. Rides depart promptly at 5:45.<br><b
 r>Non-members should sign up for a <a href="https://secure.getmeregistered.
 com/get_information.php?event_id=133776">free trial membership</a>\, good f
 or up to three rides\, and which includes electronically signing a liabilit
 y waiver\,&nbsp\;prior to participation.<br><br>Questions? Contact <a href=
 "mailto:allan.edmonds@gmail.com">Allan Edmonds</a> or <a href="mailto:gail.
 morell@gmail.com">Gail Morell</a>
