DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/39354417" id
 ="ow709" __is_owner="true">https://ridewithgps.com/routes/39354417</a><br><
 u></u><br>Please observe social distancing norms as we gather and ride.&nbs
 p\;<ul><li>Be SAFE. Don't blow through stop signs. Consider bike lights.<br
 ></li><li>Be COURTEOUS: Single up in traffic<br></li><li>Be PREDICTABLE: Si
 gnal your intentions to cars and fellow riders.</li></ul>The "Older\, Wiser
 \, and a Little Slower" training group emphasizes moderate rides\, and a ro
 ute planned in advance that is posted on the ride calendar. This is a no dr
 op ride\, but not a beginner's ride. The OWLS often average 15 to 19 mph on
  flat roads\, and typically have an overall average moving speed between 12
  and 15 mph including hills. Distances vary from 20 to 30 miles\, depending
  partly on available light. Early season rides will be somewhat shorter and
  slower. Rides depart promptly at 5:45.<br><br>Non-members should sign up f
 or a <a href="https://secure.getmeregistered.com/get_information.php?event_
 id=136627">free trial membership</a>\, good for up to three rides\, and whi
 ch includes electronically signing a liability waiver\,&nbsp\;prior to part
 icipation.<br><br>Questions? Contact&nbsp\;<a href="mailto:gail.morell@gmai
 l.com">Gail Morell</a>.<u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u></html-blob>
