 er="true">GPS Files</a><br></p><p>The iRide is a no-drop Intermediate level
  ride of moderate pace and distance with regrouping points.&nbsp\; Pace is 
 anticipated to be 15-17 mph.<br></p><p>The tRide is an advanced level ride 
 of high pace and moderate distance that may or may not include regrouping p
 oints. &nbsp\;Pace is anticipated to be 18+ mph. Expect occasional sprint o
 r Strava segments\, pace line riding at high speed\, intervals\, and fewer 
 regrouping stops.</p><p>The iRide and tRide will start at the same place an
 d will ride the same scheduled route\, but the start of these two groups wi
 ll be staggered with the tRide starting first at 5:45 and the iRide just be
 hind them. Mileages will increase as the season progresses.&nbsp\; </p><p>R
 iders are expected to look out for each other during the rides.&nbsp\; Ride
  maps and GPS links will be posted here in advance. Riders unfamiliar with 
 the route should bring along a copy of the map.</p>Non-members should sign 
 up for a&nbsp\;<a href="https://secure.getmeregistered.com/get_information.
 php?event_id=133776">free trial membership</a>\, good for up to three rides
 \, and which includes electronically signing a liability waiver\,&nbsp\;pri
 or to participation.<br><br>&nbsp\;<br><br>&nbsp\;&nbsp\;
