DESCRIPTION:Watch the calendar weather-related updates and for future morni
 ng rides.<br><br><i>Please observe social distancing norms as we gather and
  ride. We plan no formal leader. EVERYONE is a leader. Familiarize yourself
  with the ride before heading out. We will ride in small groups. People in 
 the last group will endeavor to sweep the route and assist others as needed
 .</i><br><ul><li>Be SAFE. Don't blow through stop signs. Consider bike ligh
 ts.<br></li><li>Be COURTEOUS: Single up in traffic<br></li><li>Be PREDICTAB
 LE: Signal your intentions to cars and fellow riders.</li></ul>This branch 
 of the OWLS training group also emphasizes somewhat slower\, moderate rides
 \, and a route planned in advance that is posted on the ride calendar. This
  is a no drop ride\, but not a beginner's ride. Expect an overall average m
 oving speed 11 - 15 mph including hills. Distances vary from 20 to 30 miles
 . Early season rides will be somewhat shorter and slower. Rides depart prom
 ptly at 8:30am.<br><br>Non-members should sign up for a <a href="https://se
 cure.getmeregistered.com/get_information.php?event_id=133776">free trial me
 mbership</a>\, good for up to three rides\, and which includes electronical
 ly signing a liability waiver\,&nbsp\;prior to participation.<br><br>Questi
 ons? Contact <a href="mailto:allan.edmonds@gmail.com">Allan Edmonds</a>
LAST-MODIFIED:20200916T183754Z
