BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Bicycle Club
DTSTART:20220907T220000Z
DTEND:20220908T003000Z
DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:2s7s2a94j6i2onhjnh2vf978k7@google.com
CREATED:20220906T002915Z
DESCRIPTION:<u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u>
 <p><a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://ridewithgps.com/routes/343
 96702&amp\;sa=D&amp\;source=calendar&amp\;usd=2&amp\;usg=AOvVaw2YpFYSgSDcMa
 MgL7-XBKAF" target="_blank">Tulip Tree Trek 20</a><br></p><p><b>Description
 </b><br></p><p>This is a great route through the woods of Yellowwood State 
 Forest.  Ride starts at the parking lot on the north side of Yellowwood Lak
 e.  We loop south to SR 46 then north to Tulip Tree Road.  We go east on La
 nam Ridge\, turn right on Dubois Ridge Road\, and go south to Yellowwood Ro
 ad / Yellowwood Lake Road back to the parking area.  Route is gravel and do
 uble track with some pavement and is suitable for MTB or gravel bike.</p><p
 ><b>About the Off Road Rides</b></p><p>These rides feature gravel roads\, s
 ingle and double track trails\,  and just enough pavement to string the afo
 rementioned together into fun\, woodsy adventure loops.  Rides begin at 6PM
  through the Fall and Winter months as weather allows and typically last ab
 out two hours.  Lights are mandatory as we enter the Fall and Winter season
 s.</p><p>Routes are suitable for mountain bike or gravel bike\, with some m
 ore turned to one or the other.  Rides begin at different locations\, prima
 rily associated with Yellowwood State Forest\, Brown County State Park\, an
 d the Hoosier National Forest in Monroe\, Lawrence\, and Brown Counties.  S
 pecific routes may be dictated by weather conditions\, but starting locatio
 ns\, route maps\, and gps file links will be posted here in advance.</p><p>
 Expect a lot of trees and few cars.  </p><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u
 ><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u>
LAST-MODIFIED:20220906T002916Z
LOCATION:39.191900\, -86.342878
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Off Road Ride - Tulip Tree Trek 20
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Bicycle Club
DTSTART:20191211T223000Z
DTEND:20191212T013000Z
DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:1c8kdajs2u0u17ohsv81kk04o6@google.com
CREATED:20201129T164351Z
DESCRIPTION:This 20-miler begins at the Blackwell Horse<br>Camp on Tower Ri
 dge Road\, extends<br>down Dutch Ridge Road\, and loops<br>back to Blackwel
 l via Henderson Creek\,<br>Hickory Grove\, and Tower Ridge.  The<br>route i
 s a mix of one-half HNF gravel and<br>one-half paved county road.  There is
 <br>no single or double track.<br>XC or MTB are fine.<br><br>Meet at 5:30PM
  at the former K-Mart<br>East parking lot to car pool.  The ride<br>leaves 
 from Blackwell Horse Camp<br>on Tower Ridge Road about 6:00PM.<br><br>BRING
  LIGHTS !!<br>&nbsp\;<br><a href="http://bloomingtonbicycleclub.org/maps/Gr
 avel_Rides/Going%20Dutch%20Ridge%2020.pdf" target="_blank">Going Dutch Ridg
 e 20<a></a><br><br><a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/17995313" target
 ="_blank">GPS Files<a></a></a></a>
