DESCRIPTION:<a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/31260886">Shady Side + 
 Boat Ramp</a><br><br>Please observe social distancing norms as we gather an
 d ride.&nbsp\;<ul><li>Be SAFE. Don't blow through stop signs. Consider bike
  lights.<br></li><li>Be COURTEOUS: Single up in traffic<br></li><li>Be PRED
 ICTABLE: Signal your intentions to cars and fellow riders.</li></ul>The "Ol
 der\, Wiser\, and a Little Slower" training group emphasizes moderate rides
 \, and a route planned in advance that is posted on the ride calendar. This
  is a no drop ride\, but not a beginner's ride. The OWLS often average 15 t
 o 19 mph on flat roads\, and typically have an overall average moving speed
  between 12 and 15 mph including hills. Distances vary from 20 to 30 miles\
 , depending partly on available light. Early season rides will be somewhat 
 shorter and slower. Rides depart promptly at 5:45.<br><br>Non-members shoul
 d sign up for a <a href="https://secure.getmeregistered.com/get_information
 .php?event_id=133776">free trial membership</a>\, good for up to three ride
 s\, and which includes electronically signing a liability waiver\,&nbsp\;pr
 ior to participation.<br><br>Questions? Contact&nbsp\;<a href="mailto:gail.
 morell@gmail.com">Gail Morell</a>.
LAST-MODIFIED:20211014T010756Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:OWLS Ride - Shady Side
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Bicycle Club
DTSTART:20211218T213000Z
DTEND:20211218T230000Z
DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:4utge5massfuu6vllemdlqijr9@google.com
CREATED:20211205T135011Z
DESCRIPTION:<p><b>It looks like the Rain will pass and allow us to ride wit
 h Santa today</b></p><p><b>The ride is a go!</b></p><p><b>The 6th annual Ch
 ristmas Bike Ride. Saturda</b>y\, December 18th&nbsp\; @ 4:30 p.m.</p><p>&n
 bsp\;A year has passed since Santa was last seen on his cruiser bike in Blo
 omington. That means it's time to dust off your Christmas spirit and your b
 icycle and parade it down the B-line.<br></p><p>Decorate your bike and your
 self (lights encouraged) for a short holiday cruise. We will meet at the Co
 untry Club Trail Head for a spin up the B-line to the Sample gates and back
 . . It's your annual opportunity to display your ugliest holiday sweater\, 
 favorite Christmas morning pj’s\, killer bike light display \,pine bough ar
 rangement expertise\, or whatever other weird holiday mojo you want to shar
 e with the unsuspecting pedestrians of our little burg.&nbsp\;</p><p>Bring 
 your bike (of course).</p><p>Bring the kids. </p><p>Bring a helmet. </p><p>
 Leave&nbsp\; your sense of dignity at home.</p><p>&nbsp\;</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20211218T154217Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Ride with Santa is a go for today!
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
