DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u><u></u><br><br>Please observe social distanci
 ng norms as we gather and ride.&nbsp\;<ul><li>Be SAFE. Don't blow through s
 top signs. Consider bike lights.<br></li><li>Be COURTEOUS: Single up in tra
 ffic<br></li><li>Be PREDICTABLE: Signal your intentions to cars and fellow 
 riders.</li></ul>The "Older\, Wiser\, and a Little Slower" training group e
 mphasizes moderate rides\, and a route planned in advance that is posted on
  the ride calendar. This is a no drop ride\, but not a beginner's ride.The 
 OWLS group welcomes a wide range of intermediate riders\, and typically bre
 aks off into a faster and slower group with the former averaging an overall
  moving speed of 16-18 mph\, and the slower group averaging 13-15 mph (incl
 uding hills).&nbsp\;Distances vary from 20 to 30 miles\, depending partly o
 n available light. Early season rides will be somewhat shorter and slower. 
 Rides depart promptly at 5:45.<br><br>Non-members should sign up for a <a h
 ref="https://secure.getmeregistered.com/get_information.php?event_id=136627
 ">free trial membership</a>\, good for up to three rides\, and which includ
 es electronically signing a liability waiver\,&nbsp\;prior to participation
 .<br><br>Questions? Contact&nbsp\;<a href="mailto:gail.morell@gmail.com">Ga
 il Morell</a>.<u></u><u></u></html-blob>
