BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Bicycle Club
DTSTART:20200823T210000Z
DTEND:20200824T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:12f6di60nj1olkaf66l50ung7f@google.com
CREATED:20200810T135355Z
DESCRIPTION:<p>Mark your calendar\, you're invited to the&nbsp\;2020 Bloomi
 ngton Bicycle Club Summer Social!</p><p><b>When:</b>&nbsp\;Sunday\, August 
 23&nbsp\;@ 5 PM</p><p><b>Where:</b><b>Bryant Creek Shelter House&nbsp\;@ Mo
 rgan-Monroe State Forest</b></p><p>(Thisis the shelter located nearest the 
 Forest Entrance from Old SR 37 on Bryant CreekLane.)</p><p>&nbsp\;</p><p><b
 >Note:</b>&nbsp\;Bring your own food and drink and spend some time&nbsp\;wi
 th your cycling friends!</p><p>&nbsp\;As you know\, the club hosts a summer
  picnic every year.&nbsp\; Traditionally\, the club&nbsp\;would provide&nbs
 p\;burgers\, brats\, and hotdogs and folks&nbsp\;were&nbsp\;asked to bring 
 a side dish or dessert to share.&nbsp\;&nbsp\;This year however\,&nbsp\;COV
 ID&nbsp\;concerns have forced us to reconsider this tradition&nbsp\;so we a
 sk that you&nbsp\;bring&nbsp\;your&nbsp\;own food and drink.</p><p>&nbsp\;T
 he<b>Bryant Creek Shelter House</b>&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&nbsp\;was reserved&nbsp\;
 after considering the&nbsp\;latest Public Health Order from the Monroe Coun
 ty Health Department\,&nbsp\;available <a href="https://bloomington.in.gov/
 sites/default/files/2020-08/Executive%20Order%2020-03_1.pdf" id="ow384" __i
 s_owner="true">Here&nbsp\; </a>. &nbsp\;Based on this order\, face covering
 s are mandatory in outdoor spaces when adequate physical distancing is not 
 possible.&nbsp\; The&nbsp\;<b>Bryant Creek Shelter House</b>&nbsp\;&nbsp\;&
 nbsp\;is a large\, open\, outdoor space that will accommodate up to 72 occu
 pants.&nbsp\; There is also plenty of surrounding park space if we're unabl
 e to maintain social distancing practices within the shelter.&nbsp\; Nevert
 heless\, we ask that you wear a face covering unless actively engaged in ea
 ting and drinking.</p><p>&nbsp\;As always\, we continue to monitor the&nbsp
 \;very fluid&nbsp\;situation&nbsp\;and&nbsp\;follow federal\, state\, and l
 ocal guidance.&nbsp\; At present\, we believe this event&nbsp\;can be respo
 nsibly managed&nbsp\;with the&nbsp\;aforementioned&nbsp\;measures&nbsp\;in 
 place.&nbsp\; If the situation changes however\, I'll send another notice t
 o cancel the event.</p><p>&nbsp\;As with all BBC events\, I ask for your co
 operation with the following guidance:</p><p>1. DO NOT attend any BBC event
  (be it a group ride or social)\, if you suspect you may be getting sick</p
 ><p>2. DO NOT attend any BBC event when you live with someone who is sick</
 p><p>3. DO NOT attend any BBC event if you\, someone you live with\, or a c
 lose contact\, is waiting on COVID test results</p><p>Take care\, I look fo
 rward to seeing you at the social!</p><p>&nbsp\;Matt Summers</p><p>BBC Pres
 ident</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20200821T221842Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:BBC Summer Social
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
