DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:3rgauj7p3j1m03gakn7lsr5bc7@google.com
CREATED:20220828T161826Z
DESCRIPTION:<u></u><u></u><u></u><p><a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=h
 ttps://bloomingtonbicycleclub.org/maps/Gravel_Rides/Ten_O-Clock_and_Lime_Ki
 ln_16.pdf&amp\;sa=D&amp\;source=calendar&amp\;usd=2&amp\;usg=AOvVaw2NYNziUz
 xUKRfPzU_CA1nI" target="_blank">Ten O&#39\;Clock Line and Lime Kiln 16</a><
 br></p><p><a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://ridewithgps.com/rou
 tes/40722910&amp\;sa=D&amp\;source=calendar&amp\;usd=2&amp\;usg=AOvVaw1Bnh4
 OXerR6QVzm_fERlxc" target="_blank">GPS Files</a><br></p><p>Ride starts at t
 he Upper Handicapped Hunter Parking Lot on Crooked Creek Road.  We take Mil
 ler Ridge and the Ten O&#39\;Clock Line Trail to Brown County State Park an
 d do the Lime Kiln trail loop counterclockwise.  Route is suitable for MTB 
 or gravel bike\, but you may be more comfortable on the MTB.</p><p>These ri
 des feature gravel roads\, single and double track trails\,  and just enoug
 h pavement to string the aforementioned together into fun\, woodsy adventur
 e loops.  Rides begin at 6PM through the Fall and Winter months as weather 
 allows and typically last about two hours.  Lights are mandatory as we ente
 r the Fall and Winter seasons.</p><p>Routes are suitable for mountain bike 
 or gravel bike\, with some more turned to one or the other.  Rides begin at
  different locations\, primarily associated with Yellowwood State Forest\, 
 Brown County State Park\, and the Hoosier National Forest in Monroe\, Lawre
 nce\, and Brown Counties.  Specific routes may be dictated by weather condi
 tions\, but starting locations\, route maps\, and gps file links will be po
 sted here in advance.</p><p>Expect a lot of trees and few cars.  </p><u></u
 ><u></u><u></u>
LAST-MODIFIED:20220828T161826Z
LOCATION:39.135507\, -86.300870
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Off Road Adventure Ride - Ten O'Clock Line and Lime Kiln 16
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
