DESCRIPTION:<a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/30873539">Up Koontz and
  Back Ison</a> 25 miles<br><br>Watch the calendar for weather-related updat
 es and for future morning rides.<br><br><i>Please observe social distancing
  norms as we gather and ride. We plan no formal leader. EVERYONE is a leade
 r. Familiarize yourself with the ride before heading out. We will ride in s
 mall groups. People in the last group will endeavor to sweep the route and 
 assist others as needed.</i><br><ul><li>Be SAFE. Don't blow through stop si
 gns. Consider bike lights.<br></li><li>Be COURTEOUS: Single up in traffic<b
 r></li><li>Be PREDICTABLE: Signal your intentions to cars and fellow riders
 .</li></ul>This branch of the OWLS training group also emphasizes somewhat 
 slower\, moderate rides\, and a route planned in advance that is posted on 
 the ride calendar. This is a no drop ride\, but not a beginner's ride. Expe
 ct an overall average moving speed 11 - 15 mph including hills. Distances v
 ary from 20 to 30 miles. Early season rides will be somewhat shorter and sl
 ower. Rides depart promptly at 8:30am.<br><br>Non-members should sign up fo
 r a <a href="https://secure.getmeregistered.com/get_information.php?event_i
 d=133776">free trial membership</a>\, good for up to three rides\, and whic
 h includes electronically signing a liability waiver\,&nbsp\;prior to parti
 cipation.<br><br>Questions? Contact <a href="mailto:allan.edmonds@gmail.com
 ">Allan Edmonds</a>
