DESCRIPTION:<p><a href="https://bloomingtonbicycleclub.org/maps/John_Basset
 t_Maps/Waterworks_Plus_a_Hill_20.pdf">Waterworks Plus a Hill 20</a><br></p>
 <p><a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/6360172">GPS Files</a></p><p>The
  iRide is a no-drop Intermediate level ride of moderate pace and distance w
 ith regrouping points.&nbsp\; Pace is anticipated to be 15-17 mph.<br></p><
 p>The tRide is an advanced level ride of high pace and moderate distance th
 at may or may not include regrouping points. &nbsp\;Pace is anticipated to 
 be 18+ mph. Expect occasional sprint or Strava segments\, pace line riding 
 at high speed\, intervals\, and fewer regrouping stops.</p><p>The iRide and
  tRide will start at the same place and will ride the same scheduled route\
 , but the start of these two groups will be staggered with the tRide starti
 ng first at 5:45 and the iRide just behind them. Mileages will increase as 
 the season progresses.&nbsp\; </p><p>Riders are expected to look out for ea
 ch other during the rides.&nbsp\; Ride maps and GPS links will be posted he
 re in advance. Riders unfamiliar with the route should bring along a copy o
 f the map.</p>Non-members should sign up for a&nbsp\;<a href="https://secur
 e.getmeregistered.com/get_information.php?event_id=133776">free trial membe
 rship</a>\, good for up to three rides\, and which includes electronically 
 signing a liability waiver\,&nbsp\;prior to participation.
