DESCRIPTION:<a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/30818351">Leonard Sprin
 gs and Duvall/Koontz</a> 25 miles<br><br>Watch the calendar for weather-rel
 ated updates and for future morning rides.<br><br><i>Please observe social 
 distancing norms as we gather and ride. We plan no formal leader. EVERYONE 
 is a leader. Familiarize yourself with the ride before heading out. We will
  ride in small groups. People in the last group will endeavor to sweep the 
 route and assist others as needed.</i><br><ul><li>Be SAFE. Don't blow throu
 gh stop signs. Consider bike lights.<br></li><li>Be COURTEOUS: Single up in
  traffic<br></li><li>Be PREDICTABLE: Signal your intentions to cars and fel
 low riders.</li></ul>This branch of the OWLS training group also emphasizes
  somewhat slower\, moderate rides\, and a route planned in advance that is 
 posted on the ride calendar. This is a no drop ride\, but not a beginner's 
 ride. Expect an overall average moving speed 11 - 15 mph including hills. D
 istances vary from 20 to 30 miles. Early season rides will be somewhat shor
 ter and slower. Rides depart promptly at 8:30am.<br><br>Non-members should 
 sign up for a <a href="https://secure.getmeregistered.com/get_information.p
 hp?event_id=133776">free trial membership</a>\, good for up to three rides\
 , and which includes electronically signing a liability waiver\,&nbsp\;prio
 r to participation.<br><br>Questions? Contact <a href="mailto:allan.edmonds
 @gmail.com">Allan Edmonds</a>
