 orms as we gather and ride. We plan no formal leader. EVERYONE is a leader.
  Familiarize yourself with the ride before heading out. We will ride in sma
 ll groups. People in the last group will endeavor to sweep the route and as
 sist others as needed.</i><br><ul><li>Be SAFE. Don't blow through stop sign
 s. Consider bike lights.<br></li><li>Be COURTEOUS: Single up in traffic<br>
 </li><li>Be PREDICTABLE: Signal your intentions to cars and fellow riders.<
 /li></ul>This branch of the OWLS training group also emphasizes somewhat sl
 ower\, moderate rides\, and a route planned in advance that is posted on th
 e ride calendar. This is a no drop ride\, but not a beginner's ride. Expect
  an overall average moving speed 11 - 15 mph including hills. Distances var
 y from 20 to 30 miles. Early season rides will be somewhat shorter and slow
 er. Rides depart promptly at 9:30am.<br><br>Non-members should sign up for 
 a <a href="https://secure.getmeregistered.com/get_information.php?event_id=
