CREATED:20220221T214100Z
DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u><u></u><u></u><a href="https://ridewithgps.co
 m/routes/39355434">https://ridewithgps.com/routes/39355434</a><br><br>Pleas
 e observe social distancing norms as we gather and ride.&nbsp\;<ul><li>Be S
 AFE. Don't blow through stop signs. Consider bike lights.<br></li><li>Be CO
 URTEOUS: Single up in traffic<br></li><li>Be PREDICTABLE: Signal your inten
 tions to cars and fellow riders.</li></ul>The "Older\, Wiser\, and a Little
  Slower" training group emphasizes moderate rides\, and a route planned in 
 advance that is posted on the ride calendar. This is a no drop ride\, but n
 ot a beginner's ride.&nbsp\;The OWLS group welcomes a wide range of interme
 diate riders\, and typically breaks off into a faster and slower group with
  the former averaging an overall moving speed of 16-18 mph\, and the slower
  group averaging 13-15 mph (including hills).&nbsp\; Distances vary from 20
  to 30 miles\, depending partly on available light. Early season rides will
  be somewhat shorter and slower. Rides depart promptly at 5:45.<br><br>Non-
 members should sign up for a <a href="https://secure.getmeregistered.com/ge
 t_information.php?event_id=136627">free trial membership</a>\, good for up 
 to three rides\, and which includes electronically signing a liability waiv
 er\,&nbsp\;prior to participation.<br><br>Questions? Contact&nbsp\;<a href=
 "mailto:gail.morell@gmail.com">Gail Morell</a>.<u></u><u></u><u></u></html-
 blob>
