DESCRIPTION:Watch the calendar for weather-related updates and for future r
 ides. Rides will switch to morning times as the weather warms.<br><br><i>Pl
 ease observe social distancing norms as we gather and ride. We plan no form
 al leader. EVERYONE is a leader. Familiarize yourself with the ride before 
 heading out. We will ride in small groups. People in the last group will en
 deavor to sweep the route and assist others as needed.</i><ul><li>Be SAFE. 
 Don't blow through stop signs. Consider bike lights.<br></li><li>Be COURTEO
 US: Single up in traffic<br></li><li>Be PREDICTABLE: Signal your intentions
  to cars and fellow riders.</li></ul>This branch of the OWLS training group
  also emphasizes somewhat slower\, moderate rides\, and a route planned in 
 advance that is posted on the ride calendar. This is a no drop ride\, but n
 ot a beginner's ride. Expect an overall average moving speed 11 - 15 mph in
 cluding hills. Distances vary from 20 to 30 miles. Early season rides will 
 be somewhat shorter and slower. Rides depart promptly at 1:30pm.<br><br>Non
 -members should sign up for a <a href="https://secure.getmeregistered.com/g
 et_information.php?event_id=133776">free trial membership</a>\, good for up
  to three rides\, and which includes electronically signing a liability wai
 ver\,&nbsp\;prior to participation.<br><br>Questions? Contact <a href="mail
 to:allan.edmonds@gmail.com">Allan Edmonds</a>
