 up in traffic<br></li><li>Be PREDICTABLE: Signal your intentions to cars an
 d fellow riders.</li></ul>The "Older\, Wiser\, and a Little Slower" trainin
 g group emphasizes moderate rides\, and a route planned in advance that is 
 posted on the ride calendar. This is a no drop ride\, but not a beginner's 
 ride. The OWLS often average 15 to 19 mph on flat roads\, and typically hav
 e an overall average moving speed between 12 and 15 mph including hills. Di
 stances vary from 20 to 30 miles\, depending partly on available light. Ear
 ly season rides will be somewhat shorter and slower. Rides depart promptly 
 at 5:45.<br><br>Non-members will be required to sign a <a href="https://dri
 ve.google.com/file/d/1jDxK92FPgpyvj2cCT7vV2S8RZTWDR_RH/view" target="_blank
