DESCRIPTION:<a href="http://www.bloomingtonbicycleclub.org/maps/BBCMaps/map
 _pack_1/nashville_90.pdf">Nashville 90</a><br><br><a href="https://ridewith
 gps.com/routes/4608332">GPS Files</a><br><br><b>NOTE:&nbsp\; As of July 4 t
 here is a bridge closure on SR58&nbsp\;</b><b>about route mile 34 and j</b>
 <b>ust east of Kurtz.&nbsp\; There are Road Closed signs at the SR135 / SR5
 8 intersection.&nbsp\; The bridge may be competed by July 10\, but is walka
 ble in its current state.&nbsp\; There is no planned detour at this time.</
 b><br><br>This one has become the iconic club ride.&nbsp\; At 90 miles\, an
 d rated difficult\, this "almost" century incorporates the best of what thi
 s area has to offer cyclists - big climbs\, rolling hills\, curves\, flats\
 , buccolic views\, bizarre town names (Zelma) and sites (the Stonehead). Ri
 de this once and you'll ride it again !<br><br>There is a lot of newish pav
 ement.&nbsp\; SR 446\, SR58\, and SR135 have all been redone since last yea
 r.&nbsp\;<br><br>Non-members should sign up for a <a href="https://secure.g
 etmeregistered.com/get_information.php?event_id=133776">free trial membersh
 ip</a>\, good for up to three rides\, and which includes electronically sig
 ning a liability waiver\,&nbsp\;prior to participation.&nbsp\;&nbsp\;
LAST-MODIFIED:20220614T150547Z
LOCATION:Bryan Park Pool Parking Lot @ 39.15435\,-86.523
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Nashville 90  Ride - Leaders:  TBD
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
