DESCRIPTION:Description:<a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/34791207">K
 arst Greenway</a> 22 miles. Probably we'll do a shorter ride\, given the co
 ld weather.&nbsp\;<br><br>Watch the calendar for weather-related updates an
 d for future morning rides.<br><br><i>Please observe social distancing norm
 s as we gather and ride. We plan no formal leader. EVERYONE is a leader. Fa
 miliarize yourself with the ride before heading out. We will ride in small 
 groups. People in the last group will endeavor to sweep the route and assis
 t others as needed.</i><br><ul><li>Be SAFE. Don't blow through stop signs. 
 Consider bike lights.<br></li><li>Be COURTEOUS: Single up in traffic<br></l
 i><li>Be PREDICTABLE: Signal your intentions to cars and fellow riders.</li
 ></ul>This branch of the OWLS training group also emphasizes somewhat slowe
 r\, moderate rides\, and a route planned in advance that is posted on the r
 ide calendar. This is a no drop ride\, but not a beginner's ride. Expect an
  overall average moving speed 11 - 15 mph including hills. Distances vary f
 rom 20 to 30 miles. Early season rides will be somewhat shorter and slower.
  Rides depart promptly at 9:30am.<br><br>Non-members should sign up for a <
 a href="https://secure.getmeregistered.com/get_information.php?event_id=133
 776">free trial membership</a>\, good for up to three rides\, and which inc
 ludes electronically signing a liability waiver\,&nbsp\;prior to participat
 ion.<br><br>Questions? Contact <a href="mailto:allan.edmonds@gmail.com">All
 an Edmonds</a>
