 rmal leader. EVERYONE is a leader. Familiarize yourself with the ride befor
 e heading out. We will ride in small groups. People in the last group will 
 endeavor to sweep the route and assist others as needed.</i><ul><li>Be SAFE
 . Don't blow through stop signs. Consider bike lights.<br></li><li>Be COURT
 EOUS: Single up in traffic<br></li><li>Be PREDICTABLE: Signal your intentio
 ns to cars and fellow riders.</li></ul>This branch of the OWLS training gro
 up also emphasizes somewhat slower\, moderate rides\, and a route planned i
 n advance that is posted on the ride calendar. This is a no drop ride\, but
  not a beginner's ride. Expect an overall average moving speed 11 - 15 mph 
 including hills. Distances vary from 20 to 30 miles. Early season rides wil
 l be somewhat shorter and slower. Rides depart promptly at 9:30am.<br><br>N
 on-members should sign up for a <a href="https://secure.getmeregistered.com
 /get_information.php?event_id=133776">free trial membership</a>\, good for 
 up to three rides\, and which includes electronically signing a liability w
 aiver\,&nbsp\;prior to participation.<br><br>Questions? Contact <a href="ma
 ilto:allan.edmonds@gmail.com">Allan Edmonds</a>
