DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u><u></u><u></u><a href="https://ridewithgps.co
 m/routes/37555570" id="ow1519" __is_owner="true">https://ridewithgps.com/ro
 utes/37555570</a></html-blob><br><html-blob><br>Please observe social dista
 ncing norms as we gather and ride.&nbsp\;<ul><li>Be SAFE. Don't blow throug
 h stop signs. Consider bike lights.<br></li><li>Be COURTEOUS: Single up in 
 traffic<br></li><li>Be PREDICTABLE: Signal your intentions to cars and fell
 ow riders.</li></ul>The "Older\, Wiser\, and a Little Slower" training grou
 p emphasizes moderate rides\, and a route planned in advance that is posted
  on the ride calendar. This is a no drop ride\, but not a beginner's ride.T
 he OWLS group welcomes a wide range of intermediate riders\, and typically 
 breaks off into a faster and slower group with the former averaging an over
 all moving speed of 16-18 mph\, and the slower group averaging 13-15 mph (i
 ncluding hills).&nbsp\;Distances vary from 20 to 30 miles\, depending partl
 y on available light. Early season rides will be somewhat shorter and slowe
 r. Rides depart promptly at 5:45.<br><br>Non-members should sign up for a <
 a href="https://secure.getmeregistered.com/get_information.php?event_id=136
 627">free trial membership</a>\, good for up to three rides\, and which inc
 ludes electronically signing a liability waiver\,&nbsp\;prior to participat
 ion.<br><br>Questions? Contact&nbsp\;<a href="mailto:gail.morell@gmail.com"
 >Gail Morell</a>.<u></u><u></u><u></u></html-blob>
LAST-MODIFIED:20220828T234237Z
