DESCRIPTION:<a href="http://bloomingtonbicycleclub.org/maps/John_Bassett_Ma
 ps/The_Wineries_Ride_2019_Ver_46.pdf">The Wineries Ride 2019 Ver 46</a><br>
 <br><a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/29730807">GPS Files</a><br><br>
 This route is sort of known for Wineries\, but mainly known for hills.  You
  get a good dose of Lake Lemon and some nice country roads in the northwest
  part of the county.<br><br>With the completion of the Sample Road intercha
 nge on I-69 we can again do this route approximately as it was originally d
 esigned.&nbsp\; From Oliver Winery we will follow the new I-69 access road 
 (actually the old highway) north to Fox Hollow Road\, and resume the tradit
 ional Wineries route at Anderson Road.&nbsp\; The whole thing is about 46 m
 iles\;&nbsp\; come join in the fun!!<br><br>Non-members should sign up for 
 a <a href="https://secure.getmeregistered.com/get_information.php?event_id=
 133776">free trial membership</a>\, good for up to three rides\, and which 
 includes electronically signing a liability waiver\,&nbsp\;prior to partici
 pation.&nbsp\;&nbsp\;<br><br><a><br></a>
LAST-MODIFIED:20210503T163916Z
LOCATION:Bryan Park Pool Parking Lot @ 39.15435\,-86.523
