DESCRIPTION:<br><br>Please observe social distancing norms as we gather and
  ride.&nbsp\;<ul><li>Be SAFE. Don't blow through stop signs. Consider bike 
 lights.<br></li><li>Be COURTEOUS: Single up in traffic<br></li><li>Be PREDI
 CTABLE: Signal your intentions to cars and fellow riders.</li></ul>The "Old
 er\, Wiser\, and a Little Slower" training group emphasizes moderate rides\
 , and a route planned in advance that is posted on the ride calendar. This 
 is a no drop ride\, but not a beginner's ride. The OWLS often average 15 to
  19 mph on flat roads\, and typically have an overall average moving speed 
 between 12 and 15 mph including hills. Distances vary from 20 to 30 miles\,
  depending partly on available light. Early season rides will be somewhat s
 horter and slower. Rides depart promptly at 5:45.<br><br>Non-members should
  sign up for a <a href="https://secure.getmeregistered.com/get_information.
 php?event_id=133776">free trial membership</a>\, good for up to three rides
 \, and which includes electronically signing a liability waiver\,&nbsp\;pri
 or to participation.<br><br>Questions? Contact&nbsp\;<a href="mailto:gail.m
 orell@gmail.com">Gail Morell</a>.
