CREATED:20220519T162753Z
DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u><p><a href="https://bloomingtonbicycleclub.or
 g/maps/John_Bassett_Maps/Joes_Cemetery_Ride_74.pdf">Joe's Cemetery Ride 74<
 /a></p><p><a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/40876564" id="ow424" __is
 _owner="true">GPS Files</a><br></p><p>On this the twentieth anniversary of 
 9/11\, the BBC offers a special memorial ride that honors the three thousan
 d souls that perished that day. It also honors the seven thousand service m
 embers who have been killed in the Iraq and Afghanistan wars. </p><p>Last y
 ear this ride was the CIBA Cemetery Tour\, and was a drive and ride from Ma
 rtinsville. This year’s version leaves from Bryan Park. While the new route
  bypasses several of the thirteen cemeteries\, it does incorporate the “Cry
 baby Bridge”.&nbsp\; It eliminates all of last year’s fresh chip and seal r
 oads and replaces them with many miles of glass smooth\, freshly paved blac
 ktop\, and a new crossing of I-69 north of Martinsville.</p><p>Services are
  available at miles 28 and 50 of the route.</p><p>Non-members should sign u
 p for a <a href="https://secure.getmeregistered.com/get_information.php?eve
 nt_id=136627">free trial membership</a>\, good for up to three rides\, and 
 which includes electronically signing a liability waiver\,&nbsp\;prior to p
 articipation.&nbsp\;&nbsp\;<br></p><u></u></html-blob>
