UID:55e33nrsjgiudmcq81qdav5i27@google.com
CREATED:20220518T152243Z
DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u>This is a beautiful ride with challenging hil
 ls down to the historic Williams Covered Bridge on the East Fork White Rive
 r.&nbsp\; The traditional route is here:<br><br><a href="http://www.bloomin
 gtonbicycleclub.org/maps/BBCMaps/map_pack_1/williams_bridge.pdf">Williams C
 overed Bridge</a><br><br>Recently\, we have utilized an alternate route to 
 Williams following the&nbsp\;Milwaukee Trail (a neat\, privately-built ston
 e dust rail trail)&nbsp\; southwest from Bedford to Williams\, and an alter
 nate route back to Fayetteville from Williams on Ridge Road.&nbsp\; We thro
 w in another rail trail (the new Limestone Trail) connecting Dillman Road a
 nd Church Lane near the end of the ride.&nbsp\; The complete route for Satu
 rday is here:&nbsp\;<br><br><a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/3101595
 1" id="ow673" __is_owner="true">GPS File</a><br><br>The complete Milwaukee 
 Trail from Bedford to Williams is about 10 miles.&nbsp\; The trail is a lit
 tle shorter than the road route to Williams\, and is substantially less hil
 ly.&nbsp\; It is a little slower due to the the crushed stone surface\, but
  presents little problem for a normal road bike.&nbsp\;<br><br>Of course\, 
 you can always opt to do the traditional route via road from Bedford to Wil
 liams\, and skip the Milwaukee Trail.&nbsp\; We just all meet at the covere
 d bridge!<u></u><br><u></u><br><u></u><br><u></u>Non-members should sign up
  for a <a href="https://secure.getmeregistered.com/get_information.php?even
 t_id=136627"><u>free trial membership</u></a>\, good for up to three rides\
 , and which includes electronically signing a liability waiver\,&nbsp\;prio
 r to participation.&nbsp\;<br><u></u></html-blob>
LAST-MODIFIED:20220603T014232Z
LOCATION:Bryan Park Pool Parking Lot @ 39.15435\,-86.523
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Williams Covered Bridge with Rail Trails 72 - Jim Powers
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
