 ingle up in traffic<br></li><li>Be PREDICTABLE: Signal your intentions to c
 ars and fellow riders.</li></ul>The "Older\, Wiser\, and a Little Slower" t
 raining group emphasizes moderate rides\, and a route planned in advance th
 at is posted on the ride calendar. This is a no drop ride\, but not a begin
 ner's ride. The OWLS often average 15 to 19 mph on flat roads\, and typical
 ly have an overall average moving speed between 12 and 15 mph including hil
 ls. Distances vary from 20 to 30 miles\, depending partly on available ligh
 t. Early season rides will be somewhat shorter and slower. Rides depart pro
 mptly at 5:45.<br><br>Non-members will be required to sign a <a href="https
 ://drive.google.com/file/d/1jDxK92FPgpyvj2cCT7vV2S8RZTWDR_RH/view" target="
