BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Bicycle Club
DTSTART:20210605T130000Z
DTEND:20210605T190000Z
DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:2o0k8jfkcrdchdft1q0chk4vud@google.com
CREATED:20190903T013202Z
DESCRIPTION:This is a beautiful ride with challenging hills down to the his
 toric Williams Covered Bridge on the East Fork White River.&nbsp\; The trad
 itional route is here:<br><br><a href="http://www.bloomingtonbicycleclub.or
 g/maps/BBCMaps/map_pack_1/williams_bridge.pdf">Williams Covered Bridge</a><
 br><br>Recently\, we have utilized an alternate route to Williams following
  the&nbsp\;Milwaukee Trail (a neat\, privately-built stone dust rail trail)
 &nbsp\; southwest from Bedford to Williams\, and an alternate route back to
  Fayetteville from Williams on Ridge Road.&nbsp\; We throw in another rail 
 trail (the new Limestone Trail) connecting Dillman Road and Church Lane nea
 r the end of the ride.&nbsp\; The complete route for Saturday is here:&nbsp
 \;<br><br><a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/31015951">Williams Covere
 d Bridge with Rail Trails 72</a><br><br>The complete Milwaukee Trail from B
 edford to Williams is about 10 miles.&nbsp\; The trail is a little shorter 
 than the road route to Williams\, and is substantially less hilly.&nbsp\; I
 t is a little slower due to the the crushed stone surface\, but presents li
 ttle problem for a normal road bike.&nbsp\;<br><br>Of course\, you can alwa
 ys opt to do the traditional route via road from Bedford to Williams\, and 
 skip the Milwaukee Trail.&nbsp\; We just all meet at the covered bridge!
LAST-MODIFIED:20210516T230312Z
LOCATION:Bryan Park Pool Parking Lot @ 39.15435\,-86.523
SEQUENCE:2
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Williams Covered Bridge with Rail Trails 72 - Leader: TBD
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
