DTSTART:20220220T170000Z
DTEND:20220220T220000Z
DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:16v4079lqnm3pp4iemjteo28j4@google.com
CREATED:20220217T214524Z
DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><b><br></b>&nbsp\;<br>Join in for a fun Brown County
  gravel ride starting and ending at Hard Truth in Nashville.&nbsp\; This is
  a loop ride borrowed from Jeff Fetterer and has its fair share of ups and 
 downs.&nbsp\; With the exception of Covered Bridge Road the clockwise loop 
 generally goes down the steep grades and up the gentler grades.&nbsp\; Get 
 to near the top of Bear Wallow Hill without ever being on Bear Wallow Hill 
 Road. And\, finish up with a great gravel decent on Wallow Hollow.<br><br>R
 oute is entirely gravel and pavement&nbsp\;- no trail.&nbsp\;<br><br>Shorte
 r options are possible&nbsp\;<br><br><b>No formal car pooling will be offer
 ed</b><br><br><a href="https://bloomingtonbicycleclub.org/maps/Gravel_Rides
 /Jeff-s_Salmeron_-_Wallow_Hollow_Loop_from_Hard_Truth_29.pdf">PDF Map and Q
 ueue Sheet</a><br><br><a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/38585376" id=
 "ow798" __is_owner="true">GPS Files</a></html-blob>
LAST-MODIFIED:20220217T214731Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Jeff's Salmeron / Wallow Hollow Loop from Hard Truth 29man 
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
