 ="ow771" __is_owner="true">https://ridewithgps.com/routes/37164807</a></htm
 l-blob><br><html-blob><br><br>Please observe social distancing norms as we 
 gather and ride.&nbsp\;<ul><li>Be SAFE. Don't blow through stop signs. Cons
 ider bike lights.<br></li><li>Be COURTEOUS: Single up in traffic<br></li><l
 i>Be PREDICTABLE: Signal your intentions to cars and fellow riders.</li></u
 l>The "Older\, Wiser\, and a Little Slower" training group emphasizes moder
 ate rides\, and a route planned in advance that is posted on the ride calen
 dar. This is a no drop ride\, but not a beginner's ride.The OWLS group welc
 omes a wide range of intermediate riders\, and typically breaks off into a 
 faster and slower group with the former averaging an overall moving speed o
 f 16-18 mph\, and the slower group averaging 13-15 mph (including hills).&n
 bsp\;Distances vary from 20 to 30 miles\, depending partly on available lig
 ht. Early season rides will be somewhat shorter and slower. Rides depart pr
 omptly at 5:45.<br><br>Non-members should sign up for a <a href="https://se
 cure.getmeregistered.com/get_information.php?event_id=136627">free trial me
 mbership</a>\, good for up to three rides\, and which includes electronical
 ly signing a liability waiver\,&nbsp\;prior to participation.<br><br>Questi
 ons? Contact&nbsp\;<a href="mailto:gail.morell@gmail.com">Gail Morell</a>.<
 u></u><u></u><u></u></html-blob>
