DESCRIPTION:<a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/28617991" id="ow3526" _
 _is_owner="true">Lampkins Ridge to Brewsters</a>&nbsp\;14 miles<br>LAST OWL
 S EVENING RIDE FOR THE YEAR<br><br>Please observe social distancing norms a
 s we gather and ride. We plan no formal leader. EVERYONE is a leader. Famil
 iarize yourself with the ride before heading out. We will ride in small gro
 ups.People in the last group will endeavor to sweep the route and assist ot
 hers as needed.<br><ul><li>Be SAFE. Don't blow through stop signs. Consider
  bike lights.<br></li><li>Be COURTEOUS: Single up in traffic<br></li><li>Be
  PREDICTABLE: Signal your intentions to cars and fellow riders.</li></ul>Th
 e "Older\, Wiser\, and a Little Slower" training group emphasizes moderate 
 rides\, and a route planned in advance that is posted on the ride calendar.
  This is a no drop ride\, but not a beginner's ride. The OWLS often average
  15 to 19 mph on flat roads\, and typically have an overall average moving 
 speed between 12 and 15 mph including hills. Distances vary from 20 to 30 m
 iles\, depending partly on available light. Early season rides will be some
 what shorter and slower. Rides depart promptly at 5:45.<br><br>Non-members 
 should sign up for a <a href="https://secure.getmeregistered.com/get_inform
 ation.php?event_id=133776">free trial membership</a>\, good for up to three
  rides\, and which includes electronically signing a liability waiver\,&nbs
 p\;prior to participation.<br><br>Questions? Contact <a href="mailto:allan.
 edmonds@gmail.com">Allan Edmonds</a> or <a href="mailto:gail.morell@gmail.c
 om">Gail Morell</a>
