DESCRIPTION:<a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/33346254">Triple Creek<
 /a> 26 miles<br><br>Watch the calendar for weather-related updates and for 
 future morning rides.<br><br><i>Please observe social distancing norms as w
 e gather and ride. We plan no formal leader. EVERYONE is a leader. Familiar
 ize yourself with the ride before heading out. We will ride in small groups
 . People in the last group will endeavor to sweep the route and assist othe
 rs as needed.</i><br><ul><li>Be SAFE. Don't blow through stop signs. Consid
 er bike lights.<br></li><li>Be COURTEOUS: Single up in traffic<br></li><li>
 Be PREDICTABLE: Signal your intentions to cars and fellow riders.</li></ul>
 This branch of the OWLS training group also emphasizes somewhat slower\, mo
 derate rides\, and a route planned in advance that is posted on the ride ca
 lendar. This is a no drop ride\, but not a beginner's ride. Expect an overa
 ll average moving speed 11 - 15 mph including hills. Distances vary from 20
  to 30 miles. Early season rides will be somewhat shorter and slower. Rides
  depart promptly at 8:30am.<br><br>Non-members should sign up for a <a href
 ="https://secure.getmeregistered.com/get_information.php?event_id=133776">f
 ree trial membership</a>\, good for up to three rides\, and which includes 
 electronically signing a liability waiver\,&nbsp\;prior to participation.<b
 r><br>Questions? Contact <a href="mailto:allan.edmonds@gmail.com">Allan Edm
 onds</a>
