 will ride in small groups.People in the last group will endeavor to sweep t
 he route and assist others as needed.<br><ul><li>Be SAFE. Don't blow throug
 h stop signs. Consider bike lights.<br></li><li>Be COURTEOUS: Single up in 
 traffic<br></li><li>Be PREDICTABLE: Signal your intentions to cars and fell
 ow riders.</li></ul>The "Older\, Wiser\, and a Little Slower" training grou
 p emphasizes moderate rides\, and a route planned in advance that is posted
  on the ride calendar. This is a no drop ride\, but not a beginner's ride. 
 The OWLS often average 15 to 19 mph on flat roads\, and typically have an o
 verall average moving speed between 12 and 15 mph including hills. Distance
 s vary from 20 to 30 miles\, depending partly on available light. Early sea
 son rides will be somewhat shorter and slower. Rides depart promptly at 5:4
 5.<br><br>Non-members should sign up for a <a href="https://secure.getmereg
 istered.com/get_information.php?event_id=133776">free trial membership</a>\
 , good for up to three rides\, and which includes electronically signing a 
