BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Bicycle Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20200804T174500
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20200804T194500
DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:15rm2p5r1cldsblb0bmpeaofq5_R20200721T214500@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20200804T174500
CREATED:20200525T122037Z
DESCRIPTION:<p><a href="https://bloomingtonbicycleclub.org/maps/iRides/Ramp
 _It_Up_2017_Version_30.pdf">Ramp It Up 2017 Version 30</a><br></p><p><a hre
 f="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/21187951" id="ow581" __is_owner="true">GP
 S Files</a><br></p><p>The iRide is a no-drop Intermediate level ride of mod
 erate pace and distance with regrouping points.&nbsp\; Pace is anticipated 
 to be 15-17 mph.</p><p>The tRide is an advanced level ride of high pace and
  moderate distance that may or may not include regrouping points. &nbsp\;Pa
 ce is anticipated to be 18+ mph. Expect occasional sprint or Strava segment
 s\, pace line riding at high speed\, intervals\, and fewer regrouping stops
 .</p><p>The iRide and tRide will start at the same place and will ride the 
 same scheduled route\, but the start of these two groups will be staggered 
 with the tRide starting first at 5:45 and the iRide just behind them. Milea
 ges will increase as the season progresses.&nbsp\; </p><p>Riders are expect
 ed to look out for each other during the rides.&nbsp\; Ride maps and GPS li
 nks will be posted here in advance. Riders unfamiliar with the route should
  bring along a copy of the map.</p>Non-members should sign up for a&nbsp\;<
 a href="https://secure.getmeregistered.com/get_information.php?event_id=133
 776">free trial membership</a>\, good for up to three rides\, and which inc
 ludes electronically signing a liability waiver\,&nbsp\;prior to participat
 ion.<br><br>&nbsp\;<br><br>&nbsp\;&nbsp\;
LAST-MODIFIED:20200803T172334Z
LOCATION:Bryan Park Pool Parking Lot @ 39.15435\,-86.523\, 
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:iRide / tRide - Ramp It Up 2017 Version 30
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Bicycle Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20200714T174500
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20200714T194500
DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:9p45m8hkqk5cb1cv973v44b00o@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20200714T174500
CREATED:20200302T150145Z
DESCRIPTION:<a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/30161829" id="ow371" __
 is_owner="true">Long Leonard Springs</a> 26 miles<br><br>Please observe soc
 ial distancing norms as we gather and ride. We plan no formal leader. EVERY
 ONE is a leader. Familiarize yourself with the ride before heading out. We 
 will ride in small groups.People in the last group will endeavor to sweep t
 he route and assist others as needed.<br><ul><li>Be SAFE. Don't blow throug
 h stop signs. Consider bike lights.<br></li><li>Be COURTEOUS: Single up in 
 traffic<br></li><li>Be PREDICTABLE: Signal your intentions to cars and fell
 ow riders.</li></ul>The "Older\, Wiser\, and a Little Slower" training grou
 p emphasizes moderate rides\, and a route planned in advance that is posted
  on the ride calendar. This is a no drop ride\, but not a beginner's ride. 
 The OWLS often average 15 to 19 mph on flat roads\, and typically have an o
 verall average moving speed between 12 and 15 mph including hills. Distance
 s vary from 20 to 30 miles\, depending partly on available light. Early sea
 son rides will be somewhat shorter and slower. Rides depart promptly at 5:4
 5.<br><br>Non-members should sign up for a <a href="https://secure.getmereg
 istered.com/get_information.php?event_id=133776">free trial membership</a>\
 , good for up to three rides\, and which includes electronically signing a 
 liability waiver\,&nbsp\;prior to participation.<br><br>Questions? Contact 
 <a href="mailto:allan.edmonds@gmail.com">Allan Edmonds</a> or <a href="mail
 to:gail.morell@gmail.com">Gail Morell</a>
LAST-MODIFIED:20200713T233443Z
