 m/routes/22503400" id="ow380" __is_owner="true">https://ridewithgps.com/rou
 tes/22503400</a><br><br>Please observe social distancing norms as we gather
  and ride.&nbsp\;<ul><li>Be SAFE. Don't blow through stop signs. Consider b
 ike lights.<br></li><li>Be COURTEOUS: Single up in traffic<br></li><li>Be P
 REDICTABLE: Signal your intentions to cars and fellow riders.</li></ul>The 
 "Older\, Wiser\, and a Little Slower" training group emphasizes moderate ri
 des\, and a route planned in advance that is posted on the ride calendar. T
 his is a no drop ride\, but not a beginner's ride.The OWLS group welcomes a
  wide range of intermediate riders\, and typically breaks off into a faster
  and slower group with the former averaging an overall moving speed of 16-1
 8 mph\, and the slower group averaging 13-15 mph (including hills).&nbsp\;D
 istances vary from 20 to 30 miles\, depending partly on available light. Ea
 rly season rides will be somewhat shorter and slower. Rides depart promptly
  at 5:45.<br><br>Non-members should sign up for a <a href="https://secure.g
 etmeregistered.com/get_information.php?event_id=136627">free trial membersh
 ip</a>\, good for up to three rides\, and which includes electronically sig
 ning a liability waiver\,&nbsp\;prior to participation.<br><br>Questions? C
 ontact&nbsp\;<a href="mailto:gail.morell@gmail.com">Gail Morell</a>.<u></u>
