DESCRIPTION:<a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/33436383" id="ow419" __
 is_owner="true">Down the Dam Hill and Up Gore</a> 28 miles<br><br>Please ob
 serve social distancing norms as we gather and ride.&nbsp\;<ul><li>Be SAFE.
  Don't blow through stop signs. Consider bike lights.<br></li><li>Be COURTE
 OUS: Single up in traffic<br></li><li>Be PREDICTABLE: Signal your intention
 s to cars and fellow riders.</li></ul>The "Older\, Wiser\, and a Little Slo
 wer" training group emphasizes moderate rides\, and a route planned in adva
 nce that is posted on the ride calendar. This is a no drop ride\, but not a
  beginner's ride. The OWLS often average 15 to 19 mph on flat roads\, and t
 ypically have an overall average moving speed between 12 and 15 mph includi
 ng hills. Distances vary from 20 to 30 miles\, depending partly on availabl
 e light. Early season rides will be somewhat shorter and slower. Rides depa
 rt promptly at 5:45.<br><br>Non-members should sign up for a <a href="https
 ://secure.getmeregistered.com/get_information.php?event_id=133776">free tri
 al membership</a>\, good for up to three rides\, and which includes electro
 nically signing a liability waiver\,&nbsp\;prior to participation.<br><br>Q
 uestions? Contact&nbsp\;<a href="mailto:gail.morell@gmail.com">Gail Morell<
 /a>.
