DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><a href="http://bloomingtonbicycleclub.org/maps/John
 _Bassett_Maps/Spring%20Mill%20Leavenworth%2096%20revised.pdf">Spring Mill t
 o Leavenworth</a><br><br><a href="http://ridewithgps.com/routes/2970469">GP
 S Links</a><br><br>This is a drive and ride has been very well attended the
  last several years\, and&nbsp\;is back by by popular demand. The entire ro
 ute is 96 miles and begins and&nbsp\;ends at Spring Mill State Park.  Start
  there&nbsp\;because a century ride will get you to the Ohio&nbsp\;River an
 d back.  Shorter options include turning&nbsp\;back north at Marengo for a 
 63 mile loop\, or&nbsp\;turning right at the famous Crawford County&nbsp\;S
 hoe Tree for about 82 miles.  Tour some of&nbsp\;the best southern Indiana 
 has to offer\, and&nbsp\;enjoy the spectacular view of the Ohio River&nbsp\
 ;at the Leavenworth Overlook\, the point where&nbsp\;we turn back north.<br
 ><br>The first part of the ride is relatively flat with several miles of ne
 w pavement on SR 337\; the middle part is hilly\, and the last part is flat
  again on a lot of newish&nbsp\; pavement north of US 150.&nbsp\; See Lost 
 River\, Marengo\, the Blue River at Milltown\, the world famous Shoe Tree\,
  Wyandotte Cave\, the Leavenworth Overlook\, idyllic Amish countryside in O
 range County\, and the "Knob" you have to go right over the top of.&nbsp\;&
 nbsp\;<br><br>Meet&nbsp\;at Spring Mill State Park Inn (upper level of the 
 parking garage) at 8:00.&nbsp\; Bring your park pass.&nbsp\;This is a good 
 one.<br><br>Non-members should sign up for a <a href="https://secure.getmer
 egistered.com/get_information.php?event_id=136627" id="ow2036" __is_owner="
 true">free trial membership</a>\, good for up to three rides\, and which in
 cludes electronically signing a liability waiver\,&nbsp\;prior to participa
 tion.</html-blob>
LAST-MODIFIED:20220720T220001Z
LOCATION:Spring Mill Inn Parking Garage @38.734283\, -86.414433
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Spring Mill to Leavenworth 96 - Leader:  John Bassett
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
