DESCRIPTION:<a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/33286705" id="ow494" __
 is_owner="true">Fairfax Boat Ramp</a>&nbsp\;26 miles. Hope to get in on one
  or two DNR permits. Bring yours if you have one.<br><br>Watch the calendar
  for weather-related updates and for future morning rides.<br><br><i>Please
  observe social distancing norms as we gather and ride. We plan no formal l
 eader. EVERYONE is a leader. Familiarize yourself with the ride before head
 ing out. We will ride in small groups. People in the last group will endeav
 or to sweep the route and assist others as needed.</i><br><ul><li>Be SAFE. 
 Don't blow through stop signs. Consider bike lights.<br></li><li>Be COURTEO
 US: Single up in traffic<br></li><li>Be PREDICTABLE: Signal your intentions
  to cars and fellow riders.</li></ul>This branch of the OWLS training group
  also emphasizes somewhat slower\, moderate rides\, and a route planned in 
 advance that is posted on the ride calendar. This is a no drop ride\, but n
 ot a beginner's ride. Expect an overall average moving speed 11 - 15 mph in
 cluding hills. Distances vary from 20 to 30 miles. Early season rides will 
 be somewhat shorter and slower. Rides depart promptly at 8:30am.<br><br>Non
 -members should sign up for a <a href="https://secure.getmeregistered.com/g
 et_information.php?event_id=133776">free trial membership</a>\, good for up
  to three rides\, and which includes electronically signing a liability wai
 ver\,&nbsp\;prior to participation.<br><br>Questions? Contact <a href="mail
 to:allan.edmonds@gmail.com">Allan Edmonds</a>
LAST-MODIFIED:20200916T183754Z
LOCATION:Sherwood Oaks Christian Church\, 2700 E Rogers Rd\, Bloomington\, 
 IN 47401\, USA\, 
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Early Bird Ride-Fairfax Boat Ramp
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
