BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Bicycle Club
DTSTART:20210529T140000Z
DTEND:20210529T190000Z
DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:2hb9kimneuflt8dpsaeg6h4uk2@google.com
CREATED:20180505T230919Z
DESCRIPTION:<a href="http://bloomingtonbicycleclub.org/maps/John_Bassett_Ma
 ps/Best_Ride_in_Indiana_Story_Option_61.pdf">Best Ride in Indiana Story Opt
 ion 61</a><a></a><br><br><a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/2375442">G
 PS Files</a><br><br>This 61 mile route in Eastern Brown and&nbsp\;Western B
 artholomew Counties was&nbsp\;listed as the “Best Ride in Indiana” in the&n
 bsp\;September 2012 issue of Bicycling&nbsp\;Magazine.<br><br>“You can ride
  50 miles and see 10 cars&nbsp\;total\, and you can start and finish at Dag
 ’s\,&nbsp\;a great ice-cream shop with unique flavors.&nbsp\;Try persimmon\
 , heavenly hash\, or a&nbsp\;concoction called coffee and brownies.”<br><br
 >You be the judge on the ride and the&nbsp\;ice cream !<br><br>The ice crea
 m place is now closed\, but this is still a fun adventure.&nbsp\;The route 
 is a figure-of-eight crossing at&nbsp\;Pike’s Peak in eastern Brown County.
 &nbsp\; It is&nbsp\;revised from the original route due to the closing&nbsp
 \;of Crouch's Market in Pike's Peak.&nbsp\; &nbsp\;Instead\, we will&nbsp\;
 loop westward to Story for a rest stop at Story Inn.&nbsp\; Alternatively\,
  you can delete the south part of the figure-of-eight which gives a nice sh
 ort option of about 38&nbsp\;miles.<br><br>This is a drive and ride. Ride w
 ill depart at&nbsp\;10:00 from the Jay C on the west side of&nbsp\;Columbus
 .<br><br>Non-members should sign up for a <a href="https://secure.getmeregi
 stered.com/get_information.php?event_id=133776">free trial membership</a>\,
  good for up to three rides\, and which includes electronically signing a l
 iability waiver\,&nbsp\;prior to participation.&nbsp\;&nbsp\;
LAST-MODIFIED:20210528T230544Z
LOCATION:Jay C Parking Lot\, Columbus\, IN @ 39.200238\, -85.9722
SEQUENCE:4
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Best Ride in Indiana: Leader: Jeremy Schott
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
