DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u><u></u><u></u>Long option&nbsp\;<u><a href="h
 ttps://ridewithgps.com/routes/39308757">South Shore via Mt. Gilead</a></u> 
 32 miles.<u></u><br>Somewhat shorter option <a href="https://ridewithgps.co
 m/routes/40786905" id="ow962" __is_owner="true">Shuffle Creekvia Mt Gilead<
 /a> about 26 miles.<br><u></u>Shortest option returns from North Mt. Gilead
  via 45 about 20 miles&nbsp\;<br><u></u><br><u></u>Watch the calendar for w
 eather-related updates and for future rides.&nbsp\;<ul><li>Be SAFE. Don't b
 low through stop signs. Consider bike lights.<br></li><li>Be COURTEOUS: Sin
 gle up in traffic<br></li><li>Be PREDICTABLE: Signal your intentions to car
 s and fellow riders.</li></ul>This branch of the OWLS training group also e
 mphasizes somewhat slower\, moderate rides\, and a route planned in advance
  that is posted on the ride calendar. This is a no drop ride\, but not a be
 ginner's ride. Expect an overall average moving speed 11 - 15 mph including
  hills. Distances vary from 20 to 30 miles. Early season rides will be some
 what shorter and slower.During cold weather the ride departs at 1:30pm.<br>
 <br>Non-members should sign up for a&nbsp\;<a href="https://secure.getmereg
 istered.com/get_information.php?event_id=136627">free trial membership</a>\
 , good for up to three rides\, and which includes electronically signing a 
 liability waiver\,&nbsp\;prior to participation.<br><br>Questions? Contact&
 nbsp\;<a href="mailto:allan.edmonds@gmail.com">Allan Edmonds</a><u></u><u><
 /u><u></u><u></u></html-blob>
