DESCRIPTION:80 miles difficult\, shorter option 50 miles\nmoderate (but sti
 ll includes Bear Wallow Hill).\nThose 30 extra miles are worth it! This is 
 a\nchallenging route with some great scenery.\nThe Cordry-Sweetwater Bermud
 a Triangle has\nswallowed some riders so bring a map and try\nto keep other
  riders in sight. Excellent saddle\ntime for RAIN trainees.\n\nNote:  It is
  reported the a bridge is out on Bear\nWallow Hill Road unitil June 28.  Yo
 ur may or \nmay not be able to wade the creek.  Consider\nalternate short r
 oute to Nashville via Salt Creek\nRoad or Greasy Creek Road.\n\n<a href="ht
 tp://www.bloomingtonbicycleclub.org/private/BBCMaps/map_pack_1/cordry_sweet
 water.pdf">Cordry-Sweetwater Lakes</a>\n\n6/14/13 - Route will utllize Uppe
 r Bean\nBlossom Road going north from Gatesville\nRoad rather than Bittersw
 eet Road.  The GPS\nlink below has the correct route map. \n\n<a href="http
 ://ridewithgps.com/routes/2655239">GPS Revised Route</a>
