CREATED:20130609T120805Z
DESCRIPTION:Training Ride-Route to be determined by assembled riders before
  setting out-this is not a no-drop ride\, though we will stop @ several pre
 determined points to allow everyone to gather. Many rides will feature bris
 k\, pace-line riding. Average speeds will vary from around 16mph up to the 
 high 19mph range depending on how we feel and where we go. Distances range 
 from the high 20mi to mid 40mi range depending on the season. Get on your b
 ikes and ride!!
LAST-MODIFIED:20230110T182442Z
LOCATION:Bryan Park
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Training Ride\, Bryan Park
TRANSP:OPAQUE
CATEGORIES:http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#event
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Bicycle Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20220914T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20220914T203000
DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:32sjplfvo35sffcd3c9kcs716p@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20220914T180000
CREATED:20220822T224915Z
DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u><p><b>Ride will leave from the Blackwell&nbsp
 \;Horse Camp on Tower Ridge Road at 6:00PM</b><br></p><p>This route is most
 ly gravel with about two miles of easy double track on HNF Trail 19\, and a
  short&nbsp\;section of pavement on the east&nbsp\;side from Maumee to the 
 Boy&nbsp\;Scout Camp.</p><p>Route is suitable for CX\, MTB\, or Gravel bike
 s.<br><b>&nbsp\;&nbsp\;</b><br>A few club members are planning on camping a
 t Blackwell so stick around after the ride\, there will be a fire for sure 
 and maybe some smores etc.<br><br>BRING LIGHTS !!<br><br><a href="http://bl
 oomingtonbicycleclub.org/maps/Gravel_Rides/Blackwell%20Loop%20to%20HNF%20Tr
 ail%2019.pdf"><u>Blackwell Loop to HNF Trail 19</u></a><br><br><a href="htt
 ps://ridewithgps.com/routes/10147577" id="ow812" __is_owner="true"><u>GPS F
 iles</u></a><br></p><p>These rides feature gravel roads\, single and double
  track trails\,&nbsp\; and just enough pavement to string the aforementione
 d together into fun\, woodsy adventure loops.&nbsp\; Rides begin at 6PM thr
 ough the Fall and Winter months as weather allows and typically last about 
 two hours.&nbsp\; Lights are mandatory as we enter the Fall and Winter seas
 ons.<br></p><p>Routes are suitable for mountain bike or gravel bike\, with 
 some more turned to one or the other.&nbsp\; Rides begin at different locat
 ions\, primarily associated with Yellowwood State Forest\, Brown County Sta
 te Park\, and the Hoosier National Forest in Monroe\, Lawrence\, and Brown 
 Counties. &nbsp\;Specific routes may be dictated by weather conditions\, bu
 t starting locations\, route maps\, and gps file links will be posted here 
 in advance.</p><p>Expect a lot of trees and few cars.&nbsp\;&nbsp\;</p><u><
 /u></html-blob>
LAST-MODIFIED:20230102T144559Z
LOCATION:39.017417\, -86.389368
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Blackwell to HNF Trail 19
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
