DESCRIPTION:<p>These rides feature gravel roads\, single and double track t
 rails\,&nbsp\; and just enough pavement to string the aforementioned togeth
 er into fun\, woodsy adventure loops.&nbsp\; Rides begin at 10am through th
 e Fall and Winter months as weather allows and typically last about three t
 o four hours.</p><p>Routes are suitable for mountain bike or gravel bike\, 
 with some more turned to one or the other.&nbsp\; Rides begin at different 
 locations\, primarily associated with Yellowwood State Forest\, Brown Count
 y State Park\, and the Hoosier National Forest in Monroe\, Lawrence\, and B
 rown Counties. &nbsp\;Specific routes may be dictated by weather conditions
 \, but starting locations\, route maps\, and gps file links will be posted 
 here in advance.</p><p>Expect a lot of trees and few cars.</p>
