BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Bicycle Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20221013T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20221013T203000
DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:32sjplfvo35sffcd3c9kcs716p@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20221012T180000
CREATED:20220822T224915Z
DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u><u></u><u></u><p>This is a Ride not to miss..
 .so much so that Warren calls this the best off road ride ever.&nbsp\; The 
 fall foliage is looking fabulous.<br><br>We will start at the Crooked Creek
  Boat Ramp go up Elkinsville Rd (across Lake Monroe ) to Elkinsville\, up C
 ombs Rd to the Nebo Connector\, and down Nebo to the North parking lot. The
 n it's up Blue Creek Rd to Trail D\, up Trail D to Miller Ridge\, down the 
 water bars to Crooked Creek Rd\, and back to the parking lot - a total of 1
 8.4 beautiful miles.<br><br>PLEASE DON'T MISS THIS ONE.<br><br>BRING LIGHTS
 ! BRING LIGHTS! BRING LIGHTS<br></p><p><a href="https://ridewithgps.com/rou
 tes/17463607">Reverse Blue Creek Elkinsville Loop Plus Trail D 18 - A bike 
 ride in Brown County\, IN (ridewithgps.com)</a><br></p><p>This route favors
  MTB but is rideable with a gravel bike</p><p>These rides feature gravel ro
 ads\, single and double track trails\,&nbsp\; and just enough pavement to s
 tring the aforementioned together into fun\, woodsy adventure loops.&nbsp\;
  Rides begin at 6PM through the Fall and Winter months as weather allows an
 d typically last about two hours.&nbsp\; Lights are mandatory as we enter t
 he Fall and Winter seasons.</p><p>Routes are suitable for mountain bike or 
 gravel bike\, with some more turned to one or the other.&nbsp\; Rides begin
  at different locations\, primarily associated with Yellowwood State Forest
 \, Brown County State Park\, and the Hoosier National Forest in Monroe\, La
 wrence\, and Brown Counties. &nbsp\;Specific routes may be dictated by weat
 her conditions\, but starting locations\, route maps\, and gps file links w
 ill be posted here in advance.</p><p>Expect a lot of trees and few cars.&nb
 sp\;&nbsp\;</p><u></u><u></u><u></u></html-blob>
LAST-MODIFIED:20230102T144559Z
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Reverse Blue Creek Elkinsville Loop - Off Road Adventure Ride
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Bicycle Club
