DESCRIPTION:<a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/34394090" id="ow766" __
 is_owner="true">https://ridewithgps.com/routes/34394090</a><br><br><html-bl
 ob>Please observe social distancing norms as we gather and ride.&nbsp\;<ul>
 <li>Be SAFE. Don't blow through stop signs. Consider bike lights.<br></li><
 li>Be COURTEOUS: Single up in traffic<br></li><li>Be PREDICTABLE: Signal yo
 ur intentions to cars and fellow riders.</li></ul>The "Older\, Wiser\, and 
 a Little Slower" training group emphasizes moderate rides\, and a route pla
 nned in advance that is posted on the ride calendar. This is a no drop ride
 \, but not a beginner's ride.The OWLS group welcomes a wide range of interm
 ediate riders\, and typically breaks off into a faster and slower group wit
 h the former averaging an overall moving speed of 16-18 mph\, and the slowe
 r group averaging 13-15 mph (including hills).&nbsp\;Distances vary from 20
  to 30 miles\, depending partly on available light. Early season rides will
  be somewhat shorter and slower. Rides depart promptly at 5:45.<br><br>Non-
 members should sign up for a <a href="https://secure.getmeregistered.com/ge
 t_information.php?event_id=136627">free trial membership</a>\, good for up 
 to three rides\, and which includes electronically signing a liability waiv
 er\,&nbsp\;prior to participation.<br><br>Questions? Contact&nbsp\;<a href=
 "mailto:gail.morell@gmail.com">Gail Morell</a>.<u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u>
 </html-blob>
LAST-MODIFIED:20221011T180341Z
