CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20091217T064809Z
DESCRIPTION:The OWLS (Older or Wiser or a Little Slower) group is dedicated
  to training and touring rides at a moderate rate\, typically in the 13-14 
 mph range. We keep an eye on each other. We take time to enjoy the scenery\
 , even stop to take a picture. Week day rides will typically be in the 20-2
 5 mile range.\n\nEmail bbcowls@me.com for more information.
LAST-MODIFIED:20230110T181635Z
LOCATION: 2700 E Rogers Rd\, Bloomington\, IN (Sherwood Oaks Church)
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:OWLS Training Ride
TRANSP:OPAQUE
CATEGORIES:http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#event
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Bicycle Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20221123T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20221123T203000
DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:32sjplfvo35sffcd3c9kcs716p@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20221123T180000
CREATED:20220822T224915Z
DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u><p><span style="background-color: var(--textf
 ield-surface)\; color: var(--on-surface)\;">This 21 mile ride will start / 
 finish at TC Steele and head across East Kent Road to McGowan.&nbsp\; You'l
 l get the chance to pit your wits\, strength\, legs and lungs against 'Jack
 ass' hill before heading across Bartley Ridge.&nbsp\; We'll loop back aroun
 d Crooked Creek road before climbing back up to TC Steele.</span><br></p><p
 ><span style="background-color: var(--textfield-surface)\; color: var(--on-
 surface)\;">Bring Lights!</span></p><p><a href="https://ridewithgps.com/rou
 tes/41476243" id="ow414" __is_owner="true">TC Steele Figure 8</a></p><p>The
 se rides feature gravel roads\, single and double track trails\,&nbsp\; and
  just enough pavement to string the aforementioned together into fun\, wood
 sy adventure loops.&nbsp\; Rides begin at 6PM through the Fall and Winter m
 onths as weather allows and typically last about two hours.&nbsp\; Lights a
 re mandatory as we enter the Fall and Winter seasons.</p><p>Routes are suit
 able for mountain bike or gravel bike\, with some more turned to one or the
  other.&nbsp\; Rides begin at different locations\, primarily associated wi
 th Yellowwood State Forest\, Brown County State Park\, and the Hoosier Nati
 onal Forest in Monroe\, Lawrence\, and Brown Counties. &nbsp\;Specific rout
 es may be dictated by weather conditions\, but starting locations\, route m
 aps\, and gps file links will be posted here in advance.</p><p>Expect a lot
  of trees and few cars.&nbsp\;&nbsp\;</p><u></u></html-blob>
LAST-MODIFIED:20230102T144559Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:TC Steele Figure 8 - Off Road Adventure Ride
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
