CREATED:20120415T220642Z
DESCRIPTION:2012 Bike Summit: Reflect\, Innovate\, and Respond (theme)\n\n 
    4:00 - 4:15 Welcome and introductions\n    4:15 to 5:15 break-out sessio
 ns (up to four) that will focus on ways to improve and build momentum. \n  
   5:30 - 6:00 - Keynote presentation by Jeffery Olson from Alta Planning an
 d Design will unveil Bloomington's Bikeways designs\n    6:00 to 7:00/7:30 
 - Open house to view the Bikeway designs and mingle with fellow cyclists\, 
 project designers\, staff\, and elected officials. \n    7:30 to ??? Apre B
 ike Summit - may be an option for a bike tour or another fun event to help 
 kick-off Bloomington Bikes Week. \n\nSummit Objective:\n\n    Educate/Incre
 ase Awareness\n    Implement - move some ideas into action\n    Increase pa
 rticipation/commitments\, build social capital\, etc.   \n\nSessions (tenta
 tive):\n\n    Social Equity of Bicycling - round table/panel discussion fro
 m BHA\, Shalom\, New Hope Family Shelter on basic needs of lower income cyc
 lists\n    Gateway Trail System - Wapehani Mountain Bike Park: sustainable 
 trail system\, trail building\, promotions\, and the Gateway Trail System (
 Invited guest - IMBA Regional Director Andy Williamson) \n    Bicycle Frien
 dly Town and Gown Integration - IU's Bicycle Friendly Campus\n    The Makin
 g of Bikes Month 2013 - many encouragement ideas are listed within BAJP. Wo
 rk with agencies and City Staff to shift gears and build upon existing succ
 ess and embark on new endeavors for 2013
LAST-MODIFIED:20230110T181542Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Bloomington Bike Summit\, City Hall
TRANSP:OPAQUE
CATEGORIES:http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#event
END:VEVENT
