DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u><u></u><u></u>Long option: <a href="https://r
 idewithgps.com/routes/39390952">Shiloh </a>30 miles</html-blob><br><html-bl
 ob>Shorter option <a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/40935851" id="ow1
 648" __is_owner="true">Nehrt </a>26 miles</html-blob><br><html-blob><u></u>
 <br><u></u>Watch the calendar for weather-related updates and for future ri
 des.&nbsp\;<ul><li>Be SAFE. Don't blow through stop signs. Consider bike li
 ghts.<br></li><li>Be COURTEOUS: Single up in traffic<br></li><li>Be PREDICT
 ABLE: Signal your intentions to cars and fellow riders.</li></ul>This branc
 h of the OWLS training group also emphasizes somewhat slower\, moderate rid
 es\, and a route planned in advance that is posted on the ride calendar. Th
 is is a no drop ride\, but not a beginner's ride. Expect an overall average
  moving speed 11 - 15 mph including hills. Distances vary from 20 to 30 mil
 es. Early season rides will be somewhat shorter and slower.During cold weat
 her the ride departs at 1:30pm.<br><br>Non-members should sign up for a&nbs
 p\;<a href="https://secure.getmeregistered.com/get_information.php?event_id
 =136627">free trial membership</a>\, good for up to three rides\, and which
  includes electronically signing a liability waiver\,&nbsp\;prior to partic
 ipation.<br><br>Questions? Contact&nbsp\;<a href="mailto:allan.edmonds@gmai
 l.com">Allan Edmonds</a><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u></html-blob>
