DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u><u></u><u></u><a href="https://bloomingtonbic
 ycleclub.org/maps/iRides/Southern_Loop_30_rev_1.pdf">Southern Loop 30 rev1.
 pdf</a><u></u><br><br><u></u><a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/219158
 21">GPS Files</a><br><u></u><br><u></u>Watch the calendar for weather-relat
 ed updates and for future rides.&nbsp\;<ul><li>Be SAFE. Don't blow through 
 stop signs. Consider bike lights.<br></li><li>Be COURTEOUS: Single up in tr
 affic<br></li><li>Be PREDICTABLE: Signal your intentions to cars and fellow
  riders.</li></ul>This branch of the OWLS training group also emphasizes so
 mewhat slower\, moderate rides\, and a route planned in advance that is pos
 ted on the ride calendar. This is a no drop ride\, but not a beginner's rid
 e. Expect an overall average moving speed 11 - 15 mph including hills. Dist
 ances vary from 20 to 30 miles. Early season rides will be somewhat shorter
  and slower.During cold weather the ride departs at 1:30pm.<br><br>Non-memb
 ers should sign up for a&nbsp\;<a href="https://secure.getmeregistered.com/
 get_information.php?event_id=136627">free trial membership</a>\, good for u
 p to three rides\, and which includes electronically signing a liability wa
 iver\,&nbsp\;prior to participation.<br><br>Questions? Contact&nbsp\;<a hre
 f="mailto:allan.edmonds@gmail.com">Allan Edmonds</a><u></u><u></u><u></u><u
 ></u></html-blob>
