UID:76goke0o1n3k5j8qk81fu0sg83@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20221217T100000
CREATED:20220901T172010Z
DESCRIPTION:<p>We have not done the western part of HNF Trail 18 or Trail 4
  in a couple of years\, so we are giving this little MTB loop a try.&nbsp\;
  Expect a couple of steep climbs and perhaps some soggy bottom terrain.&nbs
 p\; Meet at the Hickory Ridge Fire Tower on Tower Ridge Road at 10:00AM.&nb
 sp\; MTB is recommended.</p><p><a href="https://bloomingtonbicycleclub.org/
 maps/Gravel_Rides/Hickory_Ridge_Trails_18_and_4.pdf">Hickory Ridge Trails 1
 8 and 4</a><br></p><p><a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/41612835">GPS
  Files</a><br></p><p>These rides feature gravel roads\, single and double t
 rack trails\,&nbsp\; and just enough pavement to string the aforementioned 
 together into fun\, woodsy adventure loops.&nbsp\; Rides begin at 10am thro
 ugh the Fall and Winter months as weather allows and typically last about t
 hree to four hours.</p><p>Routes are suitable for mountain bike or gravel b
 ike\, with some more turned to one or the other.&nbsp\; Rides begin at diff
 erent locations\, primarily associated with Yellowwood State Forest\, Brown
  County State Park\, and the Hoosier National Forest in Monroe\, Lawrence\,
  and Brown Counties. &nbsp\;Specific routes may be dictated by weather cond
 itions\, but starting locations\, route maps\, and gps file links will be p
 osted here in advance.</p><p>Expect a lot of trees and few cars.</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20221216T170503Z
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Hickory Ridge Trails 18 and 4
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
