CREATED:20220103T154704Z
DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u><p>Longer option&nbsp\;<a href="https://ridew
 ithgps.com/routes/39390952"><u>Shiloh</u></a> 30 miles. Out Kerr Cr and ret
 urn via Cascades.</p><p>Shorter option&nbsp\;<a href="https://ridewithgps.c
 om/routes/1623341"><u>Long Russell</u></a> (Out Kerr Cr and Mt Gilead) 23 m
 iles. Shorter options skip Russell or go south on Mt Gilead instead of nort
 h.</p><u></u><br><u></u>Watch the calendar for weather-related updates and 
 for future rides.&nbsp\;<ul><li>Be SAFE. Don't blow through stop signs. Con
 sider bike lights.<br></li><li>Be COURTEOUS: Single up in traffic<br></li><
 li>Be PREDICTABLE: Signal your intentions to cars and fellow riders.</li></
 ul>This branch of the OWLS training group also emphasizes somewhat slower\,
  moderate rides\, and a route planned in advance that is posted on the ride
  calendar. This is a no drop ride\, but not a beginner's ride. Expect an ov
 erall average moving speed 11 - 15 mph including hills. Distances vary from
  20 to 30 miles. Early season rides will be somewhat shorter and slower.Dur
 ing cold weather the ride departs at 1:30pm.<br><br>Non-members should sign
  up for a&nbsp\;<a href="https://secure.getmeregistered.com/get_information
 .php?event_id=136627">free trial membership</a>\, good for up to three ride
 s\, and which includes electronically signing a liability waiver\,&nbsp\;pr
 ior to participation.<br><br>Questions? Contact&nbsp\;<a href="mailto:allan
 .edmonds@gmail.com">Allan Edmonds</a><u></u><u></u><u></u><u></u></html-blo
 b>
