BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Bicycle Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20221112T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20221112T140000
DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:76goke0o1n3k5j8qk81fu0sg83@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20221112T100000
CREATED:20220901T172010Z
DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><p>Hi Everyone\,\,</p><p>Saturday is the start of fi
 reams hunting season so we'll stick mostly to the roads this week.</p><p>Th
 is ride will start at the church on Hickory Grove and head towards Houston 
 via Maumee.&nbsp\; We will head up Berry Road and loop back to Houston wher
 e we have the choice to do only one or both Baldy's.&nbsp\; We will take Tr
 ail 21 on the way back to the Church which is a mile of easy going single a
 nd double track.</p><p><a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/41388150" id
 ="ow413" __is_owner="true">Hickory Grove Church Berry Ridge And Baldy's</a>
 <br></p><p><span style="background-color: var(--textfield-surface)\; color:
  var(--on-surface)\;">These rides feature gravel roads\, single and double 
 track trails\,&nbsp\; and just enough pavement to string the aforementioned
  together into fun\, woodsy adventure loops.&nbsp\; Rides begin at 10am thr
 ough the Fall and Winter months as weather allows and typically last about 
 three to four hours.</span><br></p><p>Routes are suitable for mountain bike
  or gravel bike\, with some more turned to one or the other.&nbsp\; Rides b
 egin at different locations\, primarily associated with Yellowwood State Fo
 rest\, Brown County State Park\, and the Hoosier National Forest in Monroe\
 , Lawrence\, and Brown Counties. &nbsp\;Specific routes may be dictated by 
 weather conditions\, but starting locations\, route maps\, and gps file lin
 ks will be posted here in advance.</p><p>Expect a lot of trees and few cars
 .</p></html-blob>
