BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Bicycle Club
DTSTART:20120616T100000Z
DTEND:20120617T010000Z
DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:8p3jorrej82g0fd1540ffgsigc@google.com
CREATED:20120217T015518Z
DESCRIPTION:MAP: <a href="http://ridewithgps.com/routes/1012908">GPS</a> Du
 bbed "Rudy's Double"\, Rudy Savich mapped out a route and also raised money
  for a Bloomington charity.\nLast year\, it was mapped out by Jim Schroeder
 \, as six riders started out in the rain in Ellettsville and travelled to P
 aris\, Illinois.\nA very special route has been designed for 2012 in order 
 to travel to Henryville and Marysville\, IN where the March tornadoes hamme
 red that area.  Jim Schroeder would like any Bloomington Bicycle Club membe
 r and anyone in the community to donate or pledge money to a reputable char
 ity down in Henryville\, www.henryvillehope.com (check out their website an
 d videos).   When we come into Henryville at about 105 miles\, we will pres
 ent them what money we have gathered or pledged to help their plight.\nJim 
 says it's payback time.  We all ride Southern Indiana because of the quiet 
 scenic hills and the sparseness of automobiles and trucks.  But\, this area
  is also quite poor and this is our opportunity to give something back.\n20
 0 miles too much?  Then get a partner\, and each one of you do 100 miles.  
 Sylvia Stoub will crew one support vehicle and has some room in the Subaru\
 , but more crew vehicles would help out a lot as the riders can spread out.
 \nJim would like to see an immense turnout for this charitable effort.  If 
 you're interested in any way\, please e-mail him jimmyschweb@gmail.com.\nEa
 ch rider can organize their own pledge efforts among the community\, and an
 y BBC member that just wants to give can mail a check to HCC Recovery\, c/o
  Jim Schroeder\, 1407 S Lincoln St\, Bloomington\, IN 47401.
LAST-MODIFIED:20230110T182626Z
LOCATION:Bryan Park @ 39.15435\,-86.523
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Jim's Double Century
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#event
END:VEVENT
