BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Bicycle Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230107T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20230107T140000
DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:76goke0o1n3k5j8qk81fu0sg83@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20230107T100000
CREATED:20220901T172010Z
DESCRIPTION:<p>This ride hits 9 of the checkpoints on the Death March and s
 tarts at the fire tower.  We'll head down Tower Ridge road and veer off to 
 hit Robertson Cemetery then say Hi to the cool dog (he really is a cool dog
 !) on the way to Fleetwood.  We'll double back slightly and head to Houston
  and hit Thompson before doubling back again to go up Baldy 1 and head to G
 orbetts.  Enjoy the great downhill on the way to Hanner as things start to 
 get lumpy as we hit Cornett and then head off-road onto Trail 16 to hit Cal
 lahan and head towards Hoosier Horse Camp on Trail 15 where we get back on 
 the 'smooth' stuff (it's all relative right?) and head to Hickory Grove Chu
 rch and back to the fire tower.</p><p>Suitable for Gravel or MTB but if you
  have an MTB bring it as there is a 4 mile section of mostly single track t
 o get to Callahan.</p><p><a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/41720806?p
 rivacy_code=qrE8ee5PhX6w4Uf3">Death March Training - 33</a></p><p>For those
  of you not familiar with the Death March checkout the link below...</p><p>
 <a href="https://www.dinoseries.com/death-march-route/">https://www.dinoser
 ies.com/death-march-route/</a><br /></p><p><span>These rides feature gravel
  roads\, single and double track trails\,  and just enough pavement to stri
 ng the aforementioned together into fun\, woodsy adventure loops.  Rides be
 gin at 10am through the Fall and Winter months as weather allows and typica
 lly last about three to four hours.</span><br /></p><p>Routes are suitable 
 for mountain bike or gravel bike\, with some more turned to one or the othe
 r.  Rides begin at different locations\, primarily associated with Yellowwo
 od State Forest\, Brown County State Park\, and the Hoosier National Forest
  in Monroe\, Lawrence\, and Brown Counties.  Specific routes may be dictate
 d by weather conditions\, but starting locations\, route maps\, and gps fil
 e links will be posted here in advance.</p><p>Expect a lot of trees and few
  cars.</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20230106T135355Z
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Death March 33 - Off Road Adventure
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Bicycle Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20220719T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20220719T123000
DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:87ij495mak18b1ai2sionaobp1@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20220719T093000
CREATED:20220103T154704Z
DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/40234715" id
 ="ow572" __is_owner="true">Griffy-Shuffle</a> 29 miles</html-blob><br><html
 -blob><br><u></u>Watch the calendar for weather-related updates and for fut
 ure rides.&nbsp\;<ul><li>Be SAFE. Don't blow through stop signs. Consider b
 ike lights.<br></li><li>Be COURTEOUS: Single up in traffic<br></li><li>Be P
 REDICTABLE: Signal your intentions to cars and fellow riders.</li></ul>This
  branch of the OWLS training group also emphasizes somewhat slower\, modera
 te rides\, and a route planned in advance that is posted on the ride calend
 ar. This is a no drop ride\, but not a beginner's ride. Expect an overall a
 verage moving speed 11 - 15 mph including hills. Distances vary from 20 to 
 30 miles. Early season rides will be somewhat shorter and slower.During col
 d weather the ride departs at 1:30pm.<br><br>Non-members should sign up for
  a&nbsp\;<a href="https://secure.getmeregistered.com/get_information.php?ev
 ent_id=136627">free trial membership</a>\, good for up to three rides\, and
  which includes electronically signing a liability waiver\,&nbsp\;prior to 
 participation.<br><br>Questions? Contact&nbsp\;<a href="mailto:allan.edmond
 s@gmail.com">Allan Edmonds</a><u></u><u></u></html-blob>
LAST-MODIFIED:20221006T224643Z
LOCATION:Bryan Park Parking Lot\, S Woodlawn Ave\, Bloomington\, IN 47401\,
  USA
SEQUENCE:3
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Early Birds - Griffy-Shuffle
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
