CREATED:20120317T003320Z
DESCRIPTION:This is the 2nd (annual?) Tweed ride\, which is a\nslow-pace so
 cial ride with games and tea. Instead\nof lycra\, you'll want to sport twee
 d jackets or other\nproper attire appropriate for tea and biscuits.\nThis i
 s a group bicycle ride through Bloomington\,\nin which the cyclists are exp
 ected to dress in\ntraditional British cycling attire\, particularly tweed\
 nplus four suits.  Those would be those knicker type\nthings that extend 4 
 inches below the knee.\nAny bicycle is acceptable on the Tweed Ride\,\nbut 
 classic vintage bicycles are encouraged.\nSome effort to recreate the spiri
 t of a bygone era\nis always appreciated.\n\nAssemble at the Irish Lion at 
 12:00 for a\n1:00 PM departure.  The ride will end at Max’s\nPlace on 6th S
 treet.  You get the idea here.\n\nLeader: Vince Caristo\, City of Bloomingt
 on\n\nGo here to see what a Tweed Ride is all about.\n<a href="http://sacto
 tweed.blogspot.com/">A Tweed Ride</a>
LAST-MODIFIED:20230110T181429Z
LOCATION:Meet at Irish Lion at noon\, depart at 1:00\, then Max's Place at 
 3:00 @ 39.166723\, -86.535530
