BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Bicycle Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20110417T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20110417T160000
DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:s9fu80t194h5u5cudmec6a4qhk@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20110417T133000
CLASS:PUBLIC
CREATED:20130609T120752Z
DESCRIPTION:The Nice N' Easy Ride will be joining the Breaking Away Ride le
 d by Jim Schroeder. We will be meeting one-half hour earelier.\n\nIf you ju
 st can't get enough of The Little 500 (held this year April 15-16)\, then y
 ou should come ride the BBC Breaking Away Ride on Sunday\, April 17. It's a
  nostalgic ride that visits many of the scenes in the classic 1979 movie Br
 eaking Away. Ride by the Dave Stohler house and shout "Refund! Refund!" Man
 y more landmarks will be called out by ride leader Jim Schroeder who has se
 en the movie well over 100 times. The ride is only 31 miles and includes on
 e rest stop. See the movie before you go\, attend the Little 500 and then r
 ide the movie rich in local history. See you Sunday at Bryan Park Pool park
 ing lot for a 1 p.m. departure. Ciao!\n\n<a href="http://www.bloomingtonbic
 ycleclub.org/maps/Jim%20Schroeder/Breaking_Away.pdf">Breaking Away Ride Map
 </a>
LAST-MODIFIED:20230110T181610Z
LOCATION:Bryan Park Pool Parking Lot @ 39.15435\,-86.523
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Nice N Easy Ride MEETS EARLIER
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#event
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Bicycle Club
DTSTART:20101017T173000Z
DTEND:20101017T213000Z
DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:5b7gc8vn6d8t21u1t8umm0hvdc@google.com
CREATED:20100929T123132Z
DESCRIPTION:Distance 27 to 30 mile range.<br>Start time (1:30)<br><br>Start
 ing at the parking lot of the Clear Creek Bike Trail at That Road.<br><br><
 a href="http://www.gmap-pedometer.com/?r=4043622">Gmap of Ride</a><br><br>T
 his is a ride to prepare members to make informed comments to the I-69 Stud
 y in order to mitigate or improve the conditions for cycling in S.W. Monroe
  County to the best of our ability.<br><br>Ride leader Jean Smith<br>jean@b
 ikesmiths.net<br>BBC representative to the I-69 Citizen Advisory Commission
  section 4<br><br>Maps of the proposed closures and grade separated crossin
 gs are on the <a href="http://www.bloomingtonbicycleclub.org/advocacy.php">
 BBC Advocacy Page</a>.
LAST-MODIFIED:20230110T182854Z
LOCATION:The Parking Lot of the Clear Creek Bike Trail at That Road @ 39.11
 5170\, -86.549480
SEQUENCE:2
