BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Bicycle Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20221221T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20221221T203000
DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:32sjplfvo35sffcd3c9kcs716p@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20221221T180000
CREATED:20220822T224915Z
DESCRIPTION:<u></u><p>We did the trail parts of this a few weeks ago and ha
 d a blast.&nbsp\; this ride starts at the Hickory Ridge Fire Tower on Tower
  Ridge Road.&nbsp\; We'll take gravel down to HNF Trail 19 then gravel to T
 rail 20.&nbsp\; We go up the big gravel hill at the pipeline crossing and t
 ake Poke Patch down to Horse Camp Road before looping back north past Hicko
 ry Grove Church to the Fire Tower.&nbsp\; MTB would be most comfortable\, b
 ut entirely doable on a gravel bike.&nbsp\;&nbsp\;</p><p><a href="https://r
 idewithgps.com/routes/41630749" id="ow616" __is_owner="true">Trails to Poke
  Patch 16</a></p><p>These rides feature gravel roads\, single and double tr
 ack trails\,&nbsp\; and just enough pavement to string the aforementioned t
 ogether into fun\, woodsy adventure loops.&nbsp\; Rides begin at 6PM throug
 h the Fall and Winter months as weather allows and typically last about two
  hours.&nbsp\; Lights are mandatory as we enter the Fall and Winter seasons
 .</p><p>Routes are suitable for mountain bike or gravel bike\, with some mo
 re turned to one or the other.&nbsp\; Rides begin at different locations\, 
 primarily associated with Yellowwood State Forest\, Brown County State Park
 \, and the Hoosier National Forest in Monroe\, Lawrence\, and Brown Countie
 s. &nbsp\;Specific routes may be dictated by weather conditions\, but start
 ing locations\, route maps\, and gps file links will be posted here in adva
 nce.</p><p>Expect a lot of trees and few cars.&nbsp\;&nbsp\;</p><u></u>
LAST-MODIFIED:20230102T144559Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Trails to Poke Patch 16
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
