UID:upgnsr5941p54pshb3pb9rs37c@google.com
CREATED:20130609T120756Z
DESCRIPTION:Tu/Thurs training rides are for those of us who like to challen
 ge ourselves in a cooperative group riding style. This is Not a no-drop rid
 e but we do stop to gather from time to time. Paceline riding with occasion
 al sprint zones. Routes are determined by those who gather after a brief di
 scussion. Take it easy on the way out of town\, ramp it up later. Early sea
 son averages around 16-17mph\, later in season 18-20mph.
LAST-MODIFIED:20230110T181832Z
LOCATION:Bryan Park @ 39.154673\, -86.522430
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Tu/Thurs Training Rides
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#event
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Bicycle Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20221210T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20221210T140000
DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:76goke0o1n3k5j8qk81fu0sg83@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20221210T100000
CREATED:20220901T172010Z
DESCRIPTION:<p>This 33 mile ride starts at 10am from the hunters checkin on
  East Kent road.</p><p><a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/41573444" id
 ="ow426" __is_owner="true">Up Sewel to Beanblossom</a><br></p><p>Suitable f
 or MTB\, Cross or Gravel bikes</p><p>These rides feature gravel roads\, sin
 gle and double track trails\,&nbsp\; and just enough pavement to string the
  aforementioned together into fun\, woodsy adventure loops.&nbsp\; Rides be
 gin at 10am through the Fall and Winter months as weather allows and typica
 lly last about three to four hours.</p><p>Routes are suitable for mountain 
 bike or gravel bike\, with some more turned to one or the other.&nbsp\; Rid
 es begin at different locations\, primarily associated with Yellowwood Stat
 e Forest\, Brown County State Park\, and the Hoosier National Forest in Mon
 roe\, Lawrence\, and Brown Counties. &nbsp\;Specific routes may be dictated
  by weather conditions\, but starting locations\, route maps\, and gps file
  links will be posted here in advance.</p><p>Expect a lot of trees and few 
 cars.</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20221208T203825Z
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Up Sewel to Beanblossom - Off Road Adventure
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
