UID:87ij495mak18b1ai2sionaobp1_R20220726T133000@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20220726T093000
CREATED:20220103T154704Z
DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><p><u><a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/360915
 49">Down Gore and Back Ketcham</a></u> 28 miles</p><u></u><br><u></u>Watch 
 the calendar for weather-related updates and for future rides.&nbsp\;<ul><l
 i>Be SAFE. Don't blow through stop signs. Consider bike lights.<br></li><li
 >Be COURTEOUS: Single up in traffic<br></li><li>Be PREDICTABLE: Signal your
  intentions to cars and fellow riders.</li></ul>This branch of the OWLS tra
 ining group also emphasizes somewhat slower\, moderate rides\, and a route 
 planned in advance that is posted on the ride calendar. This is a no drop r
 ide\, but not a beginner's ride. Expect an overall average moving speed 11 
 - 15 mph including hills. Distances vary from 20 to 30 miles. Early season 
 rides will be somewhat shorter and slower.During cold weather the ride depa
 rts at 1:30pm.<br><br>Non-members should sign up for a&nbsp\;<a href="https
 ://secure.getmeregistered.com/get_information.php?event_id=136627">free tri
 al membership</a>\, good for up to three rides\, and which includes electro
 nically signing a liability waiver\,&nbsp\;prior to participation.<br><br>Q
 uestions? Contact&nbsp\;<a href="mailto:allan.edmonds@gmail.com">Allan Edmo
 nds</a><u></u><u></u><u></u></html-blob>
LAST-MODIFIED:20221006T224643Z
LOCATION:Bryan Park Parking Lot\, S Woodlawn Ave\, Bloomington\, IN 47401\,
  USA
SEQUENCE:3
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Early Birds - Down Gore
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Bicycle Club
DTSTART:20091011T140000Z
DTEND:20091011T170000Z
DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:hv4duamqf5vd2tdeerhghj83ao@google.com
CREATED:20090927T135416Z
DESCRIPTION:The Morgan County Fall Foliage Festival is celebrating 50 years
 ! What better reason for a 50-mile bicycle ride. The ride heads to the hill
 s along the north side of the beautiful White River Valley. The 15-mile rid
 e is flat. The 30-mile and the 50-mile will have challenging hills. There w
 ill be a police escort at the start. CIBA (Central Indiana Bicycle Associat
 ion) is sponsoring the ride so there is no cost to the riders\, the ride is
  free. The roads will be marked and maps will be given out at the start. Th
 ere will also be food (SAG) stops on the ride.\n\n For more info\, contact 
 Mark Stuttgen 765-349-1537 mlstuttgen@comcast.net
LAST-MODIFIED:20230110T181844Z
LOCATION:Martinsville: meet at Jimmy Nash City Park (Harrison St. & Home Av
 e.)
SEQUENCE:2
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:CIBA Fall Foliage Ride
TRANSP:OPAQUE
CATEGORIES:http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#event
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Bicycle Club
