BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Bicycle Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230111T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20230111T203000
DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:4ah2ib1u9kb6kau6sf6b5blc6m_R20230104T230000@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20230111T180000
CREATED:20220822T224915Z
DESCRIPTION:<u></u><p>This 20 mile ride starts at the parking lot overlooki
 ng Yellowwood Lake and heads towards 46 via Jacskon Creek Road.  We'll get 
 on 46 for a brief stint before heading up Scare-O-Fat and picking up Tulip 
 Tree up to 45.  Tulip Tree is an easy going 5 mile stretch of double track.
  When we get to 45 we'll head across Lanan Ridge\, down Dubois and then hea
 d back to the cars at Yellowwood Lake. </p><p>Suitable for Gravel\, Cross o
 r MTB</p><p>Hope to see you there!</p><p><a href="https://ridewithgps.com/r
 outes/34396702">Tulip Tree Trek 20</a><br /></p><p>These rides feature grav
 el roads\, single and double track trails\,  and just enough pavement to st
 ring the aforementioned together into fun\, woodsy adventure loops.  Rides 
 begin at 6PM through the Fall and Winter months as weather allows and typic
 ally last about two hours.  Lights are mandatory as we enter the Fall and W
 inter seasons.</p><p>Routes are suitable for mountain bike or gravel bike\,
  with some more turned to one or the other.  Rides begin at different locat
 ions\, primarily associated with Yellowwood State Forest\, Brown County Sta
 te Park\, and the Hoosier National Forest in Monroe\, Lawrence\, and Brown 
 Counties.  Specific routes may be dictated by weather conditions\, but star
 ting locations\, route maps\, and gps file links will be posted here in adv
 ance.</p><p>Expect a lot of trees and few cars.  </p><u></u>
LAST-MODIFIED:20230109T140346Z
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Tulip Tree Trek - Off Road Adventure
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
