BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Bicycle Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20221102T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20221102T203000
DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:32sjplfvo35sffcd3c9kcs716p@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20221102T180000
CREATED:20220822T224915Z
DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u><p>This route is borrowed from Wes &amp\; Dan
 a\, and is a 21 mile gravel loop through and around the Yellowwood State Fo
 rest.&nbsp\; Park At old Little Nashville Opry parking lot and start at 6:0
 0PM.<br><br>All gravel or paved roads NO TRAILS!<br><br>BRING LIGHTS!!!!<br
 ><a href="http://goog_1922713921"><u><br></u></a><a href="https://ridewithg
 ps.com/routes/16544605" id="ow644" __is_owner="true"><u>Yellowwood Dubois L
 oop 21</u></a></p><p>These rides feature gravel roads\, single and double t
 rack trails\,&nbsp\; and just enough pavement to string the aforementioned 
 together into fun\, woodsy adventure loops.&nbsp\; Rides begin at 6PM throu
 gh the Fall and Winter months as weather allows and typically last about tw
 o hours.&nbsp\; Lights are mandatory as we enter the Fall and Winter season
 s.</p><p>Routes are suitable for mountain bike or gravel bike\, with some m
 ore turned to one or the other.&nbsp\; Rides begin at different locations\,
  primarily associated with Yellowwood State Forest\, Brown County State Par
 k\, and the Hoosier National Forest in Monroe\, Lawrence\, and Brown Counti
 es. &nbsp\;Specific routes may be dictated by weather conditions\, but star
 ting locations\, route maps\, and gps file links will be posted here in adv
 ance.</p><p>Expect a lot of trees and few cars.&nbsp\;&nbsp\;</p><u></u></h
 tml-blob>
LAST-MODIFIED:20230102T144559Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Yellowwood / Dubois Loop - Off Road Adventure Ride
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
