UID:32sjplfvo35sffcd3c9kcs716p@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20221109T180000
CREATED:20220822T224915Z
DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u><u></u><p>This 21 mile ride from Blackwell Ho
 rse Camp is mostly gravel with about 2 miles of easy going single track.</p
 ><p>A couple of club members are planning on camping at the horse camp so s
 tick around for some fellowship around a camp fire after the ride.&nbsp\;Th
 is ight be our last ride in the 70's for a while so let's make the most of 
 it<br></p><p><a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/41387945">Tower Ridge\
 , Trail 19 &amp\; 20</a><br></p><p>Suitable for Gravel\, Cross or MTB.</p><
 p>Clocks have gone back so we'll be starting in the dark - Bring Lights!</p
 ><p><br></p><p>These rides feature gravel roads\, single and double track t
 rails\,&nbsp\; and just enough pavement to string the aforementioned togeth
 er into fun\, woodsy adventure loops.&nbsp\; Rides begin at 6PM through the
  Fall and Winter months as weather allows and typically last about two hour
 s.&nbsp\; Lights are mandatory as we enter the Fall and Winter seasons.</p>
 <p>Routes are suitable for mountain bike or gravel bike\, with some more tu
 rned to one or the other.&nbsp\; Rides begin at different locations\, prima
 rily associated with Yellowwood State Forest\, Brown County State Park\, an
 d the Hoosier National Forest in Monroe\, Lawrence\, and Brown Counties. &n
 bsp\;Specific routes may be dictated by weather conditions\, but starting l
 ocations\, route maps\, and gps file links will be posted here in advance.<
 /p><p>Expect a lot of trees and few cars.&nbsp\;&nbsp\;</p><u></u><u></u></
 html-blob>
LAST-MODIFIED:20230102T144559Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Tower Ridge\, Trail 19 & 20 - Off Road Adventure Ride
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
