CREATED:20130407T131023Z
DESCRIPTION:Ninety miles difficult. This "almost" century\nincorporates the
  best of what this area has to\noffer cyclists - big climbs\, rolling hills
 \, curves\,\nflats\, buccolic views\, bizarre town names\n(Zelma) and sites
  (the Stonehead). Ride this\nonce and you will be hooked. Warning: no\nindo
 or plumbing till Story at mile 50.\n\n<a href="http://www.bloomingtonbicycl
 eclub.org/private/BBCMaps/map_pack_1/nashville_90.pdf">Nashville 90</a>
LAST-MODIFIED:20230110T182717Z
LOCATION:Bryan Park Pool Parking Lot @ 39.15435\,-86.523
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Nashville 90  Ride Leader:  Warren Smith
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Bicycle Club
DTSTART:20130518T140000Z
DTEND:20130518T190000Z
DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:1fq2bsru8p2b3t6tc41666bgeo@google.com
CREATED:20130228T020510Z
DESCRIPTION:This 56 mile route in Eastern Brown and Western\nBartholomew Co
 unties was listed as the “Best\nRide in Indiana” in the September 2012 issu
 e of\nBicycling Magazine.\n\n“You can ride 50 miles and see 10 cars total\,
  and\nyou can start and finish at Dag’s\, a great ice-\ncream shop with uni
 que flavors.  Try persimmon\,\nheavenly hash\, or a concoction called coffe
 e and\nbrownies.”  You be the judge on the ride and the\nice cream !\n\nThe
  route is a Figure-of-Eight crossing at Pike’s\nPeak in eastern Brown Count
 y.  Doing only the\nnorth part of the loop gives a nice short option of\nab
 out 38 miles.\n\nThis is a drive and ride.  Meet at Bryan Park at\n8:45 AM 
 to car pool or provide your own transport\nto Columbus.  Ride will depart a
 t 10:00 from the\nJay C on the west side of Columbus.\n\n<a href="http://bl
 oomingtonbicycleclub.org/maps/Special_Maps/Bicycling_Mag_East_Barth-56.pdf"
 >Best Bicycle Ride in Indiana</a>\n\n<a href="http://ridewithgps.com/routes
 /2375442">GPS</a>
LAST-MODIFIED:20230110T182413Z
LOCATION:Jay C Parking Lot\, Columbus\, IN @ 39.200238\, -85.9722
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Best Ride in Indiana   Leader: John Bassett
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
