BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Bicycle Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20221228T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20221228T203000
RRULE:FREQ=WEEKLY;WKST=SU;UNTIL=20230104T045959Z;BYDAY=WE
DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:4ah2ib1u9kb6kau6sf6b5blc6m@google.com
CREATED:20220822T224915Z
DESCRIPTION:<u></u><p><a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/41661050">Bar
 tley and Miller Ridge 12</a></p><p>Route is mostly forestry road and some s
 ingle track in Yellowwood State Forest.&nbsp\; Start at TC Steele\, ride do
 wn Bartley to Crooked Creek\, then Miller Ridge to Crooked Creek Dam\, up t
 he double back back to Miller Ride\, then back Bartley to TC Steele.&nbsp\;
  Route most suitable for MTB.</p><p>These rides feature gravel roads\, sing
 le and double track trails\,&nbsp\; and just enough pavement to string the 
 aforementioned together into fun\, woodsy adventure loops.&nbsp\; Rides beg
 in at 6PM through the Fall and Winter months as weather allows and typicall
 y last about two hours.&nbsp\; Lights are mandatory as we enter the Fall an
 d Winter seasons.</p><p>Routes are suitable for mountain bike or gravel bik
 e\, with some more turned to one or the other.&nbsp\; Rides begin at differ
 ent locations\, primarily associated with Yellowwood State Forest\, Brown C
 ounty State Park\, and the Hoosier National Forest in Monroe\, Lawrence\, a
 nd Brown Counties. &nbsp\;Specific routes may be dictated by weather condit
 ions\, but starting locations\, route maps\, and gps file links will be pos
 ted here in advance.</p><p>Expect a lot of trees and few cars.&nbsp\;&nbsp\
 ;</p><u></u>
LAST-MODIFIED:20230102T144719Z
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Bartley and Miller Ridge 12
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
