BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Bicycle Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20221207T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20221207T203000
DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:32sjplfvo35sffcd3c9kcs716p@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20221207T180000
CREATED:20220822T224915Z
DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><u></u><p>This ride starts at the Upper Handicapped 
 Hunter Parking Lot on Crooked Creek Road.&nbsp\; We take Miller Ridge and t
 he Ten O'Clock Line Trail to Brown County State Park and do the Lime Kiln t
 rail loop counterclockwise.&nbsp\; Route is suitable for MTB or gravel bike
 \, but you may be more comfortable on the MTB</p><p><a href="https://bloomi
 ngtonbicycleclub.org/maps/Gravel_Rides/Ten_O-Clock_and_Lime_Kiln_16.pdf" id
 ="ow405" __is_owner="true"><u>Ten O'Clock Line and Lime Kiln 16</u></a><br>
 </p><p><a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/40722910" id="ow409" __is_ow
 ner="true"><u>GPS Files</u></a></p><p>These rides feature gravel roads\, si
 ngle and double track trails\,&nbsp\; and just enough pavement to string th
 e aforementioned together into fun\, woodsy adventure loops.&nbsp\; Rides b
 egin at 6PM through the Fall and Winter months as weather allows and typica
 lly last about two hours.&nbsp\; Lights are mandatory as we enter the Fall 
 and Winter seasons.</p><p>Routes are suitable for mountain bike or gravel b
 ike\, with some more turned to one or the other.&nbsp\; Rides begin at diff
 erent locations\, primarily associated with Yellowwood State Forest\, Brown
  County State Park\, and the Hoosier National Forest in Monroe\, Lawrence\,
  and Brown Counties. &nbsp\;Specific routes may be dictated by weather cond
 itions\, but starting locations\, route maps\, and gps file links will be p
 osted here in advance.</p><p>Expect a lot of trees and few cars.&nbsp\;&nbs
 p\;</p><u></u></html-blob>
LAST-MODIFIED:20230102T144559Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Ten O'Clock Line and Lime Kiln 16 - Off Road Adventure Ride
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
