CREATED:20090930T215724Z
DESCRIPTION:The Bucket 100 is a bike ride that starts at Purdue and ends at
  IU.  The riders will leave Saturday morning (the 7th) for Purdue\, stay ov
 ernight in Purdue's provided housing\, and wake up early Sunday to ride bac
 k to IU where food will be provided.  During the ride\, there will be stops
  and food/water available.\n\nRegistration is $40 a rider.  That includes t
 he overnight stay\, food\, transportation to Purdue\, and a long-sleeved T-
 shirt.\n\nWe also ask riders to find sponsors who can donate to Habitat for
  Humanity.  All donations go towards building and sponsoring a Habitat home
  in Monroe County.  While finding a sponsor is not required to participate 
 in the event\, it is encouraged and appreciated.\n\nTo register\, riders ca
 n go to this website:  \nhttp://www.active.com/event_detail.cfm?event_id=17
 97108
LAST-MODIFIED:20230110T182848Z
LOCATION:Purdue University\; West Lafayette
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Habitat for Humanity Bucket 100
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
CATEGORIES:http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#event
END:VEVENT
