BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Bicycle Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230121T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20230121T140000
DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:76goke0o1n3k5j8qk81fu0sg83@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20230121T100000
CREATED:20220901T172010Z
DESCRIPTION:<p><span>This 30 mile ride starts at the Dam at Yellowwood and 
 heads up Dubois <i><u>Ridge</u></i> Road\, across Lanam <i><u>Ridge</u></i>
  and drops down Salmeron and Indian <i><u>Hill</u></i> to get to SR45.  Fro
 m there we'll head up Carmel <i><u>Ridge</u></i> Road\, loop around Waycros
 s and drop back down to North Shore\, South Shore\, climb back up to Lanam 
 <i><u>Ridge</u></i> before enjoying a nice down hill back to the dam.</span
 ><br></p><p>Seeing a theme here?  You get the idea.</p><p>Saturday is going
  to be another gorgeous day so hope to see you all there.</p><p><a href="ht
 tps://ridewithgps.com/routes/41824705">Up Up and aWaycross</a><br></p><p>Th
 ese rides feature gravel roads\, single and double track trails\,  and just
  enough pavement to string the aforementioned together into fun\, woodsy ad
 venture loops.  Rides begin at 10am through the Fall and Winter months as w
 eather allows and typically last about three to four hours.</p><p>Routes ar
 e suitable for mountain bike or gravel bike\, with some more turned to one 
 or the other.  Rides begin at different locations\, primarily associated wi
 th Yellowwood State Forest\, Brown County State Park\, and the Hoosier Nati
 onal Forest in Monroe\, Lawrence\, and Brown Counties.  Specific routes may
  be dictated by weather conditions\, but starting locations\, route maps\, 
 and gps file links will be posted here in advance.</p><p>Expect a lot of tr
 ees and few cars.</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20230120T155705Z
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Up Up and aWaycross - Off Road Adventure
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Bicycle Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230829T174500
