DESCRIPTION:<a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/39638841">26 Southshore
  Shuffle</a><br><br>Please observe social distancing norms as we gather and
  ride. <ul><li>Be SAFE. Don't blow through stop signs. Consider bike lights
 .<br></li><li>Be COURTEOUS: Single up in traffic<br></li><li>Be PREDICTABLE
 : Signal your intentions to cars and fellow riders.</li></ul>The "Older\, W
 iser\, and a Little Slower" training group emphasizes moderate rides\, and 
 a route planned in advance that is posted on the ride calendar. This is a n
 o drop ride\, but not a beginner's ride.The OWLS group welcomes a wide rang
 e of intermediate riders\, and typically breaks off into a faster and slowe
 r group with the former averaging an overall moving speed of 16-18 mph\, an
 d the slower group averaging 13-15 mph (including hills). Distances vary fr
 om 20 to 30 miles\, depending partly on available light. Early season rides
  will be somewhat shorter and slower. Rides depart promptly at 5:45.<br><br
 >Non-members should sign up for a <a href="https://secure.getmeregistered.c
 om/get_information.php?event_id=136627"><u>free trial membership</u></a>\, 
 good for up to three rides\, and which includes electronically signing a li
 ability waiver\, prior to participation.<br><br>Questions? Contact <a href=
 "mailto:gail.morell@gmail.com"><u>Gail Morell</u></a>.
