BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Bicycle Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230906T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20230906T203000
DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:3h1ht7sn6m0fusnrfvjqc9342k@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20230906T180000
CREATED:20230814T185924Z
DESCRIPTION:<p><span>Ride starts at the Upper Handicapped Hunter Parking Lo
 t on Crooked Creek Road.  We take Miller Ridge and the Ten O'Clock Line Tra
 il to Brown County State Park and do the Lime Kiln trail loop counterclockw
 ise.  Route is suitable for MTB or gravel bike\, but you may be more comfor
 table on the MTB</span><br></p><a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/4072
 2910">Ten O'Clock and Lime Kiln 16</a><br><br><span>These rides feature gra
 vel roads\, single and double track trails\,  and just enough pavement to s
 tring the aforementioned together into fun\, woodsy adventure loops.  Rides
  begin at 6PM through the Fall and Winter months as weather allows and typi
 cally last about two hours.  Lights are mandatory as we enter the Fall and 
 Winter seasons.</span><p>Routes are suitable for mountain bike or gravel bi
 ke\, with some more turned to one or the other.  Rides begin at different l
 ocations\, primarily associated with Yellowwood State Forest\, Brown County
  State Park\, and the Hoosier National Forest in Monroe\, Lawrence\, and Br
 own Counties.  Specific routes may be dictated by weather conditions\, but 
 starting locations\, route maps\, and gps file links will be posted here in
  advance.</p><p>Expect a lot of trees and few cars</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20230914T170844Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Ten O'Clock Line and Lime Kiln 16 - Off Road Adventure Ride
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
