DESCRIPTION:<a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/39128059">Leonard Sprin
 gs Ison Loop Revised April 19\, 2022</a><br><br>Please observe social dista
 ncing norms as we gather and ride. <ul><li>Be SAFE. Don't blow through stop
  signs. Consider bike lights.<br></li><li>Be COURTEOUS: Single up in traffi
 c<br></li><li>Be PREDICTABLE: Signal your intentions to cars and fellow rid
 ers.</li></ul>The "Older\, Wiser\, and a Little Slower" training group emph
 asizes moderate rides\, and a route planned in advance that is posted on th
 e ride calendar. This is a no drop ride\, but not a beginner's ride.The OWL
 S group welcomes a wide range of intermediate riders\, and typically breaks
  off into a faster and slower group with the former averaging an overall mo
 ving speed of 16-18 mph\, and the slower group averaging 13-15 mph (includi
 ng hills). Distances vary from 20 to 30 miles\, depending partly on availab
 le light. Early season rides will be somewhat shorter and slower. Rides dep
 art promptly at 5:45.<br><br>Non-members should sign up for a <a href="http
 s://secure.getmeregistered.com/get_information.php?event_id=136627"><u>free
  trial membership</u></a>\, good for up to three rides\, and which includes
  electronically signing a liability waiver\, prior to participation.<br><br
 >Questions? Contact <a href="mailto:gail.morell@gmail.com"><u>Gail Morell</
 u></a>.
