BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Bicycle Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240203T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20240203T143000
DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:5mu5cn4ulv9saduakntkumeqne@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20240203T100000
CREATED:20231017T184315Z
DESCRIPTION:<p>This ride will start/finish at the Bloomington Yacht Club.</
 p><p>This is a shorter ride for a Saturday at 23 miles but has some punchy 
 climbs\,\,\, I don't think many of us got much riding in this past month.  
 Weather is looking fantastic and we can hit the Port Hole when we're done r
 iding.</p><p>Many thanks to the Bloomington Yacht Club for letting us park 
 there!</p><p><a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/45185257">Sail aWaycro
 ss · Ride with GPS</a><br></p><p><br></p><p>These rides feature gravel road
 s\, single and double track trails\,  and just enough pavement to string th
 e aforementioned together into fun\, woodsy adventure loops.  Rides begin a
 t 10am through the Fall and Winter months as weather allows and typically l
 ast about three to four hours.</p><p>Routes are suitable for mountain bike 
 or gravel bike\, with some more turned to one or the other.  Rides begin at
  different locations\, primarily associated with Yellowwood State Forest\, 
 Brown County State Park\, and the Hoosier National Forest in Monroe\, Lawre
 nce\, and Brown Counties.  Specific routes may be dictated by weather condi
 tions\, but starting locations\, route maps\, and gps file links will be po
 sted here in advance.</p><p>Expect a lot of trees and few cars</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20240202T003444Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Sail aWaycross - Off Road Adventure Ride
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
