 ee rides\, and which includes electronically signing a liability waiver\, p
 rior to participation.<ul><li>Be SAFE. Don't blow through stop signs. Consi
 der bike lights.<br></li><li>Be COURTEOUS: Single up in traffic<br></li><li
 >Be PREDICTABLE: Signal your intentions to cars and fellow riders.</li></ul
 >The "Older\, Wiser\, and a Little Slower" training group emphasizes modera
 te rides\, and a route planned in advance that is posted on the ride calend
 ar. This is a no drop ride\, but not a beginner's ride.The OWLS group welco
 mes a wide range of intermediate riders\, and typically breaks off into a f
 aster and slower group with the former averaging an overall moving speed of
  16-18 mph\, and the slower group averaging 13-15 mph (including hills). Di
 stances vary from 20 to 30 miles\, depending partly on available light. Ear
 ly season rides will be somewhat shorter and slower. Rides depart promptly 
 at 5:45.<br><br>Questions? Contact <a href="mailto:gail.morell@gmail.com" t
 arget="_blank"><u>Gail Morell</u></a>.
