X-SOURCE:Bloomington Bicycle Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230727T174500
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20230727T204500
DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:1v04bd50vmk9nh42ouber307fk@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20230727T174500
CREATED:20230518T113658Z
DESCRIPTION:<a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/39702120">Triple Creek<
 /a><br><br>Please observe social distancing norms as we gather and ride. <u
 l><li>Be SAFE. Don't blow through stop signs. Consider bike lights.<br></li
 ><li>Be COURTEOUS: Single up in traffic<br></li><li>Be PREDICTABLE: Signal 
 your intentions to cars and fellow riders.</li></ul>The "Older\, Wiser\, an
 d a Little Slower" training group emphasizes moderate rides\, and a route p
 lanned in advance that is posted on the ride calendar. This is a no drop ri
 de\, but not a beginner's ride.The OWLS group welcomes a wide range of inte
 rmediate riders\, and typically breaks off into a faster and slower group w
 ith the former averaging an overall moving speed of 16-18 mph\, and the slo
 wer group averaging 13-15 mph (including hills). Distances vary from 20 to 
 30 miles\, depending partly on available light. Early season rides will be 
 somewhat shorter and slower. Rides depart promptly at 5:45.<br><br>Non-memb
 ers should sign up for a <a href="https://secure.getmeregistered.com/get_in
 formation.php?event_id=136627"><u>free trial membership</u></a>\, good for 
 up to three rides\, and which includes electronically signing a liability w
 aiver\, prior to participation.<br><br>Questions? Contact <a href="mailto:g
 ail.morell@gmail.com"><u>Gail Morell</u></a>.
LAST-MODIFIED:20230703T170114Z
LOCATION:Sherwood Oaks Christian Church\, 2700 E Rogers Rd\, Bloomington\, 
 IN 47401\, USA
SEQUENCE:2
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:OWLS Ride - 26 Triple Creek
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Bicycle Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20240302T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20240302T143000
DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:5mu5cn4ulv9saduakntkumeqne@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20240302T100000
CREATED:20231017T184315Z
DESCRIPTION:<p><a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/45722250">2024 Death
  March Practice 35 · Ride with GPS</a><br></p><p>Meet at the Fire Tower</p>
 <p>These rides feature gravel roads\, single and double track trails\,  and
  just enough pavement to string the aforementioned together into fun\, wood
 sy adventure loops.  Rides begin at 10am through the Fall and Winter months
  as weather allows and typically last about three to four hours.</p><p>Rout
 es are suitable for mountain bike or gravel bike\, with some more turned to
  one or the other.  Rides begin at different locations\, primarily associat
 ed with Yellowwood State Forest\, Brown County State Park\, and the Hoosier
  National Forest in Monroe\, Lawrence\, and Brown Counties.  Specific route
 s may be dictated by weather conditions\, but starting locations\, route ma
 ps\, and gps file links will be posted here in advance.</p><p>Expect a lot 
 of trees and few cars</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20240229T165014Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Death March Practice 35 - Off Road Adventure Ride
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
