CREATED:20231017T184315Z
DESCRIPTION:<span>Join us for a jaunt along mostly </span><span>gravel road
 s following about one-half </span><span>of the course of the Gravel </span>
 <span>Grovel Dino Race.  There is a short </span><span>section of easy sing
 le track along </span><span>Trail 21 in the HNF. </span><br><span><br></spa
 n>Patrick Kelly will be leading this ride - Thanks Patrick!<br><br>Ride sta
 rts/ends at Hickory Ridge fire tower on Tower Ridge Road.<br><br>Suitable f
 or gravel and cyclocross bikes plus MTB so ride what you've got!<br><br>Sho
 rter routes are available. <br><br>Ride leaves from the fire tower promptly
  at 10:00AM<br><br><a href="http://bloomingtonbicycleclub.org/maps/Gravel_R
 ides/About%20Half%20of%20the%20Gravel%20Grovel%2032.pdf"><u>About Half of t
 he Gravel Grovel 32</u></a><a></a><br><br><a href="https://ridewithgps.com/
 routes/17721734"><u>GPS Files</u></a><p>These rides feature gravel roads\, 
 single and double track trails\,  and just enough pavement to string the af
 orementioned together into fun\, woodsy adventure loops.  Rides begin at 10
 am through the Fall and Winter months as weather allows and typically last 
 about three to four hours.</p><p>Routes are suitable for mountain bike or g
 ravel bike\, with some more turned to one or the other.  Rides begin at dif
 ferent locations\, primarily associated with Yellowwood State Forest\, Brow
 n County State Park\, and the Hoosier National Forest in Monroe\, Lawrence\
 , and Brown Counties.  Specific routes may be dictated by weather condition
 s\, but starting locations\, route maps\, and gps file links will be posted
  here in advance.</p><p>Expect a lot of trees and few cars</p>
