CREATED:20220901T172010Z
DESCRIPTION:<p>Hi Everyone\, this is the last official Off Road ride of the
  season.</p><p>Changing up the route for this week as the original route to
  BCSP via Ten O Clock will be a mess with all the rain.</p><p>Hoping to avo
 id most of the winds on Saturday by staying in the woods.  voiding trails\,
  sticking to Gravel &amp\; Pavement.  I'll check Lake Monroe pool level aga
 in in the morning - McGowan floods at about 543'\, we're at 539 today so lo
 oks OK right now.</p><p><a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/42326749">B
 ond Out Sewel back</a><br></p><p><u><b>6PM on SUNDAY</b></u> - weather perm
 itting (looks good at the mo) Alison and I plan to have a fire going in the
  yard and a big pot of chili.  We'd love to see you and hear your tall stor
 ies from the season.</p><p>Thanks for an awesome season.  Stay safe on the 
 roads.</p><p>Rob</p><p>These rides feature gravel roads\, single and double
  track trails\,  and just enough pavement to string the aforementioned toge
 ther into fun\, woodsy adventure loops.  Rides begin at 10am through the Fa
 ll and Winter months as weather allows and typically last about three to fo
 ur hours.</p><p>Routes are suitable for mountain bike or gravel bike\, with
  some more turned to one or the other.  Rides begin at different locations\
 , primarily associated with Yellowwood State Forest\, Brown County State Pa
 rk\, and the Hoosier National Forest in Monroe\, Lawrence\, and Brown Count
 ies.  Specific routes may be dictated by weather conditions\, but starting 
 locations\, route maps\, and gps file links will be posted here in advance.
 </p><p>Expect a lot of trees and few cars.</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20230324T192535Z
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Bond Out Sewel Back - Off Road Adventure
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
