DESCRIPTION:Clips of Faith: Film\, Bike\, and Beer Festival\, Friday\, June
  8\, 8:00 -11:00 pm (first film begins at dark)\, Bryan Park\n\n<a href="ht
 tp://simplycsl.org/clips-of-faith/">Clips of Faith Website</a>\n\nDescripti
 on: New Belgium Brewing hosts Clips of Faith\, a beer-toting\, film-traveli
 ng\, nonprofit-benefiting show that's coming to 18 cities coast-to-coast\, 
 including Bloomington this Friday!\n\nYou'll get to try New Belgium's most 
 esoteric beer offerings - up to 16 varieties on tap! - and pair them with i
 nspiring short films created by fans.  Proceeds from beer sales benefit the
  Center for Sustainable Living (our parent organization). Food will be avai
 lable from Happy Pig and Feast Bakery Cafe. Visit the Clips of Faith websit
 e for more information.
LAST-MODIFIED:20230110T182947Z
LOCATION:Bryan Park @ 39.156171\, -86.525605
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Beer\, Bike and Film Festival
TRANSP:OPAQUE
CATEGORIES:http://schemas.google.com/g/2005#event
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Bicycle Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230225T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20230225T140000
DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:76goke0o1n3k5j8qk81fu0sg83@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20230225T100000
CREATED:20220901T172010Z
DESCRIPTION:<p>This 32 mile ride will start at the Hickory Ridge Fire Tower
 \, and visit the old Combs 'Road' - we've not been up there for a couple of
  years\, let's go check it out.</p><p>Most suited to MTB but gravel / cross
  bike will work too.</p><p><a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/42031988
 ">Up Combs to Story</a></p><p>These rides feature gravel roads\, single and
  double track trails\,  and just enough pavement to string the aforemention
 ed together into fun\, woodsy adventure loops.  Rides begin at 10am through
  the Fall and Winter months as weather allows and typically last about thre
 e to four hours.</p><p>Routes are suitable for mountain bike or gravel bike
 \, with some more turned to one or the other.  Rides begin at different loc
 ations\, primarily associated with Yellowwood State Forest\, Brown County S
 tate Park\, and the Hoosier National Forest in Monroe\, Lawrence\, and Brow
 n Counties.  Specific routes may be dictated by weather conditions\, but st
 arting locations\, route maps\, and gps file links will be posted here in a
 dvance.</p><p>Expect a lot of trees and few cars.</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20230220T161915Z
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Up Combs to Story - Off Road Adventure
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
