DESCRIPTION:<p>I've shamelessly plagiarized a route put together by Marc O'
 Leary from Elevate Endurance that starts/ends in Freedom.  The route is pre
 dominantly gravel with a nice mix of hills\, flats\, wooded areas\, and fie
 lds.</p><p><span>Will be hard to not stop in Civilian Brew Co on the way ba
 ck</span></p><p><a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/42258903">Freedom 3
 3</a><br></p><p><br></p><p>These rides feature gravel roads\, single and do
 uble track trails\,  and just enough pavement to string the aforementioned 
 together into fun\, woodsy adventure loops.  Rides begin at 10am through th
 e Fall and Winter months as weather allows and typically last about three t
 o four hours.</p><p>Routes are suitable for mountain bike or gravel bike\, 
 with some more turned to one or the other.  Rides begin at different locati
 ons\, primarily associated with Yellowwood State Forest\, Brown County Stat
 e Park\, and the Hoosier National Forest in Monroe\, Lawrence\, and Brown C
 ounties.  Specific routes may be dictated by weather conditions\, but start
 ing locations\, route maps\, and gps file links will be posted here in adva
 nce.</p><p>Expect a lot of trees and few cars</p>
