BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Bicycle Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20241127T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20241127T203000
DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:4j1jbb2vm9a75jr1era2ihg9rd@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20241120T180000
CREATED:20241113T190324Z
DESCRIPTION:<p><b>Ride will leave from the Blackwell Horse Camp on Tower Ri
 dge Road at 6:00PM</b><br><u></u></p><p>This route is mostly gravel with ab
 out two miles of easy double track on HNF Trail 19\, and a short section of
  pavement on the east side from Maumee to the Boy Scout Camp.</p><p>Route i
 s suitable for CX\, MTB\, or Gravel bikes.<br><b>  </b><br><span>BRING LIGH
 TS</span></p><p><a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://ridewithgps.c
 om/routes/10147577&amp\;sa=D&amp\;source=calendar&amp\;usd=2&amp\;usg=AOvVa
 w38m75gAMWGIF-QcK7Y3l0L" target="_blank"><u><u>Blackwell Loop to HNF Trail 
 19</u></u></a></p><p><span>These rides feature gravel roads\, single and do
 uble track trails\,  and just enough pavement to string the aforementioned 
 together into fun\, woodsy adventure loops.  Rides begin at 6PM through the
  Fall and Winter months as weather allows and typically last about two hour
 s. Lights are mandatory as we enter the Fall and Winter seasons.</span></p>
 <p>Routes are suitable for mountain bike or gravel bike\, with some more tu
 rned to one or the other.  Rides begin at different locations\, primarily a
 ssociated with Yellowwood State Forest\, Brown County State Park\, and the 
 Hoosier National Forest in Monroe\, Lawrence\, and Brown Counties. Specific
  routes may be dictated by weather conditions\, but starting locations\, ro
 ute maps\, and gps file links will be posted here in advance.</p><p>Expect 
 a lot of trees and few cars</p><p>Non-members should sign up for a <a href=
 "https://www.google.com/url?q=https://secure.getmeregistered.com/get_inform
 ation.php?event_id%3D136627&amp\;sa=D&amp\;source=calendar&amp\;usd=2&amp\;
 usg=AOvVaw2vXJF5e7ex4tSNc8E8efrb" target="_blank">free trial membership</a>
 \, good for up to three rides\, and which includes electronically signing a
  liability waiver\, prior to participation.</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20241119T010542Z
SEQUENCE:3
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Blackwell & Trail 19 - Growlers Off Road Adventure Rides
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
