DESCRIPTION:<a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/46576300">26- OWLS Shuf
 fle Creek</a><br><br>I Ride Extension:  31 - OWLS Shuffle Creek:<br><br><a 
 href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/46559568" target="_blank">https://ride
 withgps.com/routes/46559568</a><br><br><br>Non-members should sign up for a
  <a href="https://secure.getmeregistered.com/get_information.php?event_id=1
 36627" target="_blank"><u><u>free trial membership</u></u></a>\, good for u
 p to three rides\, and which includes electronically signing a liability wa
 iver\, prior to participation.<ul><li>Be SAFE. Don't blow through stop sign
 s. Consider bike lights.<br></li><li>Be COURTEOUS: Single up in traffic<br>
 </li><li>Be PREDICTABLE: Signal your intentions to cars and fellow riders.<
 /li></ul>The "Older\, Wiser\, and a Little Slower" training group emphasize
 s moderate rides\, and a route planned in advance that is posted on the rid
 e calendar. This is a no drop ride\, but not a beginner's ride.The OWLS gro
 up welcomes a wide range of intermediate riders\, and typically breaks off 
 into a faster and slower group with the former averaging an overall moving 
 speed of 16-18 mph\, and the slower group averaging 13-15 mph (including hi
 lls). Distances vary from 20 to 30 miles\, depending partly on available li
 ght. Early season rides will be somewhat shorter and slower. Rides depart p
 romptly at 5:45.<br><br>Questions? Contact <a href="mailto:gail.morell@gmai
 l.com" target="_blank"><u>Gail Morell</u></a>.
