DESCRIPTION:This will be our inaugural "Family Ride". The\nroute is multipl
 e choice\, but all the answers are\nright and you can fill the bubbles in w
 ith ice\ncream and playgrounds.\n\nI have invited the BBC list e-mail and e
 veryone\nwho requested that I notify them in the Family\nRide survey. Futur
 e Family Rides will be added\nto the calendar\, but will not be broadcast t
 his way. \n\nJoin the ride at one of several points\, to get the\ntype of r
 ide you want. Options range from almost\n4 miles round trip to not quite 3.
  Riders of all ages\nand abilities are welcome. Just pick a park on the\nli
 st to start from. I anticipate each leg being\nprogressively slower as we a
 dd younger\nindependent riders.\n\nTentative schedule:\n\nLeave Butler park
  at 2:00pm (Andrew Dingman)\n            I will be wearing black shorts and
  a day-glow highlighter-yellow jersey.\n            My daughter will be wit
 h me on a silver and red recumbent tandem\n            trailer.\n\nLeave Br
 yan park at 2:25pm (Marty Schick)\n            If any wants to know who to 
 look for\, we are the grandparent figures.\n            I am riding a Trek 
 Pilot (hot pink) and my hubby is on a Cannondale\n            (patriotic...
 American flag).\n\nLeave Park Ridge park at 2:50pm (Tammy Thompson)\n      
       Tammy hasn't provided a description\, but I think more of the club kn
 ow\n            her than the rest of us. Worst case\, look for Andrew and M
 arty\, and we'll\n            find Tammy \;-)\n\nArrive at Brusters at 3:10
 pm\n\nI've mapped out two possible routes. The first\nis slightly more scen
 ic\, but crosses 46 without\na light. <a href="http://bit.ly/1jk5QH9">Route
  1</a>\n\nThe second is slightly less scenic\, but crosses\n46 with a traff
 ic light. We'll decide which to use \nbased on the comfort level of the par
 ents\nleaving Bryan Park.<a href="http://bit.ly/Scu7EL">Route 2 </a>
LAST-MODIFIED:20250326T215043Z
LOCATION:Butler Park -> Bryan Park -> Park Ridge Park -> Bruster's @ 39.170
 463\, -86.542914
SEQUENCE:5
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Family Ride: Multiple Choice Ice Cream Run
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
