DESCRIPTION:<span>Hi Everyone\, camping opportunity so keep an eye on the w
 eather.</span><br><span><br></span><br><span>Couple of club members plannin
 g on camping at Yellowwood for the night.</span><br><span>We&#39\;ll get a 
 fire going and have a pot of chilli on the go.  Bring a snack to share and 
 your favorite beverage.</span><br><span><br>Bring lights!!<br></span><br><a
  href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://ridewithgps.com/routes/44787302
 &amp\;sa=D&amp\;source=calendar&amp\;usd=2&amp\;usg=AOvVaw3vwAuozi1MwZdnTZo
 SuYdw" target="_blank">All Around Yellowwood from Campground</a><span><br><
 /span><br><span>These rides feature gravel roads\, single and double track 
 trails\,  and just enough pavement to string the aforementioned together in
 to fun\, woodsy adventure loops.  Rides begin at 6PM through the Fall and W
 inter months as weather allows and typically last about two hours.  Lights 
 are mandatory as we enter the Fall and Winter seasons.</span><p>Routes are 
 suitable for mountain bike or gravel bike\, with some more turned to one or
  the other.  Rides begin at different locations\, primarily associated with
  Yellowwood State Forest\, Brown County State Park\, and the Hoosier Nation
 al Forest in Monroe\, Lawrence\, and Brown Counties.  Specific routes may b
 e dictated by weather conditions\, but starting locations\, route maps\, an
 d gps file links will be posted here in advance.</p><p>Expect a lot of tree
 s and few cars</p>
