DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:3cvgbvfm30ojdcave0hi46pch3@google.com
CREATED:20241119T020427Z
DESCRIPTION:This 20-miler begins at the Blackwell Horse Camp on Tower Ridge
  Road\, heads to Hickory Grove Church\, and then circles back to the horse 
 camp via McPike Branch Road and Dutch Ridge Road.  The route is predominate
 ly gravel with a little bit of pavement\, and no trail.  Route is suitable 
 for CX\, gravel bike\, or MTB.<span><br></span><br><a href="https://www.goo
 gle.com/url?q=https://ridewithgps.com/routes/18155202&amp\;sa=D&amp\;source
 =calendar&amp\;usd=2&amp\;usg=AOvVaw2TO3PXSJ6BwQaB80AJFMAm" target="_blank"
 >All Around Yellowstone 20 </a><span><br></span><br><span>Bring Lights!<br>
 </span><br><span>These rides feature gravel roads\, single and double track
  trails\,  and just enough pavement to string the aforementioned together i
 nto fun\, woodsy adventure loops.  Rides begin at 6PM through the Fall and 
 Winter months as weather allows and typically last about two hours.  Lights
  are mandatory as we enter the Fall and Winter seasons.</span><p>Routes are
  suitable for mountain bike or gravel bike\, with some more turned to one o
 r the other.  Rides begin at different locations\, primarily associated wit
 h Yellowwood State Forest\, Brown County State Park\, and the Hoosier Natio
 nal Forest in Monroe\, Lawrence\, and Brown Counties.  Specific routes may 
 be dictated by weather conditions\, but starting locations\, route maps\, a
 nd gps file links will be posted here in advance.</p><p>Expect a lot of tre
 es and few cars</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20241119T020558Z
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:All Around Yellowstone - Off Road Adventure Ride
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
