RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20230315T180000
CREATED:20220822T224915Z
DESCRIPTION:<u></u><br><span><br>This ride starts at the Upper Handicapped 
 Hunter Parking Lot on Crooked Creek Road.  We take Miller Ridge and the Ten
  O'Clock Line Trail to Brown County State Park and do the Lime Kiln trail l
 oop counterclockwise.  Route is suitable for MTB or gravel bike\, but you m
 ay be more comfortable on the MTB</span><br><u></u><p><a href="https://bloo
 mingtonbicycleclub.org/maps/Gravel_Rides/Ten_O-Clock_and_Lime_Kiln_16.pdf">
 <u><u>Ten O'Clock Line and Lime Kiln 16</u></u></a><br></p><p><a href="http
 s://ridewithgps.com/routes/40722910"><u><u>GPS Files</u></u></a></p><p>Thes
 e rides feature gravel roads\, single and double track trails\,  and just e
 nough pavement to string the aforementioned together into fun\, woodsy adve
 nture loops.  Rides begin at 6PM through the Fall and Winter months as weat
 her allows and typically last about two hours.  Lights are mandatory as we 
 enter the Fall and Winter seasons.</p><p>Routes are suitable for mountain b
 ike or gravel bike\, with some more turned to one or the other.  Rides begi
 n at different locations\, primarily associated with Yellowwood State Fores
 t\, Brown County State Park\, and the Hoosier National Forest in Monroe\, L
 awrence\, and Brown Counties.  Specific routes may be dictated by weather c
 onditions\, but starting locations\, route maps\, and gps file links will b
 e posted here in advance.</p><p>Expect a lot of trees and few cars.  </p><u
 ></u>
LAST-MODIFIED:20230313T125455Z
