BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Bicycle Club
DTSTART:20230603T130000Z
DTEND:20230603T190000Z
DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:2a5bc2d121a9ltmj6amusnupdr@google.com
CREATED:20230531T122915Z
DESCRIPTION:<u></u><u></u>This is a beautiful ride with challenging hills d
 own to the historic Williams Covered Bridge on the East Fork White River.  
 The traditional route is here:<br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/url?q
 =http://www.bloomingtonbicycleclub.org/maps/BBCMaps/map_pack_1/williams_bri
 dge.pdf&amp\;sa=D&amp\;source=calendar&amp\;usd=2&amp\;usg=AOvVaw2yOYV1EnR9
 wjf_xuWKoCef" target="_blank">Williams Covered Bridge</a><br><br>Recently\,
  we have utilized an alternate route to Williams following the Milwaukee Tr
 ail (a neat\, privately-built stone dust rail trail)  southwest from Bedfor
 d to Williams\, and an alternate route back to Fayetteville from Williams o
 n Ridge Road.  We throw in another rail trail (the new Limestone Trail) con
 necting Dillman Road and Church Lane near the end of the ride.  The complet
 e route for Saturday is here: <br><br><a href="https://www.google.com/url?q
 =https://ridewithgps.com/routes/31015951&amp\;sa=D&amp\;source=calendar&amp
 \;usd=2&amp\;usg=AOvVaw37tCwgD11FNAMVtJY5I-QR" target="_blank">GPS File</a>
 <br><br>The complete Milwaukee Trail from Bedford to Williams is about 10 m
 iles.  The trail is a little shorter than the road route to Williams\, and 
 is substantially less hilly.  It is a little slower due to the the crushed 
 stone surface\, but presents little problem for a normal road bike. <br><br
 >Of course\, you can always opt to do the traditional route via road from B
 edford to Williams\, and skip the Milwaukee Trail.  We just all meet at the
  covered bridge!<u></u><br><u></u><br><u></u><br><u></u>Non-members should 
 sign up for a <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://secure.getmereg
 istered.com/get_information.php?event_id%3D136627&amp\;sa=D&amp\;source=cal
 endar&amp\;usd=2&amp\;usg=AOvVaw0_5cJvz8z3KUY7Yt6t47kW" target="_blank"><u>
 free trial membership</u></a>\, good for up to three rides\, and which incl
 udes electronically signing a liability waiver\, prior to participation. <b
 r><u></u><u></u>
