DESCRIPTION:<a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/43956496">Swartz Ridge 
 and Cutright Boat Ramp</a><br><a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/43956
 496"></a><br>Please observe social distancing norms as we gather and ride. 
 <ul><li>Be SAFE. Don't blow through stop signs. Consider bike lights.<br></
 li><li>Be COURTEOUS: Single up in traffic<br></li><li>Be PREDICTABLE: Signa
 l your intentions to cars and fellow riders.</li></ul>The "Older\, Wiser\, 
 and a Little Slower" training group emphasizes moderate rides\, and a route
  planned in advance that is posted on the ride calendar. This is a no drop 
 ride\, but not a beginner's ride.The OWLS group welcomes a wide range of in
 termediate riders\, and typically breaks off into a faster and slower group
  with the former averaging an overall moving speed of 16-18 mph\, and the s
 lower group averaging 13-15 mph (including hills). Distances vary from 20 t
 o 30 miles\, depending partly on available light. Early season rides will b
 e somewhat shorter and slower. Rides depart promptly at 5:45.<br><br>Non-me
 mbers should sign up for a <a href="https://secure.getmeregistered.com/get_
 information.php?event_id=136627"><u>free trial membership</u></a>\, good fo
 r up to three rides\, and which includes electronically signing a liability
  waiver\, prior to participation.<br><br>Questions? Contact <a href="mailto
 :gail.morell@gmail.com"><u>Gail Morell</u></a>.
