DESCRIPTION:<a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/29496732">18 - Ramp Cre
 ek and Scott Rd.</a><br><br>23 - Ramp Creek and Scott Rd - I ride extension
 <br><br><a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/45857064">https://ridewithg
 ps.com/routes/45857064</a><br><br>Non-members should sign up for a <a href=
 "https://secure.getmeregistered.com/get_information.php?event_id=136627"><u
 ><u>free trial membership</u></u></a>\, good for up to three rides\, and wh
 ich includes electronically signing a liability waiver\, prior to participa
 tion.<ul><li>Be SAFE. Don't blow through stop signs. Consider bike lights.<
 br></li><li>Be COURTEOUS: Single up in traffic<br></li><li>Be PREDICTABLE: 
 Signal your intentions to cars and fellow riders.</li></ul>The "Older\, Wis
 er\, and a Little Slower" training group emphasizes moderate rides\, and a 
 route planned in advance that is posted on the ride calendar. This is a no 
 drop ride\, but not a beginner's ride.The OWLS group welcomes a wide range 
 of intermediate riders\, and typically breaks off into a faster and slower 
 group with the former averaging an overall moving speed of 16-18 mph\, and 
 the slower group averaging 13-15 mph (including hills). Distances vary from
  20 to 30 miles\, depending partly on available light. Early season rides w
 ill be somewhat shorter and slower. Rides depart promptly at 5:45.<br><br>Q
 uestions? Contact <a href="mailto:gail.morell@gmail.com"><u>Gail Morell</u>
 </a>.
