DESCRIPTION:<u></u><u></u><u></u><p><a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=h
 ttps://bloomingtonbicycleclub.org/maps/John_Bassett_Maps/Joes_Cemetery_Ride
 _74.pdf&amp\;sa=D&amp\;source=calendar&amp\;usd=2&amp\;usg=AOvVaw3Gv2PyNcpW
 p4jikR03hdRj" target="_blank">Joe&#39\;s Cemetery Ride 74</a></p><p><a href
 ="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://ridewithgps.com/routes/40876564&amp\
 ;sa=D&amp\;source=calendar&amp\;usd=2&amp\;usg=AOvVaw25TtkHUBuf-bKoF_hqea9F
 " target="_blank">GPS Files</a><br></p><br>The past two years the BBC Septe
 mber Cemetery Ride was held on the anniversary of the 09 / 11 attack. This 
 year we are off by one day\, but it’s still appropriate to honor the memory
  of the first responders and the nearly three thousand civilians who lost t
 heir lives that day.<br><br>The route is slightly altered this year to use 
 less traveled and newly paved Mt Gilead to Unionville and Egbert / Morgan S
 t / Ohio St going into Martinsville.<p>Services are available at miles 28 a
 nd 50 of the route.</p><p>Non-members should sign up for a <a href="https:/
 /www.google.com/url?q=https://secure.getmeregistered.com/get_information.ph
 p?event_id%3D136627&amp\;sa=D&amp\;source=calendar&amp\;usd=2&amp\;usg=AOvV
 aw0_5cJvz8z3KUY7Yt6t47kW" target="_blank">free trial membership</a>\, good 
 for up to three rides\, and which includes electronically signing a liabili
 ty waiver\, prior to participation.  <br></p><u></u><u></u><u></u>
LAST-MODIFIED:20230829T193707Z
