DESCRIPTION:<u></u><a href="https://www.bloomingtonbicycleclub.org/maps/BBC
 Maps/map_pack_2/low_gap_touchables.pdf">Low Gap to Martinsville ("The Touch
 ables")</a><br><br><a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/28325235">GPS Fi
 les</a><br><br><a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/43935893">GPS Files-
  Alternate Route</a><br><br>51 moderate miles with a 26 mile short option. 
  This route takes riders through Morgan Monroe State Forest and past "The T
 ouchables" Sculpture Garden.  Consider coasting and taking a gander at the 
 unique pieces scattered on the west side of the road.<br><br>We will take t
 he new Old 37 connector on the east side of I-69 from the Liberty Church in
 terchange down to Old 37\, more or less duplicating the original mapping of
  this ride.  But\, you always have the option to spice up your life and tak
 e Hacker Creek Road back to Forest Road junction.  Of course\, that means c
 limbing the infamous Hacker Creek Hill.<br><br>An alternate route is added 
 for a less traveled roads option instead of 45.  Kerr Creek to Getty's Cree
 k to Mt. Gilead.  It adds a few miles and a little climbing but includes ne
 w pavement and beautiful scenery.  <br><br>Non-members should sign up for a
  <a href="https://secure.getmeregistered.com/get_information.php?event_id=1
 36627">free trial membership</a>\, good for up to three rides\, and which i
 ncludes electronically signing a liability waiver\, prior to participation.
 <u></u>
