BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Bicycle Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20231115T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20231115T203000
DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:3h1ht7sn6m0fusnrfvjqc9342k@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20231115T180000
CREATED:20230814T185924Z
DESCRIPTION:<span><br>This ride starts at the Yellowwood Dam\, heads up Yel
 lowwood Road and across Lanam Ridge to 45.  From there we will drop down Gr
 eenbriar Lane and head across South Shore\, up Plum Creek back to Lanam Rid
 ge and down Dubois / Marlett / Green Valley and then back to the Dam.</span
 ><br><u></u><p>Route is suitable for Gravel\, Cross or MTB.</p><p>Bring lig
 hts!!!</p><table><tbody><tr><td><a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/409
 81658"><u><u>Dam Plum Creek</u></u></a></td></tr></tbody></table><br><br>Pa
 trick Kelly is leading this ride - Thanks PK!<br><br><span>These rides feat
 ure gravel roads\, single and double track trails\,  and just enough paveme
 nt to string the aforementioned together into fun\, woodsy adventure loops.
   Rides begin at 6PM through the Fall and Winter months as weather allows a
 nd typically last about two hours.  Lights are mandatory as we enter the Fa
 ll and Winter seasons.</span><p>Routes are suitable for mountain bike or gr
 avel bike\, with some more turned to one or the other.  Rides begin at diff
 erent locations\, primarily associated with Yellowwood State Forest\, Brown
  County State Park\, and the Hoosier National Forest in Monroe\, Lawrence\,
  and Brown Counties.  Specific routes may be dictated by weather conditions
 \, but starting locations\, route maps\, and gps file links will be posted 
 here in advance.</p><p>Expect a lot of trees and few cars</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20231115T095007Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Dam Plum Creek - Off Road Adventure Ride
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Bicycle Club
DTSTART:20240425T214500Z
DTEND:20240425T234500Z
DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:3aruf2hjn78all7lpgkkgssl3r@google.com
CREATED:20240302T193754Z
DESCRIPTION:<u></u><u></u><p><u><a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=https
 ://www.strava.com/routes/2912194098535143654&amp\;sa=D&amp\;source=calendar
 &amp\;usd=2&amp\;usg=AOvVaw3am5fNOTO1g0LTgyhH5CdK" target="_blank">31 Robin
 son\, Tunnel\, Shuffle\, Brummett</a></u><br></p><p>Ready for a high spirit
 ed NO DROP ride? BV Ride is an intermediate/ advanced ride and moderate dis
 tance that may or may not include regrouping points.  Pace is anticipated t
 o be 17+ mph. Expect occasional sprint or Strava segments\, pace line ridin
 g at high speed\, intervals\, and fewer regrouping stops.</p><p>The BV Ride
  will start at the Parking lot across from the Bryan Park Pool on Woodlawn 
 at 5:45. Mileages will increase as the season progresses. If you keep comin
 g we will make you faster!</p><p>Riders are expected to look out for each o
 ther during the rides.  Ride maps and GPS links will be posted here in adva
 nce. Riders unfamiliar with the route should bring along a copy of the map.
 </p>Non-members should sign up for a <a href="https://www.google.com/url?q=
 https://secure.getmeregistered.com/get_information.php?event_id%3D133776&am
 p\;sa=D&amp\;source=calendar&amp\;usd=2&amp\;usg=AOvVaw2j50-2uvBSoK9EgtVBL-
 h8" target="_blank">free trial membership</a>\, good for up to three rides\
 , and which includes electronically signing a liability waiver\, prior to p
 articipation.<u></u><u></u>
LAST-MODIFIED:20240302T193754Z
LOCATION:Bryan Park Pool\, 1020 S Woodlawn Ave\, Bloomington\, IN 47401\, U
 SA
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:BV ride - 31 Robinson\, Tunnel\, Shuffle\, Brummett
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
