CREATED:20230518T113658Z
DESCRIPTION:<a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/37164807">26 - Up Koont
 z back Ison</a><br><br>Please observe social distancing norms as we gather 
 and ride. <ul><li>Be SAFE. Don't blow through stop signs. Consider bike lig
 hts.<br></li><li>Be COURTEOUS: Single up in traffic<br></li><li>Be PREDICTA
 BLE: Signal your intentions to cars and fellow riders.</li></ul>The "Older\
 , Wiser\, and a Little Slower" training group emphasizes moderate rides\, a
 nd a route planned in advance that is posted on the ride calendar. This is 
 a no drop ride\, but not a beginner's ride.The OWLS group welcomes a wide r
 ange of intermediate riders\, and typically breaks off into a faster and sl
 ower group with the former averaging an overall moving speed of 16-18 mph\,
  and the slower group averaging 13-15 mph (including hills). Distances vary
  from 20 to 30 miles\, depending partly on available light. Early season ri
 des will be somewhat shorter and slower. Rides depart promptly at 5:45.<br>
 <br>Non-members should sign up for a <a href="https://secure.getmeregistere
 d.com/get_information.php?event_id=136627"><u>free trial membership</u></a>
 \, good for up to three rides\, and which includes electronically signing a
  liability waiver\, prior to participation.<br><br>Questions? Contact <a hr
 ef="mailto:gail.morell@gmail.com"><u>Gail Morell</u></a>.
LAST-MODIFIED:20230725T155307Z
LOCATION:Sherwood Oaks Christian Church\, 2700 E Rogers Rd\, Bloomington\, 
 IN 47401\, USA
SEQUENCE:2
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:OWLS Ride - 26 - Up Koontz back Ison
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Bicycle Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230114T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20230114T140000
DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:76goke0o1n3k5j8qk81fu0sg83@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20230114T100000
CREATED:20220901T172010Z
DESCRIPTION:<p>This ride will start at Ogle Lake in BCSP and exit the West 
 Gate and drop down the hill towards the Ole Nashvillle Opry.  We'll get off
  46 on Green Valley and loop around to Nashville on some familiar roads lik
 e Ike Shipley and Jackson Branch.  We'll head up Greasy Creek and Bear Wall
 ow but have an easy out if we want to skip those hills by staying on old 46
  past Hard Truth before heading back into the park and back to Ogle Lake.</
 p><p>The route is mostly pavement with a couple of gravel sections so ride 
 what you got.</p><p>Carrying on a Warren Smith tradition of getting the gro
 up together early in the year...  </p><p>Saturday is going to be a gorgeous
  day if just a little bit cold.  A group of club members are planning on ga
 thering at the shelter at Ogle Lake\, get a fire going\, share some snacks\
 , some cold drinks and good times.  Hope to see you there.</p><p><a href="h
 ttps://ridewithgps.com/routes/41766418">Gathering at Ogle Lake - 26</a></p>
 <p>These rides feature gravel roads\, single and double track trails\,  and
  just enough pavement to string the aforementioned together into fun\, wood
 sy adventure loops.  Rides begin at 10am through the Fall and Winter months
  as weather allows and typically last about three to four hours.</p><p>Rout
 es are suitable for mountain bike or gravel bike\, with some more turned to
  one or the other.  Rides begin at different locations\, primarily associat
 ed with Yellowwood State Forest\, Brown County State Park\, and the Hoosier
  National Forest in Monroe\, Lawrence\, and Brown Counties.  Specific route
 s may be dictated by weather conditions\, but starting locations\, route ma
 ps\, and gps file links will be posted here in advance.</p><p>Expect a lot 
 of trees and few cars.</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20230113T142345Z
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Gathering at Ogle Lake - Off Road Adventure
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
