BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Bicycle Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250201T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250201T143000
DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:37s3cnotqccjh1ls9qofspa90h@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20250201T100000
CREATED:20240813T191734Z
DESCRIPTION:<p><b>This will be a 22 mile out and back from Bedford to Willi
 ams on the Milwaukee Trail.  Park in the designated trail parking area in t
 he southwestern quadrant of the John A Williams / Lincoln Ave intersection 
 (a traffic circle) in Bedford.  This is the designated start point on the R
 WGPS mapping below.</b></p><p><b>Route is suitable for MTB and gravel adven
 ture bike.  Expect a little residual ice on the canyon part of the trail on
  the Bedford end.  Otherwise\, the trail is pretty clear\, but mushy\, base
 d on an inspection Friday morning.</b></p><p><a href="https://ridewithgps.c
 om/routes/49591295" target="_blank">Milwaukee Trail Out and Back 22</a></p>
 <p>These rides feature gravel roads\, single and double track trails\,  and
  just enough pavement to string the aforementioned together into fun\, wood
 sy adventure loops.  Rides begin at 10am through the Fall and Winter months
  as weather allows and typically last about four hours. </p><p>Routes are s
 uitable for mountain bike or gravel bike\, with some more turned to one or 
 the other.  Rides begin at different locations\, primarily associated with 
 Yellowwood State Forest\, Brown County State Park\, and the Hoosier Nationa
 l Forest in Monroe\, Lawrence\, and Brown Counties. Specific routes may be 
 dictated by weather conditions\, but starting locations\, route maps\, and 
 gps file links will be posted here in advance.</p><p>Expect a lot of trees 
 and few cars</p><p>Non-members should sign up for a <a href="https://secure
 .getmeregistered.com/get_information.php?event_id=136627" target="_blank">f
 ree trial membership</a>\, good for up to three rides\, and which includes 
 electronically signing a liability waiver\, prior to participation.</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20250325T180159Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Milwaukee Trail Out and Back 22 - Growlers Off Road Adventure Ride
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
