CREATED:20230814T185924Z
DESCRIPTION:<b><br>Ride will leave from the Blackwell Horse Camp on Tower R
 idge Road at 6:00PM</b><br><br><u></u><p>This route is mostly gravel with a
 bout two miles of easy double track on HNF Trail 19\, and a short section o
 f pavement on the east side from Maumee to the Boy Scout Camp.</p><p>Route 
 is suitable for CX\, MTB\, or Gravel bikes.<br><b>  </b><br>A few club memb
 ers are planning on camping at Blackwell so stick around after the ride\, t
 here will be a fire for sure and maybe some smores etc.<br><br>Possible cam
 ping opportunity or at least get a fire going.</p><p><br>BRING LIGHTS Just 
 in case!!<br><br><a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/10147577"><u><u>Bl
 ackwell Loop to HNF Trail 19</u></u></a></p><br><span>These rides feature g
 ravel roads\, single and double track trails\, and just enough pavement to 
 string the aforementioned together into fun\, woodsy adventure loops.  Ride
 s begin at 6PM through the Fall and Winter months as weather allows and typ
 ically last about two hours.  Lights are mandatory as we enter the Fall and
  Winter seasons.</span><p>Routes are suitable for mountain bike or gravel b
 ike\, with some more turned to one or the other.  Rides begin at different 
 locations\, primarily associated with Yellowwood State Forest\, Brown Count
 y State Park\, and the Hoosier National Forest in Monroe\, Lawrence\, and B
 rown Counties.  Specific routes may be dictated by weather conditions\, but
  starting locations\, route maps\, and gps file links will be posted here i
 n advance.</p><p>Expect a lot of trees and few cars</p>
