RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20230926T093000
CREATED:20230904T234620Z
DESCRIPTION:<b>We explore a little Hilly Hundred country and zoom down Mt T
 abor Hill on this new route.  We return to Bloomington via the full length 
 of Bottom Road.  I have never rode the west end of Bottom Road\, so I check
 ed it out today.  We have lots of new Bottom Road pavement and about one-ha
 lf mile of easy non-chunky gravel just west of Mt. Pleasant.</b><br><br><u>
 </u><a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/44562667">North Karst Greenway\
 , Mt. Tabor\, and All of Bottom Road 32</a><br><u></u><br>Watch the calenda
 r for weather-related updates and for future rides.<br><br>This group empha
 sizes earlier\, moderate-paced rides with routes planned in advance and pos
 ted on the ride calendar. This is a no drop ride\, but not a beginner's rid
 e. Expect an overall average moving speed 11 - 15 mph. Distances vary from 
 20 to 30 miles. Early season rides will be somewhat shorter and slower. Dur
 ing colder weather the ride departs at 1:30pm.<br><br>Non-members should si
 gn up for a <a href="https://secure.getmeregistered.com/get_information.php
 ?event_id=136627">free trial membership</a>\, good for up to three rides\, 
 and which includes electronically signing a liability waiver\, prior to par
 ticipation.<br><br><br><u></u>
LAST-MODIFIED:20231009T193710Z
LOCATION:Bryan Park Parking Lot\, S Woodlawn Ave\, Bloomington\, IN 47401\,
  USA
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Early Birds - North Karst Greenway\, Mt. Tabor\, and All of Bottom 
 Road 32
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Bicycle Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250223T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250223T160000
DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:37s3cnotqccjh1ls9qofspa90h@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20250222T100000
CREATED:20240813T191734Z
DESCRIPTION:<p><b>Hopefully\, warmer temperatures on Saturday and Sunday mo
 rning are going to melt some of the ice off of the gravel.  Meet at Blackwe
 ll Horse Camp at 1PM for a trip down to Polk Patch.  There are no trails\, 
 but a lot of gravel.</b></p><p><a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/4977
 0155" target="_blank">26 - Down Polk Patch</a></p><p>These rides feature gr
 avel roads\, single and double track trails\,  and just enough pavement to 
 string the aforementioned together into fun\, woodsy adventure loops.  Ride
 s begin at 10am through the Fall and Winter months as weather allows and ty
 pically last about four hours. </p><p>Routes are suitable for mountain bike
  or gravel bike\, with some more turned to one or the other.  Rides begin a
 t different locations\, primarily associated with Yellowwood State Forest\,
  Brown County State Park\, and the Hoosier National Forest in Monroe\, Lawr
 ence\, and Brown Counties. Specific routes may be dictated by weather condi
 tions\, but starting locations\, route maps\, and gps file links will be po
 sted here in advance.</p><p>Expect a lot of trees and few cars</p><p>Non-me
 mbers should sign up for a <a href="https://secure.getmeregistered.com/get_
 information.php?event_id=136627" target="_blank">free trial membership</a>\
 , good for up to three rides\, and which includes electronically signing a 
 liability waiver\, prior to participation.</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20250325T180159Z
SEQUENCE:2
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:26 - Down Polk Patch -Growlers Off Road Adventure Ride
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
