 nard Springs</a><br><a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/39354670"></a><
 br>Please observe social distancing norms as we gather and ride. <ul><li>Be
  SAFE. Don't blow through stop signs. Consider bike lights.<br></li><li>Be 
 COURTEOUS: Single up in traffic<br></li><li>Be PREDICTABLE: Signal your int
 entions to cars and fellow riders.</li></ul>The "Older\, Wiser\, and a Litt
 le Slower" training group emphasizes moderate rides\, and a route planned i
 n advance that is posted on the ride calendar. This is a no drop ride\, but
  not a beginner's ride.The OWLS group welcomes a wide range of intermediate
  riders\, and typically breaks off into a faster and slower group with the 
 former averaging an overall moving speed of 16-18 mph\, and the slower grou
 p averaging 13-15 mph (including hills). Distances vary from 20 to 30 miles
 \, depending partly on available light. Early season rides will be somewhat
  shorter and slower. Rides depart promptly at 5:45.<br><br>Non-members shou
 ld sign up for a <a href="https://secure.getmeregistered.com/get_informatio
 n.php?event_id=136627"><u>free trial membership</u></a>\, good for up to th
 ree rides\, and which includes electronically signing a liability waiver\, 
 prior to participation.<br><br>Questions? Contact <a href="mailto:gail.more
 ll@gmail.com"><u>Gail Morell</u></a>.
