BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Bicycle Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20221203T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20221203T140000
DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:76goke0o1n3k5j8qk81fu0sg83@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20221203T100000
CREATED:20220901T172010Z
DESCRIPTION:<html-blob><p>Hello All.</p><p>Hope you're up for a Drive n Rid
 e this week.&nbsp\; I've shamelessly plagiarized a route put together by Ma
 rc O'Leary from Elevate Endurance that starts/ends in Freedom.&nbsp\; The r
 oute is predominantly gravel&nbsp\;<span style="background-color: var(--tex
 tfield-surface)\; color: var(--on-surface)\;">with a nice mix of hills\, fl
 ats\, wooded areas\, and fields. Marc rode this back in August and passed b
 y 0 cars all day except for a couple on the short stretch on 231.</span></p
 ><p>We can make a stop at the Amish-run Freedom Country Store for a mid-rid
 e snack if we need supplies.</p><p>For those who would like to Car Pool out
  to Freedom let's meet at Bryan Park and plan to leave there at 9am for a 4
 0 minute drive to Freedom.&nbsp\; Ride will start at 10am.</p><p><a href="h
 ttps://ridewithgps.com/routes/39232085" id="ow846" __is_owner="true">*Freed
 om</a><br></p><p><span style="background-color: var(--textfield-surface)\; 
 color: var(--on-surface)\;">These rides feature gravel roads\, single and d
 ouble track trails\,&nbsp\; and just enough pavement to string the aforemen
 tioned together into fun\, woodsy adventure loops.&nbsp\; Rides begin at 10
 am through the Fall and Winter months as weather allows and typically last 
 about three to four hours.</span><br></p><p>Routes are suitable for mountai
 n bike or gravel bike\, with some more turned to one or the other.&nbsp\; R
 ides begin at different locations\, primarily associated with Yellowwood St
 ate Forest\, Brown County State Park\, and the Hoosier National Forest in M
 onroe\, Lawrence\, and Brown Counties. &nbsp\;Specific routes may be dictat
 ed by weather conditions\, but starting locations\, route maps\, and gps fi
 le links will be posted here in advance.</p><p>Expect a lot of trees and fe
 w cars.</p></html-blob>
LAST-MODIFIED:20230222T174925Z
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Freedom - Off Road Adventure
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
