DESCRIPTION:<a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/45987484">20 - OWLS Swa
 rtz Ridge and PGBR</a><br><br>I ride extension -  24 Swartz Ridge and PBGR 
 Plus:<br><br><a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/46049768">https://ride
 withgps.com/routes/46049768</a><br><br>Non-members should sign up for a <a 
 href="https://secure.getmeregistered.com/get_information.php?event_id=13662
 7"><u><u>free trial membership</u></u></a>\, good for up to three rides\, a
 nd which includes electronically signing a liability waiver\, prior to part
 icipation.<ul><li>Be SAFE. Don't blow through stop signs. Consider bike lig
 hts.<br></li><li>Be COURTEOUS: Single up in traffic<br></li><li>Be PREDICTA
 BLE: Signal your intentions to cars and fellow riders.</li></ul>The "Older\
 , Wiser\, and a Little Slower" training group emphasizes moderate rides\, a
 nd a route planned in advance that is posted on the ride calendar. This is 
 a no drop ride\, but not a beginner's ride.The OWLS group welcomes a wide r
 ange of intermediate riders\, and typically breaks off into a faster and sl
 ower group with the former averaging an overall moving speed of 16-18 mph\,
  and the slower group averaging 13-15 mph (including hills). Distances vary
  from 20 to 30 miles\, depending partly on available light. Early season ri
 des will be somewhat shorter and slower. Rides depart promptly at 5:45.<br>
 <br>Questions? Contact <a href="mailto:gail.morell@gmail.com"><u>Gail Morel
 l</u></a>.
