BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Bicycle Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230830T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20230830T203000
RRULE:FREQ=WEEKLY;WKST=SU;UNTIL=20240328T035959Z;BYDAY=WE
DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:3h1ht7sn6m0fusnrfvjqc9342k@google.com
CREATED:20230814T185924Z
DESCRIPTION:<span>These rides feature gravel roads\, single and double trac
 k trails\,  and just enough pavement to string the aforementioned together 
 into fun\, woodsy adventure loops.  Rides begin at 6PM through the Fall and
  Winter months as weather allows and typically last about two hours.  Light
 s are mandatory as we enter the Fall and Winter seasons.</span><br><p>Route
 s are suitable for mountain bike or gravel bike\, with some more turned to 
 one or the other.  Rides begin at different locations\, primarily associate
 d with Yellowwood State Forest\, Brown County State Park\, and the Hoosier 
 National Forest in Monroe\, Lawrence\, and Brown Counties.  Specific routes
  may be dictated by weather conditions\, but starting locations\, route map
 s\, and gps file links will be posted here in advance.</p><p>Expect a lot o
 f trees and few cars</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20230814T185924Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Off Road Adventure Ride
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
