 rest.  Park At old Little Nashville Opry parking lot and start at 6:00PM.</
 span><br><br><p>All gravel or paved roads<br><br>BRING LIGHTS!!!!<br><a hre
 f="http://goog_1922713921"><u><u><br></u></u></a><a href="https://ridewithg
 ps.com/routes/16544605"><u><u>Yellowwood Dubois Loop 21</u></u></a></p><p>T
 hese rides feature gravel roads\, single and double track trails\,  and jus
 t enough pavement to string the aforementioned together into fun\, woodsy a
 dventure loops.  Rides begin at 6PM through the Fall and Winter months as w
 eather allows and typically last about two hours.  Lights are mandatory as 
 we enter the Fall and Winter seasons.</p><p>Routes are suitable for mountai
 n bike or gravel bike\, with some more turned to one or the other.  Rides b
 egin at different locations\, primarily associated with Yellowwood State Fo
 rest\, Brown County State Park\, and the Hoosier National Forest in Monroe\
 , Lawrence\, and Brown Counties.  Specific routes may be dictated by weathe
 r conditions\, but starting locations\, route maps\, and gps file links wil
 l be posted here in advance.</p><p>Expect a lot of trees and few cars.  </p
 ><u></u>
