 s\, and which includes electronically signing a liability waiver\, prior to
  participation.<ul><li>Be SAFE. Don't blow through stop signs. Consider bik
 e lights.<br></li><li>Be COURTEOUS: Single up in traffic<br></li><li>Be PRE
 DICTABLE: Signal your intentions to cars and fellow riders.</li></ul>The "O
 lder\, Wiser\, and a Little Slower" training group emphasizes moderate ride
 s\, and a route planned in advance that is posted on the ride calendar. Thi
 s is a no drop ride\, but not a beginner's ride.The OWLS group welcomes a w
 ide range of intermediate riders\, and typically breaks off into a faster a
 nd slower group with the former averaging an overall moving speed of 16-18 
 mph\, and the slower group averaging 13-15 mph (including hills). Distances
  vary from 20 to 30 miles\, depending partly on available light. Early seas
 on rides will be somewhat shorter and slower. Rides depart promptly at 5:45
 .<br><br>Questions? Contact <a href="mailto:gail.morell@gmail.com" target="
