BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Bicycle Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230311T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20230311T140000
DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:76goke0o1n3k5j8qk81fu0sg83@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20230311T100000
CREATED:20220901T172010Z
DESCRIPTION:<p><span>This ride is adapted from Jeff Fetterer's Hard Truth W
 allow Hollow ride and skips the Covered Bridge climb in exchange for some u
 nexplored gravel Beyond Wallow Hollow.  Ride is about 50/50 Gravel / Paveme
 nt so ride what you got.</span><span> </span></p><p><a href="https://ridewi
 thgps.com/routes/42187310">Beyond Wallow Hollow from Hard Truth</a><span><b
 r></span></p><p><span>These rides feature gravel roads\, single and double 
 track trails\,  and just enough pavement to string the aforementioned toget
 her into fun\, woodsy adventure loops.  Rides begin at 10am through the Fal
 l and Winter months as weather allows and typically last about three to fou
 r hours.</span><br></p><p>Routes are suitable for mountain bike or gravel b
 ike\, with some more turned to one or the other.  Rides begin at different 
 locations\, primarily associated with Yellowwood State Forest\, Brown Count
 y State Park\, and the Hoosier National Forest in Monroe\, Lawrence\, and B
 rown Counties.  Specific routes may be dictated by weather conditions\, but
  starting locations\, route maps\, and gps file links will be posted here i
 n advance.</p><p>Expect a lot of trees and few cars.</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20230310T132148Z
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Beyond Wallow Hollow from Hard Truth - Off Road Adventure
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Bicycle Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20230211T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20230211T140000
DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:76goke0o1n3k5j8qk81fu0sg83@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20230211T100000
CREATED:20220901T172010Z
DESCRIPTION:<p>This ride will start at the church on Hickory Grove and head
  towards Houston via Maumee.  We will head up Berry Road and loop back to H
 ouston where we have the choice to do only one or both Baldy's.  We will ta
 ke Trail 21 on the way back to the Church which is less than a mile of easy
  going single and double track.<br></p><p><a href="https://ridewithgps.com/
 routes/41388150">Hickory Grove Church Berry Ridge Both Baldys</a><br></p><p
 >These rides feature gravel roads\, single and double track trails\,  and j
 ust enough pavement to string the aforementioned together into fun\, woodsy
  adventure loops.  Rides begin at 10am through the Fall and Winter months a
 s weather allows and typically last about three to four hours.</p><p>Routes
  are suitable for mountain bike or gravel bike\, with some more turned to o
 ne or the other.  Rides begin at different locations\, primarily associated
  with Yellowwood State Forest\, Brown County State Park\, and the Hoosier N
 ational Forest in Monroe\, Lawrence\, and Brown Counties.  Specific routes 
 may be dictated by weather conditions\, but starting locations\, route maps
 \, and gps file links will be posted here in advance.</p><p>Expect a lot of
  trees and few cars.</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20230210T132644Z
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Hickory Grove Church Berry Ridge Baldys - Off Road Adventure
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
