  CANNOT MAKE IT THIS EVENING.\n\nHello All\, Joan Ellis will be hosting thi
 s week's evening ride.  Thanks Joan!\n\nCome and join us for a great mix of
  double track through the forest and single track on Limekiln\n\nTen O'Cloc
 k and Lime Kiln 16 · Ride with GPS\n\nThese rides feature gravel roads\, si
 ngle and double track trails\,  and just enough pavement to string the afor
 ementioned together into fun\, woodsy adventure loops.  Rides begin at 6PM 
 through the Fall and Winter months as weather allows and typically last abo
 ut two hours.  Lights are mandatory as we enter the Fall and Winter seasons
 .\nRoutes are suitable for mountain bike or gravel bike\, with some more tu
 rned to one or the other.  Rides begin at different locations\, primarily a
 ssociated with Yellowwood State Forest\, Brown County State Park\, and the 
 Hoosier National Forest in Monroe\, Lawrence\, and Brown Counties.  Specifi
 c routes may be dictated by weather conditions\, but starting locations\, r
 oute maps\, and gps file links will be posted here in advance.\nExpect a lo
 t of trees and few cars\n\nNon-members should sign up for a free trial memb
 ership\, good for up to three rides\, and which includes electronically sig
 ning a liability waiver\, prior to participation.
LAST-MODIFIED:20240403T190557Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Ten O'Clock and Limekiln - Off Road Adventure Ride
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
