 w.google.com/url?q=https://bloomingtonbicycleclub.org/maps/John_Bassett_Map
 s/Cedar_Bluff_with_Limestone_Trail_50_Mile_Option.pdf2016.pdf&amp\;sa=D&amp
 \;source=calendar&amp\;usd=2&amp\;usg=AOvVaw3S-gTug5PM820J458Df11e" target=
 "_blank">Cedar Bluff with Limestone Trail 50 Mile Option</a><br><a href="ht
 tps://www.google.com/url?q=https://ridewithgps.com/routes/4264004&amp\;sa=D
 &amp\;source=calendar&amp\;usd=2&amp\;usg=AOvVaw3gmhfKQkXKFDOfo5NjoSdu" tar
 get="_blank">GPS Files Cedar Bluff</a><br><a href="https://www.google.com/u
 rl?q=https://ridewithgps.com/routes/35400226&amp\;sa=D&amp\;source=calendar
 &amp\;usd=2&amp\;usg=AOvVaw2EqYV5UGFHcTfh-L9IKviu" target="_blank">GPS File
 s 50 Mile Option</a><br><br>You have a couple of distance options on this o
 ne.  The short option is 28 pretty hilly miles down south to the Cedar Buff
  Nature Preserve.  The road may be rough in spots\, but the rolling hills o
 f Ketchum Road down the Clear Creek valley and the former Monon Railroad &q
 uot\;Limestone Route&quot\; to Harrodsburg are gorgeous in the Spring.<br><
 br>There will be an optional 50 mile version extending a little farther sou
 th from the Nature Preserve\, and winding back north through Avoca.  it is 
 usually split about 50-50 each route.<u></u><u></u><br><u></u><br><u></u><b
 r><u></u>Non-members should sign up for a <a href="https://www.google.com/u
 rl?q=https://secure.getmeregistered.com/get_information.php?event_id%3D1366
 27&amp\;sa=D&amp\;source=calendar&amp\;usd=2&amp\;usg=AOvVaw0_5cJvz8z3KUY7Y
 t6t47kW" target="_blank"><u>free trial membership</u></a>\, good for up to 
 three rides\, and which includes electronically signing a liability waiver\
 , prior to participation. <br><u></u><u></u>
LAST-MODIFIED:20230217T165140Z
LOCATION:Bryan Park Pool Parking Lot @ 39.15435\,-86.523
