BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Bicycle Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20251129T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20251129T143000
DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:1b4g2bcvfdujib2rnanil63i5t@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20251129T100000
CREATED:20251122T013244Z
DESCRIPTION:<a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/45610675">Freedom 33 · 
 Ride with GPS</a><br><br>With a potential stop at Civilian Brewing in Spenc
 er on the way back to town<br><br>Suitable for Cross\, MTB or Gravel Bikes<
 p>These rides feature gravel roads\, single and double track trails\,  and 
 just enough pavement to string the aforementioned together into fun\, woods
 y adventure loops.  Rides begin at 6PM through the Fall and Winter months a
 s weather allows and typically last about two hours. Lights are mandatory a
 s we enter the Fall and Winter seasons.</p><p>Routes are suitable for mount
 ain bike or gravel bike\, with some more turned to one or the other.  Rides
  begin at different locations\, primarily associated with Yellowwood State 
 Forest\, Brown County State Park\, and the Hoosier National Forest in Monro
 e\, Lawrence\, and Brown Counties. Specific routes may be dictated by weath
 er conditions\, but starting locations\, route maps\, and gps file links wi
 ll be posted here in advance.</p><p>Expect a lot of trees and few cars</p><
 p>Non-members should sign up for a <a href="https://secure.getmeregistered.
 com/get_information.php?event_id=136627" target="_blank"><u><u><u><u><u><u>
 <u><u>free trial membership</u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></a>\, good for 
 up to three rides\, and which includes electronically signing a liability w
 aiver\, prior to participation</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260323T124700Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Freedom 33 - Growlers Off Road Adventure Ride
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
