CREATED:20251122T013244Z
DESCRIPTION:Het Everyone\, it's gonna be too darn cold even for the most ha
 rdy of Growlers this weekend.<br><br>So for those of you who have Zwift - c
 ome and join us for a virtual Club Ride.<br><br>It's been a couple of years
  since we've done this.<br><br>Rubber-banding is switched on so we'll all s
 tay together<br><br>Suitable for Cross\, MTB or Gravel Bikes<p>These rides 
 feature gravel roads\, single and double track trails\,  and just enough pa
 vement to string the aforementioned together into fun\, woodsy adventure lo
 ops.  Rides begin at 6PM through the Fall and Winter months as weather allo
 ws and typically last about two hours. Lights are mandatory as we enter the
  Fall and Winter seasons.</p><p>Routes are suitable for mountain bike or gr
 avel bike\, with some more turned to one or the other.  Rides begin at diff
 erent locations\, primarily associated with Yellowwood State Forest\, Brown
  County State Park\, and the Hoosier National Forest in Monroe\, Lawrence\,
  and Brown Counties. Specific routes may be dictated by weather conditions\
 , but starting locations\, route maps\, and gps file links will be posted h
 ere in advance.</p><p>Expect a lot of trees and few cars</p><p>Non-members 
 should sign up for a <a href="https://secure.getmeregistered.com/get_inform
 ation.php?event_id=136627" target="_blank"><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u>free tri
 al membership</u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></a>\, good for up to three ri
 des\, and which includes electronically signing a liability waiver\, prior 
 to participation</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260323T124700Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Zwift Club Ride - Coffee Ride - Flatland Loop
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
