CREATED:20250922T201508Z
DESCRIPTION:<p>I never had the privilege of meeting Gnawbone Lefty but he's
  not forgotten that's for sure.  This is one of his favorite rides.</p><p>T
 his ride starts at the Yellowwood Dam</p><p>Route is suitable for Gravel\, 
 Cross or MTB.</p><p>GPS File:</p><p><a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes
 /49215482" target="_blank"><u>Gnawbone Lefty · Ride with GPS</u></a><br><br
 ></p><p>These rides feature gravel roads\, single and double track trails\,
   and just enough pavement to string the aforementioned together into fun\,
  woodsy adventure loops.  Rides begin at 6PM through the Fall and Winter mo
 nths as weather allows and typically last about two hours.  Lights are mand
 atory as we enter the Fall and Winter seasons.</p><p>Routes are suitable fo
 r mountain bike or gravel bike\, with some more turned to one or the other.
   Rides begin at different locations\, primarily associated with Yellowwood
  State Forest\, Brown County State Park\, and the Hoosier National Forest i
 n Monroe\, Lawrence\, and Brown Counties.  Specific routes may be dictated 
 by weather conditions\, but starting locations\, route maps\, and gps file 
 links will be posted here in advance.</p><p>Expect a lot of trees and few c
 ars</p><p><b>Bring Lights! Bring Lights! Bring Lights!</b></p><p>Non-member
 s should sign up for a <a href="https://secure.getmeregistered.com/get_info
 rmation.php?event_id=136627" target="_blank"><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u>free t
 rial membership</u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></a>\, good for up to three 
 rides\, and which includes electronically signing a liability waiver\, prio
 r to participation.</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260406T132618Z
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Growlers Off Road Adventure Ride - Gnawbone Lefty
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
