 d which includes electronically signing a liability waiver\, prior to parti
 cipation.<ul><li>Be SAFE. Don't blow through stop signs. Consider bike ligh
 ts.<br></li><li>Be COURTEOUS: Single up in traffic<br></li><li>Be PREDICTAB
 LE: Signal your intentions to cars and fellow riders.</li></ul>The "Older\,
  Wiser\, and a Little Slower" training group emphasizes moderate rides\, an
 d a route planned in advance that is posted on the ride calendar. This is a
  no drop ride\, but not a beginner's ride.The OWLS group welcomes a wide ra
 nge of intermediate riders\, and typically breaks off into a faster and slo
 wer group with the former averaging an overall moving speed of 16-18 mph\, 
 and the slower group averaging 13-15 mph (including hills). Distances vary 
 from 20 to 30 miles\, depending partly on available light. Early season rid
 es will be somewhat shorter and slower. Rides depart promptly at 5:45.<br><
 br>Questions? Contact <a href="mailto:gail.morell@gmail.com" target="_blank
 "><u>Gail Morell</u></a>.
