 p?event_id=136627" target="_blank">https://secure.getmeregistered.com/get_i
 nformation.php?event_id=136627</a>)\, good for up to three rides\, and whic
 h includes electronically signing a liability waiver\, prior to participati
 on.<br>    * Be SAFE. Don't blow through stop signs. Consider bike lights.<
 br>    * Be COURTEOUS: Single up in traffic<br>    * Be PREDICTABLE: Signal
  your intentions to cars and fellow riders.<br>The "Older\, Wiser\, and a L
 ittle Slower" training group emphasizes moderate rides\, and a route planne
 d in advance that is posted on the ride calendar. This is a no drop ride\, 
 but not a beginner's ride.The OWLS group welcomes a wide range of intermedi
 ate riders\, and typically breaks off into a faster and slower group with t
 he former averaging an overall moving speed of 16-18 mph\, and the slower g
 roup averaging 13-15 mph (including hills). Distances vary from 20 to 30 mi
 les\, depending partly on available light. Early season rides will be somew
 hat shorter and slower. Rides depart promptly at 5:45.<br><br>Questions? Co
 ntact Gail Morell (mailto:<a href="mailto:gail.morell@gmail.com" target="_b
 lank">gail.morell@gmail.com</a>).
