 etmeregistered.com/get_information.php?event_id=136627" target="_blank"><u>
 <u>free trial membership</u></u></a>\, good for up to three rides\, and whi
 ch includes electronically signing a liability waiver\, prior to participat
 ion.<ul><li>Be SAFE. Don't blow through stop signs. Consider bike lights.<b
 r></li><li>Be COURTEOUS: Single up in traffic<br></li><li>Be PREDICTABLE: S
 ignal your intentions to cars and fellow riders.</li></ul>The "Older\, Wise
 r\, and a Little Slower" training group emphasizes moderate rides\, and a r
 oute planned in advance that is posted on the ride calendar. This is a no d
 rop ride\, but not a beginner's ride.The OWLS group welcomes a wide range o
 f intermediate riders\, and typically breaks off into a faster and slower g
 roup with the former averaging an overall moving speed of 16-18 mph\, and t
 he slower group averaging 13-15 mph (including hills). Distances vary from 
 20 to 30 miles\, depending partly on available light. Early season rides wi
 ll be somewhat shorter and slower. Rides depart promptly at 5:45.<br><br>Qu
 estions? Contact <a href="mailto:gail.morell@gmail.com" target="_blank"><u>
 Gail Morell</u></a>.
