DESCRIPTION:<p><a href="https://ridewithgps.com/routes/52698517" target="_b
 lank">Ten O'Clock and LimeKiln 16 from Lower Handicapped Parking Lot · Ride
  with GPS</a><br><br></p><p><b>Ride starts from the Lower Handicapped Parki
 ng Lot at the bottom of the big hill on Crooked Creek Road - NOT the usual 
 Upper Handicapped Parking Lot</b></p><p>I have left over beer (shocker!) an
 d snacks from the TDR gravel Ride this past weekend so I've got you covered
  for refreshments!</p><p>Suitable for Gravel or MTB bikes but if you have a
 n MTB bring it!</p><p><b>Bring Lights! Bring Lights! Bring Lights!</b></p><
 p>These rides feature gravel roads\, single and double track trails\, and j
 ust enough pavement to string the aforementioned together into fun\, woodsy
  adventure loops.  Rides begin at 6PM through the Fall and Winter months as
  weather allows and typically last about two hours. Lights are mandatory as
  we enter the Fall and Winter seasons.</p><p>Routes are suitable for mounta
 in bike or gravel bike\, with some more turned to one or the other.  Rides 
 begin at different locations\, primarily associated with Yellowwood State F
 orest\, Brown County State Park\, and the Hoosier National Forest in Monroe
 \, Lawrence\, and Brown Counties. Specific routes may be dictated by weathe
 r conditions\, but starting locations\, route maps\, and gps file links wil
 l be posted here in advance.</p><p>Expect a lot of trees and few cars</p><p
 >Non-members should sign up for a <a href="https://secure.getmeregistered.c
 om/get_information.php?event_id=136627" target="_blank"><u><u><u><u><u><u><
 u>free trial membership</u></u></u></u></u></u></u></a>\, good for up to th
 ree rides\, and which includes electronically signing a liability waiver\, 
 prior to participation.</p>
