 hich includes electronically signing a liability waiver\, prior to particip
 ation.<ul><li>Be SAFE. Don't blow through stop signs. Consider bike lights.
 <br></li><li>Be COURTEOUS: Single up in traffic<br></li><li>Be PREDICTABLE:
  Signal your intentions to cars and fellow riders.</li></ul>The "Older\, Wi
 ser\, and a Little Slower" training group emphasizes moderate rides\, and a
  route planned in advance that is posted on the ride calendar. This is a no
  drop ride\, but not a beginner's ride.The OWLS group welcomes a wide range
  of intermediate riders\, and typically breaks off into a faster and slower
  group with the former averaging an overall moving speed of 16-18 mph\, and
  the slower group averaging 13-15 mph (including hills). Distances vary fro
 m 20 to 30 miles\, depending partly on available light. Early season rides 
 will be somewhat shorter and slower. Rides depart promptly at 5:45.<br><br>
 Questions? Contact <a href="mailto:gail.morell@gmail.com" target="_blank"><
 u>Gail Morell</u></a>.
