DESCRIPTION:Too darn cold today<br><br>Suitable for Cross\, MTB or Gravel B
 ikes<p>These rides feature gravel roads\, single and double track trails\, 
  and just enough pavement to string the aforementioned together into fun\, 
 woodsy adventure loops.  Rides begin at 6PM through the Fall and Winter mon
 ths as weather allows and typically last about two hours. Lights are mandat
 ory as we enter the Fall and Winter seasons.</p><p>Routes are suitable for 
 mountain bike or gravel bike\, with some more turned to one or the other.  
 Rides begin at different locations\, primarily associated with Yellowwood S
 tate Forest\, Brown County State Park\, and the Hoosier National Forest in 
 Monroe\, Lawrence\, and Brown Counties. Specific routes may be dictated by 
 weather conditions\, but starting locations\, route maps\, and gps file lin
 ks will be posted here in advance.</p><p>Expect a lot of trees and few cars
 </p><p>Non-members should sign up for a <a href="https://secure.getmeregist
 ered.com/get_information.php?event_id=136627" target="_blank"><u><u><u><u><
 u><u><u><u>free trial membership</u></u></u></u></u></u></u></u></a>\, good
  for up to three rides\, and which includes electronically signing a liabil
 ity waiver\, prior to participation</p>
