 ound-tc-steele?privacy_code=MD0O8tOvmZpxM49qnnilZjemeE2j1QYq">https://ridew
 ithgps.com/events/470536-growlers-all-around-tc-steele?privacy_code=MD0O8tO
 vmZpxM49qnnilZjemeE2j1QYq</a><br><p>These rides feature gravel roads\, sing
 le and double track trails\, and just enough pavement to string the aforeme
 ntioned together into fun\, woodsy adventure loops.  Rides begin at 6PM thr
 ough the Fall and Winter months as weather allows and typically last about 
 two hours. Lights are mandatory as we enter the Fall and Winter seasons.</p
 ><p>Routes are suitable for mountain bike or gravel bike\, with some more t
 urned to one or the other.  Rides begin at different locations\, primarily 
 associated with Yellowwood State Forest\, Brown County State Park\, and the
  Hoosier National Forest in Monroe\, Lawrence\, and Brown Counties. Specifi
 c routes may be dictated by weather conditions\, but starting locations\, r
 oute maps\, and gps file links will be posted here in advance.</p><p>Expect
  a lot of trees and few cars</p><p>Non-members should sign up for a <a href
 ="https://secure.getmeregistered.com/get_information.php?event_id=136627" t
 arget="_blank"><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u><u>free trial membership</u></u></u>
 </u></u></u></u></u></u></a>\, good for up to three rides\, and which inclu
 des electronically signing a liability waiver\, prior to participation.</p>
