BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Bloomington Bicycle Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20250419T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20250419T143000
DTSTAMP:20260905T041501Z
UID:5mu5cn4ulv9saduakntkumeqne@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/New_York:20231104T100000
CREATED:20231017T184315Z
DESCRIPTION:<p>Join in for a fun Brown County gravel ride starting and endi
 ng at Hard Truth in Nashville.  This is a loop ride borrowed from Jeff Fett
 erer and has its fair share of ups and downs.  With the exception of Covere
 d Bridge Road the clockwise loop generally goes down the steep grades and u
 p the gentler grades.  Get to near the top of Bear Wallow Hill without ever
  being on Bear Wallow Hill Road. And\, finish up with a great gravel decent
  on Wallow Hollow.<br><br>Route is entirely gravel and pavement - no trail.
  <br><br>Shorter options are possible <br><br><a href="https://ridewithgps.
 com/routes/31648043" target="_blank"><u><u><u>Jeff's Salmeron / Wallow Holl
 ow Loop from Hard Truth 29</u></u></u></a></p><p>These rides feature gravel
  roads\, single and double track trails\,  and just enough pavement to stri
 ng the aforementioned together into fun\, woodsy adventure loops.  Rides be
 gin at 10am through the Fall and Winter months as weather allows and typica
 lly last about three to four hours.</p><p>Routes are suitable for mountain 
 bike or gravel bike\, with some more turned to one or the other.  Rides beg
 in at different locations\, primarily associated with Yellowwood State Fore
 st\, Brown County State Park\, and the Hoosier National Forest in Monroe\, 
 Lawrence\, and Brown Counties.  Specific routes may be dictated by weather 
 conditions\, but starting locations\, route maps\, and gps file links will 
 be posted here in advance.</p><p>Expect a lot of trees and few cars</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20260412T160702Z
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Jeff's Salmeron Wallow Hollow Ride - Off Road Adventure RideOff Roa
 d Adventure Ride
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
